window.TraceCorpus={"repo":"milbirguram/milbirguram.github.io","revision":"80d4b9138e970e3409d32f408d379cc71f3dad3d","scope":"Ten files from Almanac: pipeline, workflow, model and selected tests. Not the whole repository; no live run data.","files":[{"path":"projects/almanac/README.md","lines":["# Almanac","","A small data pipeline meant to run every day on public Canadian open data. It answers one question, how many hours the air has been high-risk in seven western Canadian cities, and it publishes its own health next to the answer: every run, every check of its data contract, and how fresh the data is. The page is `projects/almanac/index.html`; this file keeps the full record and is not linked from the page.","","## What it’s for","","Most pictures of a data pipeline are diagrams. This one is a working pipeline that keeps a public record of itself, so a visitor can see whether to trust the number at the top: which days ran, which ones broke a promise about their data, whether anything was refused, and whether the whole thing has quietly stopped. If it stops, the page says “stale” and shows the missing days, rather than going on showing an old answer as if it were current.","","## The source and the question","","**Dataset.** Environment and Climate Change Canada (ECCC), Meteorological Service of Canada: Air Quality Health Index (AQHI) observations, from the MSC Datamart (`dd.weather.gc.ca`). Two products are used, both CSV with one column per AQHI location and one row per UTC hour:","","- the live hourly file, `…/{YYYYMMDD}/WXO-DD/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/realtime/csv/{YYYYMMDDHH}_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs.csv`, republished every hour and holding the last 168 hours;","- monthly archives, `…/today/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/monthly/csv/{YYYYMM}_MONTHLY_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs.csv`, plus a corrected `…_BACKFILLED.csv` version published about three days after each month ends. The listing goes back to at least July 2025.","","Regions are `pyr` (British Columbia and Yukon) and `pnr` (Prairies and the North). A day's two regional files are about 25–30 KB each (hourly) or 100–140 KB (monthly).","","**Why this source.** It updates hourly, has a stable machine-readable path, has history for a backfill (the monthly archives), is free to reuse under a published licence, and it answers a question people in the West care about every summer: how much wildfire smoke did we breathe. I first tried the MSC GeoMet OGC API (`api.weather.gc.ca`, collection `aqhi-observations-realtime`); on 2 November 2026 it held only about three days per location, too little for a backfill, so the Datamart CSVs are used instead.","","**Licence and attribution.** Environment and Climate Change Canada Data Services End-use Licence (version 2.1.1, August 2026). It allows copying, adapting and publishing, provided the source is acknowledged with the attribution statement and, where possible, a link to the licence. The page says “Data Source: Environment and Climate Change Canada” and links the licence in its one paragraph. It must not suggest endorsement, and it does not use ECCC’s name as branding.","","**Cities.** Seven AQHI locations: Vancouver (Metro Vancouver – NW, `JBRIK`), Victoria (Victoria / Saanich, `JBOBQ`), Kelowna (Central Okanagan, `JAFUV`), Kamloops (`JAFNW`), Prince George (`JBLVS`), Calgary (`IAKID`) and Edmonton (`IACMP`). An AQHI location is a community value; Vancouver is represented by the north-west zone of Metro Vancouver only.","","**The question, exactly.** For each city, the number of UTC hours since the record began (4 August 2026) whose AQHI reading, rounded half up to a whole number as ECCC reports it, is 7 or more. ECCC’s categories: 1–3 low risk, 4–6 moderate, 7–10 high, 10+ very high. The CSV writes 10+ as 11, so “high-risk” here includes 10+. A reading counts when it is 6.5 or above.","","## The pipeline","","`pipeline/run.py`, Python 3.11 standard library only, so it runs the same locally and in GitHub Actions:","","```","python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date 2026-11-01","python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill 2026-08-04 2026-11-01","python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --aggregate-only","```","","Options: `--kind` (scheduled, manual, backfill, revision; defaults are inferred), `--source auto|hourly|monthly`, `--now` (inject the clock), `--data-dir`, `--source-dir` (read files from disk instead of the network, for tests and replays), `--pause` (seconds between requests, default 1).","","1. **Extract.** For each region, the live hourly file if the day is within the last 6 days, otherwise the corrected monthly archive if it exists, otherwise the first monthly archive. One request at a time, one-second pauses, three tries with back-off, a descriptive User-Agent, and each file fetched once per run.","2. **Validate.** `pipeline/contract.py` applies `pipeline/contract.json`, the data contract written as data. Seven checks: schema (expected columns present), types (dates, hours 0–23, numeric or blank readings), range (1 to 11; odd values quarantined, more than 1% fails the day), uniqueness (one reading per city-hour; exact repeats warn, conflicting ones fail), completeness (all 24 hours in the file), volume (each city at least 18 of 24 hours, else a warning; under half of the 168 expected readings fails) and freshness (the live file’s newest hour at most 6 hours old, else a warning; not applicable to an archive). The day’s status is the worst check: green, amber or red.","","   When there is no source file at all, no check pretends to have looked at it. If the run wanted the live feed (the day is within 6 days) and found no hourly file in the last 8 hours (`hourly_lookback_hours`) and no monthly archive for the day, the freshness check fails with “the feed seems to have stalled” and the other six are marked “not run”. If it wanted an archive and none exists, the completeness check fails instead. Before a verification pass this case showed up as a schema failure with freshness skipped, which blamed the wrong thing; the stalled-feed and missing-archive tests now pin it down.","3. **Load.** Only when the day is not red: `data/raw/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD.{pyr,pnr}.csv` (that day’s rows exactly as received), `data/validated/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD.csv` (one row per city-hour: date, hour, location, city, value, reported value, high-risk flag) and `data/quarantine/…` for readings set aside. A red day writes nothing to raw or validated, so earlier good data for that day is kept, still counted in the answer, and marked as kept on the calendar, in its tooltip and in the readings chart (a ring under the bar).","4. **Aggregate.** `data/aggregates/summary.json` (the answer, per city and per day), `health.json` (calendar of runs, lineage counts, the SLO, known issues; the last 90 days keep a full entry with run id, times and each check’s result in words, and older days are packed into short tuples, `calendar_old`, that `model.js` unpacks) and `preview.js` (a tiny snapshot for the projects card). The page loads only these.","5. **Log.** Every run, including a failed or crashed one, appends a record to `data/runs.ndjson`: run id, batch id, kind, day, start and finish, source URLs and bytes, rows in and out, quarantined count, every check’s result and detail, bytes written, notes and the commit.","","**Idempotent.** Partitions are written whole, sorted and with fixed line endings, and the summary has no timestamps. Rerunning a day on the same source gives byte-identical raw, validated and summary files; only the run log grows (by design: a rerun is a run) and `health.json`, which reports the log.","","**Schedule.** `pipeline/almanac.yml` is a GitHub Actions workflow: daily at 07:17 UTC (the previous UTC day is complete by then), manual dispatch with an optional day or backfill range, a concurrency group, a 15-minute timeout and only `contents: write`. It runs the Python contract tests first, processes yesterday, and on the 4th of each month reloads the previous month from ECCC’s corrected file as a “revision”. It commits only when something under `projects/almanac/data` changed; the run log changes on every run, so in practice every run is committed, which is what lets the page show it. If the contract failed, the data is still committed and then the job is marked failed. The owner’s token lacks the workflow scope, so the file is not in `.github/workflows`; the install line is at its top.","","**Budgets.** 90 days take about 2.2 MB on disk (raw 0.76 MB, validated 0.55 MB, run log 0.14 MB, aggregates 73 KB), so about 9 MB a year, under the 20 MB budget. The aggregates are 73 KB against a 200 KB budget. They used to grow by about 300–650 bytes a day and would have passed the budget after about 14 months; now days older than 90 are packed (about 45 bytes each), the daily maximum is stored as the reported whole number, and `tests/test_budget.py` builds two years of runs and asserts the total stays under 200 KB (it is about 150 KB). At roughly 45 KB a year, the summary should be split by year before the record reaches three years. The launch backfill downloaded 0.79 MB.","","## The page","","Back link, title, one paragraph; everything else is in the stage. The answer: a city chooser that doubles as a ranking, one big number, a sentence giving its denominator (hours that had a reading), a warning when a city’s coverage is under 90%, and a bar chart of high-risk hours per day that adds up to the big number, with a mark under days where the city had fewer than 18 readings. The health panel: a freshness clock and its rule; a tally of runs; a calendar with one square per day (status is carried by shape, like the moon-phase marks in a printed almanac: a full disc passed, a half disc warned, a struck ring was refused, a point means no run; a boxed mark ran on schedule, an unboxed one was backfilled; 22 px squares on desktop and 24 px on a phone, where the calendar scrolls sideways); the selected day’s contract results in words, each with a “what this promise means” line; a chart of readings loaded per day against the 168 expected and the 84 refusal line; a lineage strip from source to raw to contract to validated to aggregates, with live counts; and the known-issues log from `pipeline/known_issues.json`.","","**Look.** The stage is set as a two-colour almanac sheet: cream stock with a light paper grain, black ink, and one spot colour, wildfire-smoke orange (#d9662a), used only for high-risk hours (the bars, the rule under the headline number, the screen behind “high-risk”). Everything else, including pass, warning and refusal, is told by shape and words in black, so the only colour on the page means smoke. Type is Libre Caslon Text and Libre Caslon Display (SIL Open Font License, self-hosted in `fonts/` with `OFL.txt`, about 100 KB). The card preview prints the same marks into the calendar day by day while the orange bars rise.","","**Freshness, honestly.** Fresh means the newest hour is at most 36 hours old and the last run finished at most 26 hours ago (`contract.json`, `slo`). The page computes this from the visitor’s clock, not the pipeline’s. It also adds “no run” squares for every day after the last logged one up to yesterday, so a stopped pipeline shows its gap instead of hiding it. `?now=2026-11-05T12:00:00Z` sets the page’s clock for testing.","","**Preview.** On the projects card the run calendar fills in day by day while the high-risk bars draw and the total counts up, from `preview.js` (the last 91 days only, so the squares stay legible); no requests, and a full still frame when paused. Its caption counts the scheduled runs among those shown, so it will stop saying “all backfilled” once the schedule runs.","","**What the page claims about itself.** The calendar, contract results and counts come from the pipeline’s log; the freshness verdict and the “no run” squares are worked out by the page from the visitor’s clock; the known issues are written by hand. The page says so in those words. The tally’s sentence about which check causes most warnings is counted from the calendar, and only shown when one check causes most of them.","","**Not yet running on a schedule.** At launch all 90 days came from one backfill (batch `backfill-20261102T033929Z`); the workflow has not run in GitHub Actions yet, so the page will turn stale about a day after launch. That is the honest state, and it is the first known issue. The owner should move `almanac.yml` into `.github/workflows`, start it once by hand from the Actions tab, and only then describe the project as running every day.","","## How I know","","**What was checked, and how.**","","- `tests/test_contract.py`: each of the seven checks passes a clean crafted day and catches a crafted violation (renamed column, text in a reading, an hour of 25, out-of-range values below and above the 1% line, 10+ as 11, conflicting and exact duplicates, missing hours, a missing day, a quiet city, a mostly empty day, a stale feed, an unknown feed age, an archive source).","- `tests/test_pipeline.py`: end to end on crafted files with `--source-dir`: rerunning a day and a backfill gives byte-identical partitions and summary; backfill runs are labelled and share a batch id; a red day is logged, exits 2 and leaves the earlier validated data untouched; a missing archive is a red completeness failure, not a crash; a stalled live feed (no hourly file) fails freshness, not schema, with the other checks not run; a live file 7 hours old warns; a refused rerun records that the earlier load is kept; a day that is not over is refused.","- `tests/test_budget.py`: two years of runs, cycled from the real log and partitions, keep the aggregates under 200 KB, and packed old days unpack to the same entries as full ones.","- `tests/recompute-headline.js`: an independent Node script recounts each city’s high-risk hours from the stored validated CSVs (and, separately, from the raw slices as ECCC wrote them), and checks both against `summary.json` and against the sum of the chart’s bars. All seven cities match (Kamloops 137, Kelowna 61, Calgary 17, Edmonton 11, Vancouver 9, Prince George 1, Victoria 0, from 14,240 stored readings).","- `tests/freshness.test.js`: with an injected clock, fresh just inside the 36-hour limit, stale one minute past it, stale when only the run is too old, both reasons when both are, stale with no data; and the page adds “no run” days after the last logged one.","- `tests/model.test.js`: calendar layout, unpacking of old days, each day’s colour is the worst of its checks, the kept-earlier wording, the counted cause of warnings, the headline equals its bars, the aggregates are under budget.","- Run all with `node projects/almanac/tests/run-all.js`.","- Real-data idempotency: I copied the data folder, reran 10 September 2026 against the live server, and diffed: only `runs.ndjson` and `health.json` changed.","- I compared ECCC’s first and corrected September files for the BC and Yukon region: the corrected one filled 636 blank city-hours and changed 257 values. That is why the workflow reloads each month on the 4th, and why October is listed as a known issue.","- In a browser: desktop and 375 px widths, the `?preview` card on projects.html, keyboard use of the calendar and charts, the stale state with an injected clock, and no console errors.","","**What is simplified.**","","- The record starts on 4 August 2026, because the launch backfill was capped at about 90 days. The counts are hours since then, not hours this year; July 2026 alone had 119 high-risk hours in Kamloops by ECCC’s corrected file.","- One AQHI location stands for each city. Metro Vancouver’s other zones, for instance, can differ.","- Readings are ECCC’s real-time values, which it says are not quality-controlled. Missing hours are not filled in, so a city with gaps (Kelowna most of all) has a count that is a floor.","- Days are UTC days, not local days.","- The volume threshold (18 of 24 hours per city) is a judgement: fewer readings can hide high-risk hours. With it, 36 of the 90 backfilled days are amber, 31 of them because Central Okanagan (Kelowna) or Kamloops went quiet. I did not loosen it to make the calendar greener.","- The AQHI is a relative-risk index built from ozone, PM2.5 and NO2; this project counts its hours and makes no health claim beyond ECCC’s category names.","","**What would change the conclusion.** ECCC’s corrected monthly files can fill gaps and revise values, so October’s counts may move after the revision run. Extending the backfill to 1 January (one command; the archives are there) would turn “since 4 August” into “this year” and add July’s smoke. A change to the AQHI formula or to how the CSV encodes 10+ would be caught by the range check before it changed a count.","","**Local note.** On the machine that ran the backfill, the installed Python had no certificate store, so `run.py` was run with `SSL_CERT_FILE` pointing at Git for Windows’ CA bundle. GitHub’s Ubuntu runners do not need this.","","## Sources","","- Environment and Climate Change Canada, Meteorological Service of Canada. “Data and Products of the Air Quality Health Index (AQHI) observation and forecast.” MSC Open Data documentation. https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/msc-data/aqhi/readme_aqhi_en/","- Environment and Climate Change Canada. “Environment and Climate Change Canada Data Services End-use Licence,” version 2.1.1, August 2026. https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/licence/readme_en/","- MSC Datamart, AQHI observations, `https://dd.weather.gc.ca/today/air_quality/aqhi/` (hourly and monthly CSV), accessed 2 November 2026.","- MSC GeoMet OGC API, collection `aqhi-observations-realtime`, `https://api.weather.gc.ca/collections/aqhi-observations-realtime`, examined 2 November 2026 and not used (about three days of history)."],"sha256":"d9d8e74586dbfc96664fe9574543b36a3119a88021a1f07afa3dd5ba7bd16277"},{"path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","lines":["\"\"\"Almanac pipeline: AQHI observations for seven western Canadian cities.","","    python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date 2026-11-01","    python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill 2026-08-04 2026-11-01","","extract -> validate (contract.json) -> load (data/raw, data/validated) -> aggregate","(data/aggregates) -> append a run record (data/runs.ndjson). Standard library only.","","Rerunning a day on the same source gives byte-identical partitions and summary.","\"\"\"","import argparse","import csv","import io","import json","import os","import sys","import time","import urllib.error","import urllib.request","from datetime import date as Date, datetime, timedelta, timezone","","HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))","sys.path.insert(0, HERE)  # python -I does not add the script's folder to the path","import contract as C  # noqa: E402","","VERSION = \"almanac-pipeline 1.0\"","USER_AGENT = \"almanac-pipeline/1.0 (+https://milbirguram.github.io/projects/almanac/)\"","DEFAULT_DATA = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"data\"))","VALIDATED_COLS = [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\", \"city\", \"aqhi\", \"aqhi_reported\", \"high_risk\"]","QUARANTINE_COLS = [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\", \"city\", \"value\", \"reason\"]","","","# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- time","","def utcnow():","    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)","","","def iso(dt):","    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")","","","def parse_iso(s):","    s = s.strip().replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\")","    dt = datetime.fromisoformat(s)","    if dt.tzinfo is None:","        dt = dt.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)","    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc)","","","def days(start, end):","    d = start","    while d <= end:","        yield d","        d += timedelta(days=1)","","","# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- extract","","class Fetcher:","    \"\"\"One request at a time, a pause between requests, a few polite retries.","    With source_dir set, files are read from disk by their URL's file name (tests, replays).\"\"\"","","    def __init__(self, source_dir=None, pause=1.0):","        self.source_dir = source_dir","        self.pause = pause","        self.cache = {}","        self.last = 0.0","        self.downloaded = 0","        self.errors = {}","","    def get(self, url):","        \"\"\"Return (bytes, fresh) or (None, False) when the file does not exist.\"\"\"","        if url in self.cache:","            return self.cache[url], False","        if url in self.errors:  # do not hammer a server that just failed us","            raise self.errors[url]","        if self.source_dir:","            path = os.path.join(self.source_dir, url.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1])","            data = None","            if os.path.exists(path):","                with open(path, \"rb\") as f:","                    data = f.read()","            self.cache[url] = data","            return data, data is not None","        data = None","        for attempt in range(3):","            wait = self.pause - (time.time() - self.last)","            if wait > 0:","                time.sleep(wait)","            self.last = time.time()","            try:","                req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT})","                with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as resp:","                    data = resp.read()","                break","            except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:","                if e.code == 404:","                    break","                if attempt == 2:","                    self.errors[url] = e","                    raise","            except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError) as e:","                if attempt == 2:","                    self.errors[url] = e","                    raise","            time.sleep(2 ** attempt * 2)","        self.cache[url] = data","        if data is not None:","            self.downloaded += len(data)","        return data, data is not None","","","def fill(template, **kw):","    out = template","    for k, v in kw.items():","        out = out.replace(\"{\" + k + \"}\", v)","    return out","","","def hourly_snapshot(fetcher, contract, region, now, resolved):","    \"\"\"The newest hourly file (it holds the last 168 hours). Tries back hourly_lookback_hours.\"\"\"","    if region in resolved:  # already fetched in this run: reuse it, and do not count it twice","        got = resolved[region]","        return None if got is None else (got[0], got[1], got[2], False)","    top = now.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)","    for back in range(0, lookback_hours(contract) + 1):","        t = top - timedelta(hours=back)","        url = fill(contract[\"source\"][\"hourly_url\"], yyyymmdd=t.strftime(\"%Y%m%d\"),","                   yyyymmddhh=t.strftime(\"%Y%m%d%H\"), region=region, REGION=region.upper())","        data, fresh = fetcher.get(url)","        if data is not None:","            resolved[region] = (data, url, \"hourly snapshot\", fresh)","            return resolved[region]","    resolved[region] = None","    return None","","","def lookback_hours(contract):","    return int(contract[\"source\"].get(\"hourly_lookback_hours\", 8))","","","def expects_live(contract, day, now, mode):","    \"\"\"Whether this run should read the live hourly feed for `day`.\"\"\"","    recent = (now.date() - day).days <= contract[\"source\"][\"hourly_window_days\"]","    return mode == \"hourly\" or (mode == \"auto\" and recent)","","","def monthly_archive(fetcher, contract, region, day, want_revised=True):","    for suffix, label in ((\"_BACKFILLED\", \"revised monthly archive\"), (\"\", \"monthly archive\")):","        if suffix and not want_revised:","            continue","        url = fill(contract[\"source\"][\"monthly_url\"], yyyymm=day.strftime(\"%Y%m\"),","                   region=region, REGION=region.upper(), suffix=suffix)","        data, fresh = fetcher.get(url)","        if data is not None:","            return data, url, label, fresh","    return None","","","def choose_source(fetcher, contract, region, day, now, mode, resolved):","    \"\"\"auto: the live hourly file if it still covers the day, otherwise the monthly archive.\"\"\"","    if expects_live(contract, day, now, mode):","        got = hourly_snapshot(fetcher, contract, region, now, resolved)","        if got is not None or mode == \"hourly\":","            return got","    return monthly_archive(fetcher, contract, region, day)","","","def parse_source(data, date_str, date_col):","    text = data.decode(\"utf-8-sig\").replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").replace(\"\\r\", \"\\n\")","    lines = [l for l in text.split(\"\\n\") if l.strip() != \"\"]","    if not lines:","        return {\"header\": [], \"rows\": [], \"newest\": None, \"raw_lines\": []}","    header = next(csv.reader([lines[0]]))","    header = [h.strip() for h in header]","    di = header.index(date_col) if date_col in header else 0","    hi = header.index(\"Hour (UTC)\") if \"Hour (UTC)\" in header else 1","    rows, raw_lines, newest = [], [lines[0]], None","    for line in lines[1:]:","        row = next(csv.reader([line]))","        d = row[di].strip() if di < len(row) else \"\"","        try:","            stamp = \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (d, int(row[hi]))","            datetime.strptime(stamp, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")","            if newest is None or stamp > newest:","                newest = stamp","        except (ValueError, IndexError):","            pass","        if d == date_str:","            rows.append(row)","            raw_lines.append(line)","    return {\"header\": header, \"rows\": rows, \"newest\": newest, \"raw_lines\": raw_lines}","","","# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- load","","def write_text(path, text):","    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)","    tmp = path + \".tmp\"","    with open(tmp, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:","        f.write(text)","    os.replace(tmp, path)","    return len(text.encode(\"utf-8\"))","","","def csv_text(cols, rows):","    buf = io.StringIO()","    w = csv.writer(buf, lineterminator=\"\\n\")","    w.writerow(cols)","    for r in rows:","        w.writerow([r[c] for c in cols])","    return buf.getvalue()","","","def partition(data_dir, layer, day, suffix):","    return os.path.join(data_dir, layer, day.strftime(\"%Y-%m\"), day.isoformat() + suffix)","","","def process_day(day, ctx):","    contract, fetcher, data_dir = ctx[\"contract\"], ctx[\"fetcher\"], ctx[\"data_dir\"]","    now = ctx[\"now\"]()","    started = now","    ds = day.isoformat()","    record = {","        \"run_id\": \"%s-%s\" % (started.strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\"), ds),","        \"batch_id\": ctx[\"batch_id\"], \"kind\": ctx[\"kind\"], \"date\": ds,","        \"started_at\": iso(started), \"finished_at\": None, \"status\": \"fail\", \"loaded\": False,","        \"source\": [], \"rows_in\": 0, \"rows_out\": 0, \"quarantined\": 0, \"bytes_written\": 0,","        \"checks\": [], \"notes\": [], \"pipeline\": VERSION, \"commit\": (os.environ.get(\"GITHUB_SHA\") or \"\")[:7] or None,","    }","    try:","        regions = sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in contract[\"locations\"]})","        sources, raws = {}, {}","        for region in regions:","            got = choose_source(fetcher, contract, region, day, now, ctx[\"source_mode\"], ctx[\"resolved\"])","            live_wanted = expects_live(contract, day, now, ctx[\"source_mode\"])","            if got is None:","                if live_wanted:","                    record[\"notes\"].append(\"No live %s file in the last %d hours, and no monthly archive covers this day yet: \"","                                           \"the feed seems to have stalled.\" % (region.upper(), lookback_hours(contract)))","                else:","                    record[\"notes\"].append(\"No %s file covers this day; the source may not offer it any more.\" % region.upper())","                sources[region] = {\"absent\": \"live\" if live_wanted else \"archive\", \"lookback_hours\": lookback_hours(contract)}","                continue","            if live_wanted and got[2] != \"hourly snapshot\":","                record[\"notes\"].append(\"No live %s file in the last %d hours, so the day was read from the %s.\"","                                       % (region.upper(), lookback_hours(contract), got[2]))","            data, url, label, fresh = got","            parsed = parse_source(data, ds, contract[\"columns\"][\"date\"])","            sources[region] = parsed","            raws[region] = parsed[\"raw_lines\"]","            record[\"source\"].append({\"region\": region, \"url\": url, \"type\": label, \"bytes\": len(data), \"downloaded\": fresh})","        live = bool(record[\"source\"]) and all(s[\"type\"] == \"hourly snapshot\" for s in record[\"source\"])","        locs = contract[\"locations\"]","        for region, s in sources.items():","            idx = {n: i for i, n in enumerate(s.get(\"header\", []))}","            for row in s.get(\"rows\", []):","                for l in locs:","                    if l[\"region\"] == region and l[\"id\"] in idx and idx[l[\"id\"]] < len(row) and row[idx[l[\"id\"]]].strip():","                        record[\"rows_in\"] += 1","        checks, rows, quarantined = C.validate(contract, ds, sources, now=now, live=live)","        record[\"checks\"] = checks","        record[\"status\"] = C.worst(c[\"status\"] for c in checks)","        record[\"quarantined\"] = len(quarantined)","        qpath = partition(data_dir, \"quarantine\", day, \".csv\")","        if record[\"status\"] != \"fail\":","            written = 0","            for region in regions:","                if region in raws:","                    written += write_text(partition(data_dir, \"raw\", day, \".\" + region + \".csv\"), \"\\n\".join(raws[region]) + \"\\n\")","            written += write_text(partition(data_dir, \"validated\", day, \".csv\"), csv_text(VALIDATED_COLS, rows))","            if quarantined:","                written += write_text(qpath, csv_text(QUARANTINE_COLS, quarantined))","            elif os.path.exists(qpath):","                os.remove(qpath)","            record[\"rows_out\"] = len(rows)","            record[\"bytes_written\"] = written","            record[\"loaded\"] = True","        else:","            kept = os.path.exists(partition(data_dir, \"validated\", day, \".csv\"))","            record[\"kept_earlier\"] = kept","            record[\"notes\"].append(\"The contract failed, so nothing was loaded for this day.\"","                                   + (\" The day's earlier load is kept and still counted.\" if kept else \"\"))","            if quarantined:","                record[\"bytes_written\"] = write_text(qpath, csv_text(QUARANTINE_COLS, quarantined))","    except Exception as e:  # a crash is still a run, and the log should say so","        record[\"status\"] = \"fail\"","        record[\"notes\"].append(\"The run stopped with an error: %s: %s\" % (type(e).__name__, e))","        names = {c[\"name\"] for c in record[\"checks\"]}","        for c in contract[\"checks\"]:","            if c[\"name\"] not in names:","                record[\"checks\"].append({\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"status\": \"skip\", \"detail\": \"Not run, because the run stopped early.\"})","    record[\"finished_at\"] = iso(ctx[\"now\"]())","    append_run(data_dir, record)","    return record","","","def append_run(data_dir, record):","    path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"runs.ndjson\")","    os.makedirs(data_dir, exist_ok=True)","    with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:","        f.write(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")","","","def read_runs(data_dir):","    path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"runs.ndjson\")","    if not os.path.exists(path):","        return []","    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","        return [json.loads(l) for l in f if l.strip()]","","","# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- aggregate","","def dumps(obj):","    return json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))","","","def walk(root, suffix):","    out = []","    if not os.path.isdir(root):","        return out","    for dirpath, _, files in os.walk(root):","        for name in files:","            if name.endswith(suffix):","                out.append(os.path.join(dirpath, name))","    return sorted(out)","","","PREVIEW_DAYS = 91","OLD_FIELDS = [\"status\", \"kind\", \"kinds\", \"runs\", \"rows_in\", \"rows_out\", \"q\", \"loaded\", \"checks\", \"src\", \"kept\"]","STATUS_CODE = {\"pass\": \"p\", \"warn\": \"w\", \"fail\": \"f\", \"none\": \"n\"}","KIND_CODE = {\"scheduled\": \"s\", \"manual\": \"m\", \"backfill\": \"b\", \"revision\": \"r\"}","SRC_CODE = {\"hourly snapshot\": \"H\", \"monthly archive\": \"M\", \"revised monthly archive\": \"R\"}","","","def _inverse(d):","    return {v: k for k, v in d.items()}","","","def pack_day(item):","    \"\"\"A calendar entry as a short tuple in OLD_FIELDS order (a day with no run is [\"n\"]).\"\"\"","    if item[\"status\"] == \"none\":","        return [\"n\"]","    return [STATUS_CODE[item[\"status\"]], KIND_CODE[item[\"kind\"]], \"\".join(KIND_CODE[k] for k in item[\"kinds\"]),","            item[\"runs\"], item[\"rows_in\"], item[\"rows_out\"], item[\"q\"], 1 if item[\"loaded\"] else 0, item[\"checks\"],","            \"\".join(SRC_CODE.get(x, \"?\") for x in item[\"src\"].split(\",\") if x), item.get(\"kept\", 0)]","","","def calendar_items(health):","    \"\"\"Every calendar day as a dict, old packed days first (mirrors expandCalendar in model.js).\"\"\"","    out = []","    old = health.get(\"calendar_old\") or {\"days\": []}","    if old[\"days\"]:","        first = Date.fromisoformat(old[\"first\"])","        st, kd, sr = _inverse(STATUS_CODE), _inverse(KIND_CODE), _inverse(SRC_CODE)","        for i, t in enumerate(old[\"days\"]):","            ds = (first + timedelta(days=i)).isoformat()","            if t[0] == \"n\":","                out.append({\"date\": ds, \"status\": \"none\"})","                continue","            item = dict(zip(old[\"fields\"], t))","            item.update({\"date\": ds, \"status\": st[t[0]], \"kind\": kd[item[\"kind\"]], \"kinds\": [kd[c] for c in item[\"kinds\"]],","                         \"loaded\": bool(item[\"loaded\"]), \"src\": \",\".join(sorted(sr.get(c, c) for c in item[\"src\"]))})","            if not item[\"kept\"]:","                del item[\"kept\"]","            out.append(item)","    return out + list(health.get(\"calendar\", []))","","","def build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known_issues):","    locs = contract[\"locations\"]","    thr = contract[\"high_risk_threshold\"]","    vfiles = walk(os.path.join(data_dir, \"validated\"), \".csv\")","    per = {}  # date -> lid -> [hi, max, n, maxlabel, maxhour]","    latest_hour = None","    vrows = 0","    for path in vfiles:","        ds = os.path.basename(path)[:10]","        day = per.setdefault(ds, {})","        with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:","            for r in csv.DictReader(f):","                vrows += 1","                s = day.setdefault(r[\"location_id\"], [0, 0.0, 0, \"\", -1])","                x = float(r[\"aqhi\"])","                s[0] += 1 if C.reported(x) >= thr else 0","                if x > s[1]:","                    s[1], s[3], s[4] = x, r[\"aqhi_reported\"], int(r[\"hour_utc\"])","                s[2] += 1","                stamp = \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (ds, int(r[\"hour_utc\"]))","                if latest_hour is None or stamp > latest_hour:","                    latest_hour = stamp","    runs = read_runs(data_dir)","    run_dates = sorted({r[\"date\"] for r in runs})","    all_dates = sorted(set(per) | set(run_dates))","    if not all_dates:","        return None","    start = Date.fromisoformat(min(per) if per else all_dates[0])","    end = Date.fromisoformat(all_dates[-1])","    dates = [d.isoformat() for d in days(start, end)]","","    # ---- summary: the answer to the question","    cities, series = [], {}","    for l in locs:","        hi, mx, n = [], [], []","        tot_hi = tot_n = loaded_days = 0","        peak, peak_label, peak_at, worst_day, worst_hi = 0.0, \"\", None, None, 0","        for ds in dates:","            s = per.get(ds, {}).get(l[\"id\"]) if ds in per else None","            if ds not in per:","                hi.append(None); mx.append(None); n.append(None)","                continue","            loaded_days += 1","            if s is None:","                hi.append(0); mx.append(None); n.append(0)","                continue","            hi.append(s[0]); mx.append(C.reported(s[1])); n.append(s[2])  # max as reported: 11 = 10+","            tot_hi += s[0]; tot_n += s[2]","            if s[1] > peak:","                peak, peak_label, peak_at = s[1], s[3], \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (ds, s[4])","            if s[0] > worst_hi:","                worst_hi, worst_day = s[0], ds","        series[l[\"id\"]] = {\"hi\": hi, \"max\": mx, \"n\": n}","        cities.append({\"id\": l[\"id\"], \"city\": l[\"city\"], \"zone\": l[\"zone\"], \"high_hours\": tot_hi,","                       \"hours_with_reading\": tot_n, \"hours_possible\": loaded_days * 24,","                       \"peak\": round(peak, 2), \"peak_label\": peak_label, \"peak_at\": peak_at,","                       \"worst_day\": worst_day, \"worst_day_hours\": worst_hi})","    loaded_dates = sorted(per)","    summary = {","        \"question\": \"How many hours has the air been high-risk (AQHI 7 or more) in western Canadian cities?\",","        \"threshold\": thr, \"first_date\": dates[0], \"last_date\": dates[-1],","        \"first_loaded\": loaded_dates[0] if loaded_dates else None,","        \"last_loaded\": loaded_dates[-1] if loaded_dates else None,","        \"days_loaded\": len(loaded_dates), \"latest_hour\": latest_hour,","        \"dates\": dates, \"cities\": cities, \"series\": series,","        \"attribution\": contract[\"source\"][\"attribution\"],","    }","","    # ---- health: the pipeline's account of itself","    # The most recent `detail_days` keep a full entry each (ids, times, every check's words).","    # Older days are packed into short tuples (see OLD_FIELDS) so the file stays inside its","    # budget however long the pipeline runs; model.js and calendar_items() unpack them.","    by_date = {}","    for r in runs:","        e = by_date.setdefault(r[\"date\"], {\"runs\": 0, \"kinds\": []})","        e[\"runs\"] += 1","        if r[\"kind\"] not in e[\"kinds\"]:","            e[\"kinds\"].append(r[\"kind\"])","        e[\"last\"] = r","    detail_from = (end - timedelta(days=contract[\"budgets\"][\"detail_days\"] - 1)).isoformat()","    names = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]","    status_char = {\"pass\": \"p\", \"warn\": \"w\", \"fail\": \"f\", \"skip\": \"s\"}","    cal, old = [], []","    for ds in dates:","        e = by_date.get(ds)","        if not e:","            item = {\"date\": ds, \"status\": \"none\"}","        else:","            r = e[\"last\"]","            res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in r[\"checks\"]}","            item = {","                \"date\": ds, \"status\": r[\"status\"], \"kind\": r[\"kind\"], \"runs\": e[\"runs\"], \"kinds\": e[\"kinds\"],","                \"rows_in\": r[\"rows_in\"], \"rows_out\": r[\"rows_out\"], \"q\": r[\"quarantined\"],","                \"loaded\": r[\"loaded\"], \"src\": \",\".join(sorted({s[\"type\"] for s in r[\"source\"]})),","                \"checks\": \"\".join(status_char[res[n][\"status\"]] if n in res else \"s\" for n in names),","            }","            if not r[\"loaded\"] and ds in per:","                # refused, but an earlier load of this day is still in data/validated and counted","                item[\"kept\"] = sum(v[2] for v in per[ds].values())","        if ds < detail_from:","            old.append(pack_day(item))","            continue","        if e:","            r = e[\"last\"]","            res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in r[\"checks\"]}","            item.update({\"run_id\": r[\"run_id\"], \"started\": r[\"started_at\"], \"finished\": r[\"finished_at\"],","                         \"bytes\": r[\"bytes_written\"],","                         \"details\": [res[n][\"detail\"] if n in res else \"\" for n in names]})","            if r[\"notes\"]:","                item[\"notes\"] = r[\"notes\"]","        cal.append(item)","    latest = runs[-1] if runs else None","    totals = {\"runs\": len(runs), \"kinds\": {}, \"statuses\": {}}","    for r in runs:","        totals[\"kinds\"][r[\"kind\"]] = totals[\"kinds\"].get(r[\"kind\"], 0) + 1","        totals[\"statuses\"][r[\"status\"]] = totals[\"statuses\"].get(r[\"status\"], 0) + 1","    raw_files = walk(os.path.join(data_dir, \"raw\"), \".csv\")","    q_files = walk(os.path.join(data_dir, \"quarantine\"), \".csv\")","    q_rows = 0","    for p in q_files:","        with open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","            q_rows += max(0, sum(1 for _ in f) - 1)","    src_bytes = sum(s[\"bytes\"] for r in runs for s in r[\"source\"] if s.get(\"downloaded\"))","    health = {","        \"contract\": {\"name\": contract[\"name\"], \"version\": contract[\"version\"],","                     \"checks\": [{\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"title\": c[\"title\"], \"plain\": c[\"plain\"]} for c in contract[\"checks\"]],","                     \"slo\": contract[\"slo\"]},","        \"source\": {k: contract[\"source\"][k] for k in (\"publisher\", \"attribution\", \"licence\", \"licence_url\", \"docs_url\")},","        \"latest_hour\": latest_hour,","        \"latest_run\": None if latest is None else {k: latest[k] for k in (","            \"run_id\", \"kind\", \"date\", \"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"status\", \"rows_in\", \"rows_out\", \"quarantined\", \"notes\")},","        \"calendar_old\": {\"first\": dates[0], \"fields\": OLD_FIELDS, \"days\": old},","        \"calendar\": cal, \"check_names\": names, \"totals\": totals,","        \"lineage\": {","            \"source\": {\"downloaded_bytes\": src_bytes, \"files\": len({s[\"url\"] for r in runs for s in r[\"source\"]})},","            \"raw\": {\"files\": len(raw_files), \"bytes\": sum(os.path.getsize(p) for p in raw_files)},","            \"validated\": {\"files\": len(vfiles), \"rows\": vrows, \"bytes\": sum(os.path.getsize(p) for p in vfiles)},","            \"quarantine\": {\"files\": len(q_files), \"rows\": q_rows},","            \"runs_log\": {\"records\": len(runs), \"bytes\": os.path.getsize(os.path.join(data_dir, \"runs.ndjson\")) if runs else 0},","            \"aggregates\": {\"bytes\": 0, \"budget\": contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]},","        },","        \"known_issues\": known_issues,","    }","","    # ---- preview: a tiny precomputed snapshot for the projects card (no fetch in preview)","    # Only the last PREVIEW_DAYS: the card has room for about thirteen weeks of squares.","    full_cal = calendar_items({\"calendar_old\": {\"first\": dates[0], \"fields\": OLD_FIELDS, \"days\": old}, \"calendar\": cal})","    k0 = max(0, len(dates) - PREVIEW_DAYS)","    win = {l[\"id\"]: sum(h or 0 for h in series[l[\"id\"]][\"hi\"][k0:]) for l in locs}","    top = max(locs, key=lambda l: (win[l[\"id\"]], -locs.index(l)))","    letter = {\"pass\": \"g\", \"warn\": \"a\", \"fail\": \"r\", \"none\": \"n\"}","    preview = {","        \"city\": top[\"city\"], \"total\": win[top[\"id\"]], \"first\": dates[k0], \"last\": dates[-1],","        \"cal\": \"\".join(letter.get(c[\"status\"], \"n\") for c in full_cal[k0:]),","        \"backfill\": \"\".join(\"s\" if \"scheduled\" in c.get(\"kinds\", []) else \"b\" for c in full_cal[k0:]),","        \"hi\": [h if h is not None else 0 for h in series[top[\"id\"]][\"hi\"][k0:]],","    }","    preview_text = \"window.ALMANAC_PREVIEW=\" + dumps(preview) + \";\\n\"","    summary_text = dumps(summary) + \"\\n\"","    agg = os.path.join(data_dir, \"aggregates\")","    for _ in range(3):  # health includes its own size; settle it","        health_text = dumps(health) + \"\\n\"","        size = len(summary_text.encode()) + len(health_text.encode()) + len(preview_text.encode())","        health[\"lineage\"][\"aggregates\"][\"bytes\"] = size","    health_text = dumps(health) + \"\\n\"","    write_text(os.path.join(agg, \"summary.json\"), summary_text)","    write_text(os.path.join(agg, \"health.json\"), health_text)","    write_text(os.path.join(agg, \"preview.js\"), preview_text)","    return {\"summary\": summary, \"health\": health, \"bytes\": size}","","","# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- cli","","def main(argv=None):","    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Almanac: daily AQHI pipeline with a data contract.\")","    g = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)","    g.add_argument(\"--date\", help=\"process one UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\")","    g.add_argument(\"--backfill\", nargs=2, metavar=(\"START\", \"END\"), help=\"process every day from START to END\")","    g.add_argument(\"--aggregate-only\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"rebuild data/aggregates from stored data\")","    p.add_argument(\"--kind\", choices=[\"scheduled\", \"manual\", \"backfill\", \"revision\"],","                   help=\"label for the run log (default: scheduled under a GitHub cron, backfill for --backfill, else manual)\")","    p.add_argument(\"--source\", choices=[\"auto\", \"hourly\", \"monthly\"], default=\"auto\",","                   help=\"auto reads the live hourly file while it still covers the day, else the monthly archive\")","    p.add_argument(\"--now\", help=\"pretend the clock reads this ISO time (tests)\")","    p.add_argument(\"--data-dir\", default=DEFAULT_DATA)","    p.add_argument(\"--source-dir\", help=\"read source files from this folder instead of the network\")","    p.add_argument(\"--contract\", help=\"path to contract.json\")","    p.add_argument(\"--pause\", type=float, default=1.0, help=\"seconds between requests\")","    a = p.parse_args(argv)","","    contract = C.load_contract(a.contract)","    with open(os.path.join(HERE, \"known_issues.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","        known = json.load(f)","    fixed = parse_iso(a.now) if a.now else None","    now = (lambda: fixed) if fixed else utcnow","    data_dir = os.path.abspath(a.data_dir)","","    if a.aggregate_only:","        out = build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known)","        print(\"aggregates: %s bytes\" % (out[\"bytes\"] if out else 0))","        return 0","","    if a.backfill:","        start, end = Date.fromisoformat(a.backfill[0]), Date.fromisoformat(a.backfill[1])","        if end < start:","            p.error(\"END is before START\")","        kind = a.kind or \"backfill\"","    else:","        start = end = Date.fromisoformat(a.date)","        kind = a.kind or (\"scheduled\" if os.environ.get(\"GITHUB_EVENT_NAME\") == \"schedule\" else \"manual\")","    if end >= now().date():","        p.error(\"a day can only be processed once it is over (UTC)\")","","    source_mode = \"monthly\" if kind == \"revision\" and a.source == \"auto\" else a.source","    ctx = {\"contract\": contract, \"fetcher\": Fetcher(a.source_dir, a.pause), \"data_dir\": data_dir,","           \"now\": now, \"kind\": kind, \"batch_id\": \"%s-%s\" % (kind, now().strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\")),","           \"source_mode\": source_mode, \"resolved\": {}}","    worst = \"pass\"","    for day in days(start, end):","        r = process_day(day, ctx)","        worst = C.worst([worst, r[\"status\"]])","        print(\"%s  %-9s %-5s in %4d out %4d  %s\" % (r[\"date\"], r[\"kind\"], r[\"status\"], r[\"rows_in\"], r[\"rows_out\"],","                                                    \" \".join(\"%s:%s\" % (c[\"name\"], c[\"status\"]) for c in r[\"checks\"] if c[\"status\"] != \"pass\")))","    out = build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known)","    print(\"downloaded %d bytes; aggregates %d bytes\" % (ctx[\"fetcher\"].downloaded, out[\"bytes\"] if out else 0))","    if out and out[\"bytes\"] > contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]:","        print(\"WARNING: aggregates are %d bytes, over their %d-byte budget\"","              % (out[\"bytes\"], contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]), file=sys.stderr)","    return 2 if worst == \"fail\" else 0","","","if __name__ == \"__main__\":","    sys.exit(main())"],"sha256":"bdda6e18d3e146964111293a318ac40af7329c85ab4457981174241decf27daa"},{"path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","lines":["\"\"\"Almanac's data contract: the checks a day of AQHI observations must pass before it is loaded.","","The rules and thresholds live in contract.json. This module only knows how to apply them.","Each check returns {\"name\", \"status\", \"detail\"}, where status is one of","pass, warn, fail or skip (skip = does not apply to this kind of run).","\"\"\"","import json","import math","import os","import re","from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone","","HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))","DATE_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$\")","INT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\d{1,2}$\")","NUM_RE = re.compile(r\"^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$\")","RANK = {\"skip\": 0, \"pass\": 0, \"warn\": 1, \"fail\": 2}","","","def load_contract(path=None):","    with open(path or os.path.join(HERE, \"contract.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","        return json.load(f)","","","def check_cfg(contract, name):","    for c in contract[\"checks\"]:","        if c[\"name\"] == name:","            return c","    raise KeyError(name)","","","def reported(value):","    \"\"\"The AQHI as the public sees it: rounded half up to a whole number; 11 means 10+.\"\"\"","    return int(math.floor(value + 0.5))","","","def worst(statuses):","    top = \"pass\"","    for s in statuses:","        if RANK[s] > RANK[top]:","            top = s","    return top","","","def plural(n, word, many=None):","    return \"%d %s\" % (n, word if n == 1 else (many or word + \"s\"))","","","def validate(contract, date, sources, now=None, live=True):","    \"\"\"Apply the contract to one UTC day.","","    sources: {region: {\"header\": [str], \"rows\": [[str]] (rows whose date cell is `date`),","                       \"newest\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z\" or None}}","             A region with no file at all is None or {\"absent\": \"live\" | \"archive\",","             \"lookback_hours\": n}: \"live\" when the run looked for the live feed and found none.","    now:     datetime (UTC) of the run, for the freshness check.","    live:    True when the source is the live hourly feed, False for a monthly archive.","","    Returns (checks, good_rows, quarantined) where good_rows are dicts ready to load","    and quarantined are dicts with a reason.","    \"\"\"","    cols = contract[\"columns\"]","    locs = contract[\"locations\"]","    checks = []","    quarantined = []","","    # 0. no file at all -----------------------------------------------------","    # A region with no source file is not a broken schema: there is nothing to check.","    # From the live feed it means the feed has stalled (freshness); from an archive it","    # means the source does not cover the day (completeness). Every other check is not run.","    absent = [r for r in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs})","              if not sources.get(r) or sources[r].get(\"absent\")]","    if absent:","        names = \", \".join(r.upper() for r in absent)","        live_absent = [r for r in absent if (sources.get(r) or {}).get(\"absent\") == \"live\"]","        if live_absent:","            fc = check_cfg(contract, \"freshness\")","            look = (sources[live_absent[0]] or {}).get(\"lookback_hours\")","            checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                           \"detail\": \"No live file for %s in the last %s: the feed seems to have stalled (limit %d hours).\" % (","                               \", \".join(r.upper() for r in live_absent),","                               plural(look, \"hour\") if look else \"few hours\", fc[\"max_age_hours\"])})","        else:","            checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                           \"detail\": \"The source has no file that covers this day (%s).\" % names})","        done = {c[\"name\"] for c in checks}","        for c in contract[\"checks\"]:","            if c[\"name\"] not in done:","                checks.append({\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"status\": \"skip\",","                               \"detail\": \"Not run, because there was no file to check.\"})","        order_ = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]","        checks.sort(key=lambda c: order_.index(c[\"name\"]))","        return checks, [], quarantined","","    # 1. schema -------------------------------------------------------------","    missing = []","    for region in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs}):","        src = sources.get(region)","        header = src[\"header\"] if src else []","        need = [cols[\"date\"], cols[\"hour\"]] + [l[\"id\"] for l in locs if l[\"region\"] == region]","        missing += [\"%s (%s)\" % (n, region.upper()) for n in need if n not in header]","    if missing:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"schema\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                       \"detail\": \"Missing column%s: %s.\" % (\"\" if len(missing) == 1 else \"s\", \", \".join(missing))})","        return finish(contract, checks), [], quarantined","    checks.append({\"name\": \"schema\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                   \"detail\": \"All %d expected columns are present.\" % (2 + len(locs))})","","    # Gather cells: (hour, location) -> list of raw strings","    bad_types = []","    hours_seen = set()","    cells = {}","    for region in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs}):","        src = sources[region]","        idx = {name: i for i, name in enumerate(src[\"header\"])}","        mine = [l for l in locs if l[\"region\"] == region]","        region_hours = []","        for row in src[\"rows\"]:","            def cell(name):","                i = idx[name]","                return row[i].strip() if i < len(row) else \"\"","            d, h = cell(cols[\"date\"]), cell(cols[\"hour\"])","            if not DATE_RE.match(d) or not INT_RE.match(h) or not 0 <= int(h) <= 23:","                bad_types.append(\"%s row with date %r and hour %r\" % (region.upper(), d, h))","                continue","            hour = int(h)","            region_hours.append(hour)","            for l in mine:","                v = cell(l[\"id\"])","                if v == \"\":","                    continue","                if not NUM_RE.match(v):","                    bad_types.append(\"%s at %02d:00 is %r\" % (l[\"city\"], hour, v))","                    quarantined.append(qrow(date, hour, l, v, \"not a number\"))","                    continue","                cells.setdefault((hour, l[\"id\"]), []).append(v)","        hours_seen.update(region_hours)","        sources[region][\"_hours\"] = region_hours","","    # 2. types --------------------------------------------------------------","    if bad_types:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"types\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                       \"detail\": \"%s of the wrong kind, e.g. %s.\" % (plural(len(bad_types), \"value\"), bad_types[0])})","    else:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"types\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                       \"detail\": \"Every date, hour and reading parsed.\"})","","    # 3. range --------------------------------------------------------------","    rc = check_cfg(contract, \"range\")","    in_range = {}","    odd = []","    total_readings = 0","    by_id = {l[\"id\"]: l for l in locs}","    for key in sorted(cells):","        hour, lid = key","        kept = []","        for v in cells[key]:","            total_readings += 1","            x = float(v)","            if rc[\"min\"] <= x <= rc[\"max\"]:","                kept.append(v)","            else:","                odd.append(\"%s at %02d:00 = %s\" % (by_id[lid][\"city\"], hour, v))","                quarantined.append(qrow(date, hour, by_id[lid], v, \"outside %g to %g\" % (rc[\"min\"], rc[\"max\"])))","        if kept:","            in_range[key] = kept","    if not odd:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"range\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                       \"detail\": \"All %s lie between %g and %g.\" % (plural(total_readings, \"reading\"), rc[\"min\"], rc[\"max\"])})","    else:","        frac = len(odd) / float(max(total_readings, 1))","        status = \"fail\" if frac > rc[\"fail_fraction\"] else \"warn\"","        checks.append({\"name\": \"range\", \"status\": status,","                       \"detail\": \"%s of %d set aside (%s), e.g. %s.\" % (","                           plural(len(odd), \"reading\"), total_readings,","                           \"too many to trust the day\" if status == \"fail\" else \"few enough to load the rest\", odd[0])})","","    # 4. uniqueness ---------------------------------------------------------","    dup_same, dup_conflict = [], []","    good = {}","    for key in sorted(in_range):","        vals = in_range[key]","        if len(vals) == 1:","            good[key] = vals[0]","            continue","        if len({float(v) for v in vals}) == 1:","            dup_same.append(key)","            good[key] = vals[0]","        else:","            dup_conflict.append(key)","            for v in vals:","                quarantined.append(qrow(date, key[0], by_id[key[1]], v, \"conflicting duplicate\"))","    def name_key(k):","        return \"%s at %02d:00\" % (by_id[k[1]][\"city\"], k[0])","    if dup_conflict:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"uniqueness\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                       \"detail\": \"%s with two different readings, e.g. %s.\" % (plural(len(dup_conflict), \"city-hour\"), name_key(dup_conflict[0]))})","    elif dup_same:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"uniqueness\", \"status\": \"warn\",","                       \"detail\": \"%s repeated with the same reading; one copy kept.\" % plural(len(dup_same), \"city-hour\")})","    else:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"uniqueness\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                       \"detail\": \"No city has two readings for the same hour.\"})","","    # 5. completeness -------------------------------------------------------","    cc = check_cfg(contract, \"completeness\")","    short = []","    for region in sorted(sources):","        if region not in {l[\"region\"] for l in locs}:","            continue","        n = len(set(sources[region].get(\"_hours\", [])))","        if n < cc[\"hours\"]:","            short.append((region, n))","    if any(n == 0 for _, n in short):","        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                       \"detail\": \"The source has no rows for this day (%s).\" % \", \".join(r.upper() for r, n in short if n == 0)})","    elif short:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"warn\",","                       \"detail\": \"Only %s.\" % \"; \".join(\"%d of %d hours in the %s file\" % (n, cc[\"hours\"], r.upper()) for r, n in short)})","    else:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                       \"detail\": \"All %d hours are in the file.\" % cc[\"hours\"]})","","    # 6. volume -------------------------------------------------------------","    vc = check_cfg(contract, \"volume\")","    per_city = {l[\"id\"]: 0 for l in locs}","    for (hour, lid) in good:","        per_city[lid] += 1","    expected = cc[\"hours\"] * len(locs)","    total = sum(per_city.values())","    thin = [(by_id[lid][\"city\"], n) for lid, n in per_city.items() if n < vc[\"min_hours_per_city\"]]","    if total < vc[\"fail_below_fraction\"] * expected:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"fail\",","                       \"detail\": \"Only %d of %d expected readings; too few to load.\" % (total, expected)})","    elif thin:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"warn\",","                       \"detail\": \"%s; high-risk hours there may be missed (%d of %d readings in all).\" % (","                           \"; \".join(\"%s had readings for %d of 24 hours\" % t for t in thin), total, expected)})","    else:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                       \"detail\": \"%d of %d readings; every city had at least %d hours.\" % (total, expected, vc[\"min_hours_per_city\"])})","","    # 7. freshness ----------------------------------------------------------","    fc = check_cfg(contract, \"freshness\")","    if not live:","        checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"skip\",","                       \"detail\": \"Read from a monthly archive, so the live feed's age does not apply.\"})","    else:","        newest = [s.get(\"newest\") for s in sources.values() if s.get(\"newest\")]","        if not newest or now is None:","            checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"fail\", \"detail\": \"Could not tell how new the source is.\"})","        else:","            oldest_newest = min(parse_hour(n) for n in newest)","            age = (now - oldest_newest).total_seconds() / 3600.0","            if age <= fc[\"max_age_hours\"]:","                checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"pass\",","                               \"detail\": \"The feed's newest hour was %.1f hours old.\" % max(age, 0)})","            else:","                checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"warn\",","                               \"detail\": \"The feed's newest hour was %.1f hours old (limit %d).\" % (age, fc[\"max_age_hours\"])})","","    status = worst(c[\"status\"] for c in checks)","    rows = []","    if status != \"fail\":","        thr = contract[\"high_risk_threshold\"]","        for (hour, lid) in sorted(good, key=lambda k: (k[0], order(locs, k[1]))):","            x = float(good[(hour, lid)])","            r = reported(x)","            rows.append({","                \"date\": date, \"hour_utc\": hour, \"location_id\": lid, \"city\": by_id[lid][\"city\"],","                \"aqhi\": \"%.2f\" % x, \"aqhi_reported\": \"10+\" if r > 10 else str(r),","                \"high_risk\": 1 if r >= thr else 0,","            })","    return checks, rows, quarantined","","","def finish(contract, checks):","    names = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]","    done = {c[\"name\"] for c in checks}","    for n in names:","        if n not in done:","            checks.append({\"name\": n, \"status\": \"skip\", \"detail\": \"Not run, because an earlier check failed.\"})","    return checks","","","def order(locs, lid):","    for i, l in enumerate(locs):","        if l[\"id\"] == lid:","            return i","    return 99","","","def qrow(date, hour, loc, value, reason):","    return {\"date\": date, \"hour_utc\": hour, \"location_id\": loc[\"id\"], \"city\": loc[\"city\"],","            \"value\": value, \"reason\": reason}","","","def parse_hour(s):","    return datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)"],"sha256":"b88d82e41f863313e920670a5884d1fcfc432a7edd5f38f63039518b8bc93204"},{"path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json","lines":["{","  \"name\": \"aqhi-hourly-observations\",","  \"version\": 1,","  \"about\": \"The promise each day's AQHI observations must keep before Almanac loads them. Read by pipeline/contract.py; the 'plain' lines are shown on the page.\",","  \"source\": {","    \"publisher\": \"Environment and Climate Change Canada, Meteorological Service of Canada\",","    \"attribution\": \"Data Source: Environment and Climate Change Canada\",","    \"licence\": \"Environment and Climate Change Canada Data Services End-use Licence\",","    \"licence_url\": \"https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/licence/readme_en/\",","    \"docs_url\": \"https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/msc-data/aqhi/readme_aqhi_en/\",","    \"hourly_url\": \"https://dd.weather.gc.ca/{yyyymmdd}/WXO-DD/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/realtime/csv/{yyyymmddhh}_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs.csv\",","    \"monthly_url\": \"https://dd.weather.gc.ca/today/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/monthly/csv/{yyyymm}_MONTHLY_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs{suffix}.csv\",","    \"hourly_window_days\": 6,","    \"hourly_lookback_hours\": 8","  },","  \"key\": [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\"],","  \"columns\": {","    \"date\": \"Date\",","    \"hour\": \"Hour (UTC)\"","  },","  \"locations\": [","    { \"id\": \"JBRIK\", \"city\": \"Vancouver\", \"zone\": \"Metro Vancouver – NW\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },","    { \"id\": \"JBOBQ\", \"city\": \"Victoria\", \"zone\": \"Victoria / Saanich\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },","    { \"id\": \"JAFUV\", \"city\": \"Kelowna\", \"zone\": \"Central Okanagan\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },","    { \"id\": \"JAFNW\", \"city\": \"Kamloops\", \"zone\": \"Kamloops\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },","    { \"id\": \"JBLVS\", \"city\": \"Prince George\", \"zone\": \"Prince George\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },","    { \"id\": \"IAKID\", \"city\": \"Calgary\", \"zone\": \"Calgary\", \"region\": \"pnr\" },","    { \"id\": \"IACMP\", \"city\": \"Edmonton\", \"zone\": \"Edmonton\", \"region\": \"pnr\" }","  ],","  \"high_risk_threshold\": 7,","  \"checks\": [","    {","      \"name\": \"schema\",","      \"title\": \"The columns are where we expect them\",","      \"plain\": \"The file must have a date column, an hour column and one column for each of the seven cities. If ECCC renames or drops a column, nothing is loaded.\",","      \"severity\": \"fail\"","    },","    {","      \"name\": \"types\",","      \"title\": \"Every value is the right kind of thing\",","      \"plain\": \"Dates must be dates, hours must be whole numbers from 0 to 23, and readings must be numbers or blank. Anything else means the format changed, so nothing is loaded.\",","      \"severity\": \"fail\"","    },","    {","      \"name\": \"range\",","      \"title\": \"Readings are on the AQHI scale\",","      \"plain\": \"A reading must lie between 1 and 11 (the file writes the top category, 10+, as 11). Odd values are set aside; if more than 1 in 100 are odd, the day is refused.\",","      \"min\": 1.0,","      \"max\": 11.0,","      \"fail_fraction\": 0.01","    },","    {","      \"name\": \"uniqueness\",","      \"title\": \"One reading per city per hour\",","      \"plain\": \"Each city may have only one reading for each hour. Exact repeats are dropped with a warning; two different readings for the same hour stop the load.\",","      \"severity\": \"fail\"","    },","    {","      \"name\": \"completeness\",","      \"title\": \"All 24 hours of the day are in the file\",","      \"plain\": \"The source file must contain a row for every hour of the day, even if some cities are blank in it. A short day is a warning; a missing day is a failure.\",","      \"hours\": 24","    },","    {","      \"name\": \"volume\",","      \"title\": \"Enough cities reported\",","      \"plain\": \"Each city should have a reading for at least 18 of the 24 hours. Fewer is a warning, because high-risk hours could be missed. Under half of all expected readings is a failure.\",","      \"min_hours_per_city\": 18,","      \"fail_below_fraction\": 0.5","    },","    {","      \"name\": \"freshness\",","      \"title\": \"The source is up to date\",","      \"plain\": \"When the daily run reads the live feed, its newest hour should be at most 6 hours old. Older is a warning that the feed may be stalling; no live file at all in the last 8 hours means it has stalled, and the day is refused. A backfill reads a monthly archive, so this does not apply.\",","      \"max_age_hours\": 6","    }","  ],","  \"slo\": {","    \"plain\": \"Fresh means the newest hour on this page is at most 36 hours old and the pipeline has run in the last 26 hours.\",","    \"max_data_age_hours\": 36,","    \"max_run_age_hours\": 26","  },","  \"budgets\": {","    \"aggregates_bytes\": 200000,","    \"detail_days\": 90","  }","}"],"sha256":"5e92a73ff1bb87f1f4c5743a2ab9fd5ae5db3a9760d5c62ead4460cc6af6adb6"},{"path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml","lines":["# Install (once, from the repo root, with a token that has the workflow scope): mkdir -p .github/workflows && git mv projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml .github/workflows/almanac.yml && git commit -m \"Schedule the Almanac pipeline\" && git push","#","# Almanac: fetch yesterday's AQHI observations from ECCC, check them against","# projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json, store them, rebuild the page's aggregates and","# append a run record. Commits only when something under projects/almanac/data changed.","# A run whose contract fails is still committed (the page must show the red day), and","# then the job is marked failed so the owner is told.","","name: Almanac pipeline","","on:","  schedule:","    - cron: \"17 7 * * *\" # 07:17 UTC every day; the previous UTC day is complete by then","  workflow_dispatch:","    inputs:","      date:","        description: \"UTC day to process, YYYY-MM-DD (blank means yesterday)\"","        required: false","        default: \"\"","      backfill_start:","        description: \"Backfill from this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD (with backfill_end)\"","        required: false","        default: \"\"","      backfill_end:","        description: \"Backfill to this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\"","        required: false","        default: \"\"","","permissions:","  contents: write","","concurrency:","  group: almanac-pipeline","  cancel-in-progress: false","","jobs:","  run:","    runs-on: ubuntu-latest","    timeout-minutes: 15","    steps:","      - name: Check out","        uses: actions/checkout@v4","","      - name: Set up Python","        uses: actions/setup-python@v5","        with:","          python-version: \"3.11\"","","      - name: Contract tests","        run: python -I -m unittest discover -s projects/almanac/tests -p \"test_*.py\"","","      - name: Run the pipeline","        id: run","        env:","          IN_DATE: ${{ github.event.inputs.date }}","          IN_START: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_start }}","          IN_END: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_end }}","          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}","        run: |","          set +e","          code=0","          if [ -n \"$IN_START\" ] && [ -n \"$IN_END\" ]; then","            label=\"backfill $IN_START to $IN_END\"","            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$IN_START\" \"$IN_END\" || code=$?","          else","            day=\"${IN_DATE:-$(date -u -d yesterday +%F)}\"","            label=\"$day\"","            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date \"$day\" || code=$?","            # On the 4th, reload last month from ECCC's corrected (\"backfilled\") monthly file.","            if [ \"$EVENT\" = \"schedule\" ] && [ \"$(date -u +%d)\" = \"04\" ]; then","              first=$(date -u +%Y-%m-01)","              start=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 month\" +%F)","              end=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 day\" +%F)","              label=\"$label, revision $start to $end\"","              python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$start\" \"$end\" --kind revision || code=$?","            fi","          fi","          echo \"code=$code\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"","          echo \"label=$label\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"","","      - name: Commit the data if it changed","        env:","          LABEL: ${{ steps.run.outputs.label }}","        run: |","          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"","          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"","          git add projects/almanac/data","          if git diff --cached --quiet; then","            echo \"Nothing changed.\"","            exit 0","          fi","          git commit -m \"Almanac: $LABEL\"","          git pull --rebase","          git push","","      - name: Report a failed contract","        if: steps.run.outputs.code != '0'","        run: |","          echo \"The pipeline recorded a failed run (exit ${{ steps.run.outputs.code }}). See projects/almanac/data/runs.ndjson.\"","          exit 1"],"sha256":"83361fd2fa95872d325ec3d6950d6b1a6e44736cb7b344d260996cb8193dd794"},{"path":".github/workflows/almanac.yml","lines":["# Install (once, from the repo root, with a token that has the workflow scope): mkdir -p .github/workflows && git mv projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml .github/workflows/almanac.yml && git commit -m \"Schedule the Almanac pipeline\" && git push","#","# Almanac: fetch yesterday's AQHI observations from ECCC, check them against","# projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json, store them, rebuild the page's aggregates and","# append a run record. Commits only when something under projects/almanac/data changed.","# A run whose contract fails is still committed (the page must show the red day), and","# then the job is marked failed so the owner is told.","","name: Almanac pipeline","","on:","  schedule:","    - cron: \"17 7 * * *\" # 07:17 UTC every day; the previous UTC day is complete by then","  workflow_dispatch:","    inputs:","      date:","        description: \"UTC day to process, YYYY-MM-DD (blank means yesterday)\"","        required: false","        default: \"\"","      backfill_start:","        description: \"Backfill from this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD (with backfill_end)\"","        required: false","        default: \"\"","      backfill_end:","        description: \"Backfill to this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\"","        required: false","        default: \"\"","","permissions:","  contents: write","","concurrency:","  group: almanac-pipeline","  cancel-in-progress: false","","jobs:","  run:","    runs-on: ubuntu-latest","    timeout-minutes: 15","    steps:","      - name: Check out","        uses: actions/checkout@v4","","      - name: Set up Python","        uses: actions/setup-python@v5","        with:","          python-version: \"3.11\"","","      - name: Contract tests","        run: python -I -m unittest discover -s projects/almanac/tests -p \"test_*.py\"","","      - name: Run the pipeline","        id: run","        env:","          IN_DATE: ${{ github.event.inputs.date }}","          IN_START: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_start }}","          IN_END: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_end }}","          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}","        run: |","          set +e","          code=0","          if [ -n \"$IN_START\" ] && [ -n \"$IN_END\" ]; then","            label=\"backfill $IN_START to $IN_END\"","            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$IN_START\" \"$IN_END\" || code=$?","          else","            day=\"${IN_DATE:-$(date -u -d yesterday +%F)}\"","            label=\"$day\"","            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date \"$day\" || code=$?","            # On the 4th, reload last month from ECCC's corrected (\"backfilled\") monthly file.","            if [ \"$EVENT\" = \"schedule\" ] && [ \"$(date -u +%d)\" = \"04\" ]; then","              first=$(date -u +%Y-%m-01)","              start=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 month\" +%F)","              end=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 day\" +%F)","              label=\"$label, revision $start to $end\"","              python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$start\" \"$end\" --kind revision || code=$?","            fi","          fi","          echo \"code=$code\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"","          echo \"label=$label\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"","","      - name: Commit the data if it changed","        env:","          LABEL: ${{ steps.run.outputs.label }}","        run: |","          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"","          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"","          git add projects/almanac/data","          if git diff --cached --quiet; then","            echo \"Nothing changed.\"","            exit 0","          fi","          git commit -m \"Almanac: $LABEL\"","          git pull --rebase","          git push","","      - name: Report a failed contract","        if: steps.run.outputs.code != '0'","        run: |","          echo \"The pipeline recorded a failed run (exit ${{ steps.run.outputs.code }}). See projects/almanac/data/runs.ndjson.\"","          exit 1"],"sha256":"83361fd2fa95872d325ec3d6950d6b1a6e44736cb7b344d260996cb8193dd794"},{"path":"projects/almanac/model.js","lines":["// Almanac: the page's logic, kept apart from drawing so Node can test it.","// Works in the browser (window.AlmanacModel) and in Node (module.exports).","(function (root) {","  'use strict';","","  var HOUR = 3600 * 1000;","  var MONTHS = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];","  var LONG_MONTHS = ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', 'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'];","  var DAYS = ['Sun', 'Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri', 'Sat'];","","  function parse(iso) {","    if (!iso) return NaN;","    if (/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/.test(iso)) iso += 'T00:00:00Z';","    return Date.parse(iso);","  }","","  // ---- words and numbers -------------------------------------------------","","  function plural(n, word, many) {","    return fmtInt(n) + ' ' + (n === 1 ? word : (many || word + 's'));","  }","","  function fmtInt(n) {","    return String(Math.round(n)).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ',');","  }","","  function ageText(hours) {","    if (!isFinite(hours)) return 'unknown';","    if (hours < 0) hours = 0;","    if (hours < 1) {","      var m = Math.round(hours * 60);","      return m <= 1 ? 'a minute' : m + ' minutes';","    }","    if (hours < 48) {","      var h = Math.round(hours);","      return h === 1 ? '1 hour' : h + ' hours';","    }","    var d = Math.floor(hours / 24);","    return d + ' days';","  }","","  function dayLabel(iso, withYear) {","    var t = new Date(parse(iso));","    return t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + (withYear ? ' ' + t.getUTCFullYear() : '');","  }","","  function longDay(iso) {","    var t = new Date(parse(iso));","    return DAYS[t.getUTCDay()] + ' ' + t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + LONG_MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + ' ' + t.getUTCFullYear();","  }","","  function stamp(iso) {","    var t = new Date(parse(iso));","    var hh = ('0' + t.getUTCHours()).slice(-2), mm = ('0' + t.getUTCMinutes()).slice(-2);","    return t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + ', ' + hh + ':' + mm + ' UTC';","  }","","  function bytesText(b) {","    if (b >= 1e6) return (b / 1e6).toFixed(1) + ' MB';","    if (b >= 1e3) return Math.round(b / 1e3) + ' KB';","    return b + ' bytes';","  }","","  // ---- freshness ---------------------------------------------------------","  // Fresh only when the newest hour of data is within the data SLO AND the pipeline","  // ran recently enough. `now` is injected so the rule can be tested without a clock.","","  function freshness(now, latestHour, latestRunFinished, slo) {","    var dataAge = (now - parse(latestHour)) / HOUR;","    var runAge = (now - parse(latestRunFinished)) / HOUR;","    var reasons = [];","    if (!isFinite(dataAge)) reasons.push('There is no data yet.');","    else if (dataAge > slo.max_data_age_hours) {","      reasons.push('The newest hour is ' + ageText(dataAge) + ' old; the limit is ' + slo.max_data_age_hours + ' hours.');","    }","    if (!isFinite(runAge)) reasons.push('The pipeline has never run.');","    else if (runAge > slo.max_run_age_hours) {","      reasons.push('The last run was ' + ageText(runAge) + ' ago; it should run at least every ' + slo.max_run_age_hours + ' hours.');","    }","    var stale = reasons.length > 0;","    return {","      state: stale ? 'stale' : 'fresh',","      word: stale ? 'Stale' : 'Fresh',","      dataAgeHours: dataAge,","      runAgeHours: runAge,","      reasons: reasons,","      // fraction of the data SLO used, for the dial (can exceed 1)","      used: isFinite(dataAge) ? Math.max(0, dataAge) / slo.max_data_age_hours : Infinity","    };","  }","","  // ---- runs and contract -------------------------------------------------","","  var STATUS = {","    pass: { word: 'Passed', glyph: '✓', day: 'all checks passed' },","    warn: { word: 'Warning', glyph: '!', day: 'loaded with a warning' },","    fail: { word: 'Failed', glyph: '×', day: 'refused: a check failed' },","    skip: { word: 'Not run', glyph: '–', day: '' },","    none: { word: 'No run', glyph: '', day: 'no run for this day' }","  };","  var CODE = { p: 'pass', w: 'warn', f: 'fail', s: 'skip' };","","  var KIND = {","    scheduled: 'scheduled run',","    manual: 'run by hand',","    backfill: 'backfill',","    revision: 'revision from ECCC’s corrected file'","  };","","  function dayChecks(day, health) {","    // [{name, title, plain, status, detail}] for one calendar entry","    var defs = health.contract.checks;","    return defs.map(function (def, i) {","      var code = day.checks ? day.checks.charAt(i) : 's';","      return {","        name: def.name, title: def.title, plain: def.plain,","        status: CODE[code] || 'skip',","        detail: day.details ? day.details[i] : null","      };","    });","  }","","  function describeDay(day) {","    var s = STATUS[day.status] || STATUS.none;","    if (day.status === 'none') return longDay(day.date) + '. No run.';","    var kind = KIND[day.kind] || day.kind;","    var parts = [longDay(day.date) + '.', s.word + ': ' + s.day + '.'];","    parts.push(kind.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + kind.slice(1) + (day.runs > 1 ? ' (' + day.runs + ' runs; latest shown)' : '') + '.');","    parts.push(loadedText(day));","    if (day.details && day.checks) {","      for (var i = 0; i < day.checks.length; i++) {","        var c = day.checks.charAt(i);","        if ((c === 'w' || c === 'f') && day.details[i]) { parts.push(day.details[i]); break; }","      }","    }","    return parts.join(' ');","  }","","  function loadedText(day) {","    if (day.loaded) return fmtInt(day.rows_out) + ' of 168 readings loaded.';","    if (day.kept) return 'Nothing new loaded; the day’s earlier load (' + plural(day.kept, 'reading') + ') is kept and still counted.';","    return 'Nothing loaded.';","  }","","  // Which check causes the amber days: {total, counts: {name: days}, top: name, topCount}","  function warnCauses(calendar, names) {","    var out = { total: 0, counts: {}, top: null, topCount: 0 };","    calendar.forEach(function (d) {","      if (d.status !== 'warn' || !d.checks) return;","      out.total++;","      for (var i = 0; i < d.checks.length && i < names.length; i++) {","        if (d.checks.charAt(i) === 'w') out.counts[names[i]] = (out.counts[names[i]] || 0) + 1;","      }","    });","    names.forEach(function (n) {","      if ((out.counts[n] || 0) > out.topCount) { out.top = n; out.topCount = out.counts[n]; }","    });","    return out;","  }","","  // health.json keeps full entries for recent days and packs older ones into short tuples","  // (health.calendar_old); this returns one plain entry per day, oldest first.","  var UNPACK = {","    status: { p: 'pass', w: 'warn', f: 'fail', n: 'none' },","    kind: { s: 'scheduled', m: 'manual', b: 'backfill', r: 'revision' },","    src: { H: 'hourly snapshot', M: 'monthly archive', R: 'revised monthly archive' }","  };","  function expandCalendar(health) {","    var out = [], old = health.calendar_old;","    if (old && old.days && old.days.length) {","      var t0 = parse(old.first);","      old.days.forEach(function (t, i) {","        var ds = new Date(t0 + i * 24 * HOUR).toISOString().slice(0, 10);","        if (t[0] === 'n') { out.push({ date: ds, status: 'none' }); return; }","        var d = { date: ds };","        old.fields.forEach(function (f, k) { d[f] = t[k]; });","        d.status = UNPACK.status[d.status];","        d.kind = UNPACK.kind[d.kind];","        d.kinds = d.kinds.split('').map(function (c) { return UNPACK.kind[c]; });","        d.loaded = !!d.loaded;","        d.src = d.src.split('').map(function (c) { return UNPACK.src[c] || c; }).sort().join(',');","        if (!d.kept) delete d.kept;","        out.push(d);","      });","    }","    return out.concat(health.calendar || []);","  }","","  function tally(calendar) {","    var t = { pass: 0, warn: 0, fail: 0, none: 0, backfill: 0, scheduled: 0, total: 0 };","    calendar.forEach(function (d) {","      t[d.status] = (t[d.status] || 0) + 1;","      if (d.status !== 'none') {","        t.total++;","        if (d.kind === 'backfill' || d.kind === 'revision') t.backfill++;","        if (d.kind === 'scheduled') t.scheduled++;","      }","    });","    return t;","  }","","  // Lay days out as week columns (Monday first), like a wall calendar turned sideways.","  function calendarGrid(calendar) {","    if (!calendar.length) return { weeks: 0, cells: [], months: [] };","    var first = new Date(parse(calendar[0].date));","    var offset = (first.getUTCDay() + 6) % 7; // Monday = 0","    var cells = [], months = [], lastMonth = -1;","    calendar.forEach(function (d, i) {","      var k = i + offset;","      var col = Math.floor(k / 7), row = k % 7;","      var m = new Date(parse(d.date)).getUTCMonth();","      if (m !== lastMonth) { months.push({ col: col, label: MONTHS[m] }); lastMonth = m; }","      cells.push({ day: d, col: col, row: row });","    });","    return { weeks: Math.floor((calendar.length - 1 + offset) / 7) + 1, cells: cells, months: months };","  }","","  // The pipeline can only log days it ran. If it stops, the page itself adds the missing","  // days, up to yesterday by the visitor's clock, as \"no run\", so a silent gap still shows.","  function extendCalendar(calendar, now) {","    var out = calendar.slice();","    if (!out.length) return out;","    var day = 24 * HOUR;","    var last = parse(out[out.length - 1].date);","    var yesterday = Math.floor(now / day) * day - day;","    for (var t = last + day, k = 0; t <= yesterday && k < 400; t += day, k++) {","      out.push({ date: new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 10), status: 'none', added: true });","    }","    return out;","  }","","  // ---- the answer --------------------------------------------------------","","  function cityView(summary, id) {","    var c = null;","    summary.cities.forEach(function (x) { if (x.id === id) c = x; });","    if (!c) return null;","    var s = summary.series[id];","    var sum = 0;","    s.hi.forEach(function (h) { if (h) sum += h; });","    var coverage = c.hours_possible ? c.hours_with_reading / c.hours_possible : 0;","    return {","      city: c, total: c.high_hours, seriesTotal: sum, coverage: coverage,","      share: c.hours_with_reading ? c.high_hours / c.hours_with_reading : 0,","      gappy: coverage < 0.9","    };","  }","","  function ranked(summary) {","    return summary.cities.slice().sort(function (a, b) {","      return b.high_hours - a.high_hours || summary.cities.indexOf(a) - summary.cities.indexOf(b);","    });","  }","","  var api = {","    parse: parse, plural: plural, fmtInt: fmtInt, ageText: ageText, dayLabel: dayLabel, longDay: longDay,","    stamp: stamp, bytesText: bytesText, freshness: freshness, STATUS: STATUS, KIND: KIND,","    dayChecks: dayChecks, describeDay: describeDay, loadedText: loadedText, warnCauses: warnCauses, expandCalendar: expandCalendar,","    extendCalendar: extendCalendar, tally: tally, calendarGrid: calendarGrid,","    cityView: cityView, ranked: ranked, MONTHS: MONTHS","  };","  if (typeof module !== 'undefined' && module.exports) module.exports = api;","  else root.AlmanacModel = api;","})(this);"],"sha256":"e48f3229a8eb2c6b769ae69aa4e1f9542afcf543ed4897c1c4aa13cb463adfd4"},{"path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","lines":["\"\"\"Each contract check passes clean data and catches a crafted violation.","","    python -I -m unittest discover -s projects/almanac/tests -p \"test_*.py\"","\"\"\"","import copy","import os","import sys","import unittest","from datetime import datetime, timezone","","sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))","import fixtures as F  # noqa: E402","from fixtures import C, CONTRACT, DAY  # noqa: E402","","NOW = datetime(2026, 8, 16, 7, 17, tzinfo=timezone.utc)","","","def run(src, live=True, now=NOW):","    checks, rows, q = C.validate(CONTRACT, DAY, src, now=now, live=live)","    return {c[\"name\"]: c for c in checks}, rows, q","","","class CleanData(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_clean_day_passes_every_check(self):","        res, rows, q = run(F.sources())","        for name in (\"schema\", \"types\", \"range\", \"uniqueness\", \"completeness\", \"volume\", \"freshness\"):","            self.assertEqual(res[name][\"status\"], \"pass\", (name, res[name][\"detail\"]))","        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)","        self.assertEqual(q, [])","","    def test_high_risk_rounding(self):","        _, rows, _ = run(F.sources())","        hi = [r for r in rows if r[\"high_risk\"]]","        self.assertEqual(len(hi), 4)","        self.assertTrue(all(r[\"city\"] == \"Kamloops\" for r in hi))","        self.assertEqual(C.reported(6.49), 6)","        self.assertEqual(C.reported(6.5), 7)","        self.assertEqual(C.reported(11.0), 11)","","    def test_every_check_is_reported_once(self):","        res, _, _ = run(F.sources())","        self.assertEqual(sorted(res), sorted(c[\"name\"] for c in CONTRACT[\"checks\"]))","","","class Schema(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_missing_city_column_fails_and_loads_nothing(self):","        src = F.sources()","        i = src[\"pnr\"][\"header\"].index(\"IAKID\")","        src[\"pnr\"][\"header\"][i] = \"IAKIX\"","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertIn(\"IAKID\", res[\"schema\"][\"detail\"])","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")","","    def test_extra_columns_are_fine(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pyr\"][\"header\"].append(\"ZZNEW\")","        for r in src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"]:","            r.append(\"2.00\")","        res, _, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")","","","class Types(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_text_in_a_reading_fails(self):","        src = F.sources()","        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBRIK\", 5, \"n/a\")","        res, rows, q = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","        self.assertEqual(q[0][\"reason\"], \"not a number\")","","    def test_bad_hour_fails(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"][0][1] = \"25\"","        res, _, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","","    def test_blank_reading_is_allowed(self):","        src = F.sources()","        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBRIK\", 5, \"\")","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")","        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 1)","","","class Range(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_one_odd_value_is_set_aside_with_a_warning(self):","        src = F.sources()","        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBOBQ\", 3, \"-9.00\")","        res, rows, q = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")","        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 1)","        self.assertEqual(len(q), 1)","        self.assertEqual(q[0][\"city\"], \"Victoria\")","","    def test_many_odd_values_fail(self):","        src = F.sources()","        for h in range(4):","            F.set_cell(src, \"pnr\", \"IACMP\", h, \"120.00\")","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","","    def test_ten_plus_written_as_eleven_is_in_range(self):","        src = F.sources()","        F.set_cell(src, \"pnr\", \"IAKID\", 2, \"11.00\")","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")","        r = [r for r in rows if r[\"location_id\"] == \"IAKID\" and r[\"hour_utc\"] == 2][0]","        self.assertEqual(r[\"aqhi_reported\"], \"10+\")","        self.assertEqual(r[\"high_risk\"], 1)","","","class Uniqueness(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_conflicting_duplicate_fails(self):","        src = F.sources()","        dup = copy.deepcopy(src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"][0])","        dup[src[\"pyr\"][\"header\"].index(\"JBRIK\")] = \"4.00\"","        src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"].append(dup)","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"uniqueness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","","    def test_exact_duplicate_warns_and_keeps_one(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"].append(list(src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"][3]))","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"uniqueness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")","        keys = [(r[\"hour_utc\"], r[\"location_id\"]) for r in rows]","        self.assertEqual(len(keys), len(set(keys)))","        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)","","","class Completeness(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_missing_hours_warn(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"] = [r for r in src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"] if int(r[1]) not in (0, 1)]","        res, _, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")","        self.assertIn(\"22 of 24\", res[\"completeness\"][\"detail\"])","","    def test_missing_day_fails(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"] = []","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","","","class Volume(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_quiet_city_warns(self):","        src = F.sources()","        for h in range(10):","            F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JAFUV\", h, \"\")","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")","        self.assertIn(\"Kelowna had readings for 14 of 24 hours\", res[\"volume\"][\"detail\"])","        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 10)","","    def test_mostly_empty_day_fails(self):","        src = F.sources()","        for station in (\"JAFUV\", \"JAFNW\", \"JBLVS\", \"JBOBQ\"):","            for h in range(24):","                F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", station, h, \"\")","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","","","class Freshness(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_stale_feed_warns(self):","        res, _, _ = run(F.sources(newest=\"2026-08-15T20:00:00Z\"))","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")","","    def test_archive_skips(self):","        res, rows, _ = run(F.sources(), live=False)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")","        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)","","    def test_unknown_age_fails(self):","        res, _, _ = run(F.sources(newest=None))","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","","    def test_no_live_file_is_a_stalled_feed_not_a_schema_break(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pyr\"] = {\"absent\": \"live\", \"lookback_hours\": 8}","        res, rows, _ = run(src)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertIn(\"PYR\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])","        self.assertIn(\"8 hours\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])","        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","","","class NoFile(unittest.TestCase):","    def test_no_archive_file_fails_completeness(self):","        src = F.sources()","        src[\"pnr\"] = None","        res, rows, _ = run(src, live=False)","        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertIn(\"PNR\", res[\"completeness\"][\"detail\"])","        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")","        self.assertEqual(rows, [])","","","if __name__ == \"__main__\":","    unittest.main()"],"sha256":"45f011f2496433a37262921811587adf25d129924f540d907c9903ab399f8e4e"},{"path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","lines":["\"\"\"End-to-end pipeline tests on crafted files read from disk (no network):","idempotency, backfill, failed days keep earlier data, and the run log.\"\"\"","import filecmp","import json","import os","import shutil","import sys","import tempfile","import unittest","","sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))","import fixtures as F  # noqa: E402","import run as R  # noqa: E402  (pipeline/run.py, on the path via fixtures)","","DAYS = [\"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-15\", \"2026-08-16\"]","","","def write_sources(folder, days=DAYS, broken=None):","    os.makedirs(folder, exist_ok=True)","    for region in (\"pyr\", \"pnr\"):","        text = F.csv_file(region, days)","        if broken and broken[0] == region:","            text = broken[1](text)","        name = \"202608_MONTHLY_AQHI_%s_SiteObs.csv\" % region.upper()","        with open(os.path.join(folder, name), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:","            f.write(text)","","","def tree(folder, skip=(\"runs.ndjson\", \"health.json\")):","    out = {}","    for dirpath, _, files in os.walk(folder):","        for n in files:","            if n in skip:","                continue","            p = os.path.join(dirpath, n)","            with open(p, \"rb\") as f:","                out[os.path.relpath(p, folder)] = f.read()","    return out","","","class Pipeline(unittest.TestCase):","    def setUp(self):","        self.tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"almanac-test-\")","        self.src = os.path.join(self.tmp, \"src\")","        self.data = os.path.join(self.tmp, \"data\")","        write_sources(self.src)","","    def tearDown(self):","        shutil.rmtree(self.tmp, ignore_errors=True)","","    def cli(self, *args):","        return R.main(list(args) + [\"--source-dir\", self.src, \"--data-dir\", self.data,","                                    \"--now\", \"2026-11-02T07:17:00Z\", \"--pause\", \"0\"])","","    def runs(self):","        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"runs.ndjson\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","            return [json.loads(l) for l in f]","","    def test_rerunning_a_day_gives_identical_output(self):","        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\"), 0)","        first = tree(self.data)","        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\"), 0)","        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\"), 0)","        second = tree(self.data)","        self.assertEqual(sorted(first), sorted(second))","        for k in first:","            self.assertEqual(first[k], second[k], k)","        self.assertIn(os.path.join(\"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), first)","        # the log grows: every run is recorded, including reruns","        self.assertEqual(len(self.runs()), 7)","","    def test_backfill_labels_and_partitions(self):","        self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\")","        runs = self.runs()","        self.assertEqual([r[\"kind\"] for r in runs], [\"backfill\"] * 3)","        self.assertEqual(len({r[\"batch_id\"] for r in runs}), 1)","        for d in DAYS:","            self.assertTrue(os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.data, \"validated\", \"2026-08\", d + \".csv\")))","            self.assertTrue(os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.data, \"raw\", \"2026-08\", d + \".pyr.csv\")))","        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","            s = json.load(f)","        kam = [c for c in s[\"cities\"] if c[\"city\"] == \"Kamloops\"][0]","        self.assertEqual(kam[\"high_hours\"], 12)  # 4 smoky hours a day x 3 days","        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"health.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","            h = json.load(f)","        self.assertEqual([c[\"kind\"] for c in h[\"calendar\"]], [\"backfill\"] * 3)","        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][0][\"checks\"], \"pppppps\")","","    def test_failed_day_is_logged_and_keeps_earlier_data(self):","        self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")","        before = tree(os.path.join(self.data, \"validated\"))","        # the source renames a city column: the contract must refuse the day","        write_sources(self.src, broken=(\"pnr\", lambda t: t.replace(\"IAKID\", \"IAKIX\")))","        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")","        self.assertEqual(code, 2)","        last = self.runs()[-1]","        self.assertEqual(last[\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertFalse(last[\"loaded\"])","        self.assertEqual(tree(os.path.join(self.data, \"validated\")), before)","        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"health.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","            h = json.load(f)","        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"runs\"], 2)","        # the refused rerun says the earlier load is still counted, and how much of it","        self.assertTrue(last[\"kept_earlier\"])","        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"kept\"], 24 * 7)","        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:","            s = json.load(f)","        self.assertEqual(sum(c[\"high_hours\"] for c in s[\"cities\"]), 4)","","    def test_missing_archive_is_a_red_run_not_a_crash(self):","        shutil.rmtree(self.src)","        os.makedirs(self.src)","        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")","        self.assertEqual(code, 2)","        last = self.runs()[-1]","        self.assertEqual(last[\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertTrue(any(\"No PYR file\" in n for n in last[\"notes\"]))","        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}","        # no file is a missing day, not a renamed column","        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")","        self.assertEqual([c[\"name\"] for c in last[\"checks\"]], [c[\"name\"] for c in F.CONTRACT[\"checks\"]])","","    def test_stalled_live_feed_fails_freshness_not_schema(self):","        # What the daily run sees when ECCC's hourly feed has stopped: no live file at all.","        shutil.rmtree(self.src)","        os.makedirs(self.src)","        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-11-01\")","        self.assertEqual(code, 2)","        last = self.runs()[-1]","        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")","        self.assertIn(\"stalled\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])","        for name in (\"schema\", \"types\", \"range\", \"uniqueness\", \"completeness\", \"volume\"):","            self.assertEqual(res[name][\"status\"], \"skip\", name)","        self.assertTrue(any(\"stalled\" in n for n in last[\"notes\"]))","","    def test_live_feed_six_to_eight_hours_old_warns(self):","        # an hourly file from 7 hours ago is found (within the lookback), but its newest hour is old","        for region in (\"pyr\", \"pnr\"):","            text = F.csv_file(region, [\"2026-11-01\"])","            name = \"2026110200_AQHI_%s_SiteObs.csv\" % region.upper()","            with open(os.path.join(self.src, name), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:","                f.write(text)","        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-11-01\"), 0)","        last = self.runs()[-1]","        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}","        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")","        self.assertEqual(last[\"source\"][0][\"type\"], \"hourly snapshot\")","","    def test_refuses_a_day_that_is_not_over(self):","        with self.assertRaises(SystemExit):","            self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-11-02\")","","","if __name__ == \"__main__\":","    unittest.main()"],"sha256":"c3d3e9a1e44be26a953c7737801b62fc0831ed0bb3f586d7ec92796d214fdeb3"},{"path":"projects/almanac/tests/freshness.test.js","lines":["// The page must say \"stale\" honestly. The clock is injected, so no waiting is needed.","var assert = require('assert');","var path = require('path');","var fs = require('fs');","var M = require('../model.js');","","var slo = { max_data_age_hours: 36, max_run_age_hours: 26 };","var H = 3600 * 1000;","var latestHour = '2026-11-01T23:00:00Z';","var lastRun = '2026-11-02T07:20:00Z';","var t0 = Date.parse(latestHour);","","// A normal morning after the daily run: fresh.","var f = M.freshness(t0 + 9 * H, latestHour, lastRun, slo);","assert.strictEqual(f.state, 'fresh');","assert.strictEqual(f.word, 'Fresh');","assert.deepStrictEqual(f.reasons, []);","","// Exactly at the limit is still fresh; one minute past is stale.","assert.strictEqual(M.freshness(t0 + 36 * H, latestHour, '2026-11-02T20:00:00Z', slo).state, 'fresh');","var late = M.freshness(t0 + 36 * H + 60000, latestHour, '2026-11-02T20:00:00Z', slo);","assert.strictEqual(late.state, 'stale');","assert.ok(/newest hour/.test(late.reasons[0]));","","// The latest run is older than its SLO, even though the data is recent enough: stale.","var noRun = M.freshness(Date.parse('2026-11-03T10:00:00Z'), '2026-11-02T23:00:00Z', '2026-11-02T07:20:00Z', slo);","assert.strictEqual(noRun.state, 'stale');","assert.strictEqual(noRun.reasons.length, 1);","assert.ok(/last run was/.test(noRun.reasons[0]), noRun.reasons[0]);","","// Both broken: both reasons are given.","var both = M.freshness(t0 + 5 * 24 * H, latestHour, lastRun, slo);","assert.strictEqual(both.state, 'stale');","assert.strictEqual(both.reasons.length, 2);","","// No data at all is stale, never fresh by default.","assert.strictEqual(M.freshness(t0, null, null, slo).state, 'stale');","","// Against the real aggregates: what a visitor sees soon after the last run, and a month later.","var health = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, '..', 'data', 'aggregates', 'health.json'), 'utf8'));","health.calendar = M.expandCalendar(health);","var finished = health.latest_run.finished_at;","var soon = M.freshness(Date.parse(finished) + H, health.latest_hour, finished, health.contract.slo);","var month = M.freshness(Date.parse(finished) + 30 * 24 * H, health.latest_hour, finished, health.contract.slo);","assert.strictEqual(month.state, 'stale');","assert.strictEqual(health.contract.slo.max_data_age_hours, 36);","// Days with no run are not invisible: the page adds them up to yesterday by its own clock.","var lastDay = Date.parse(health.calendar[health.calendar.length - 1].date + 'T00:00:00Z');","var D = 24 * H;","var ext = M.extendCalendar(health.calendar, lastDay + 4 * D + 12 * H); // three whole days later, no runs","var added = ext.slice(health.calendar.length);","assert.deepStrictEqual(added.map(function (d) { return d.date; }),","  [1, 2, 3].map(function (k) { return new Date(lastDay + k * D).toISOString().slice(0, 10); }));","assert.ok(added.every(function (d) { return d.status === 'none'; }));","assert.strictEqual(M.extendCalendar(health.calendar, lastDay + D + 8 * H).length, health.calendar.length);","console.log('freshness: ok (an hour after the last run the page says ' + soon.word + '; a month later it says ' + month.word + ')');"],"sha256":"d79ae968064b2c66c25d3eae387b285642f2ee314d18bd06fd9d9906778ec62a"}],"chunks":[{"id":"0:1","path":"projects/almanac/README.md","start":1,"end":36,"text":"# Almanac\n\nA small data pipeline meant to run every day on public Canadian open data. It answers one question, how many hours the air has been high-risk in seven western Canadian cities, and it publishes its own health next to the answer: every run, every check of its data contract, and how fresh the data is. The page is `projects/almanac/index.html`; this file keeps the full record and is not linked from the page.\n\n## What it’s for\n\nMost pictures of a data pipeline are diagrams. This one is a working pipeline that keeps a public record of itself, so a visitor can see whether to trust the number at the top: which days ran, which ones broke a promise about their data, whether anything was refused, and whether the whole thing has quietly stopped. If it stops, the page says “stale” and shows the missing days, rather than going on showing an old answer as if it were current.\n\n## The source and the question\n\n**Dataset.** Environment and Climate Change Canada (ECCC), Meteorological Service of Canada: Air Quality Health Index (AQHI) observations, from the MSC Datamart (`dd.weather.gc.ca`). Two products are used, both CSV with one column per AQHI location and one row per UTC hour:\n\n- the live hourly file, `…/{YYYYMMDD}/WXO-DD/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/realtime/csv/{YYYYMMDDHH}_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs.csv`, republished every hour and holding the last 168 hours;\n- monthly archives, `…/today/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/monthly/csv/{YYYYMM}_MONTHLY_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs.csv`, plus a corrected `…_BACKFILLED.csv` version published about three days after each month ends. The listing goes back to at least July 2025.\n\nRegions are `pyr` (British Columbia and Yukon) and `pnr` (Prairies and the North). A day's two regional files are about 25–30 KB each (hourly) or 100–140 KB (monthly).\n\n**Why this source.** It updates hourly, has a stable machine-readable path, has history for a backfill (the monthly archives), is free to reuse under a published licence, and it answers a question people in the West care about every summer: how much wildfire smoke did we breathe. I first tried the MSC GeoMet OGC API (`api.weather.gc.ca`, collection `aqhi-observations-realtime`); on 2 November 2026 it held only about three days per location, too little for a backfill, so the Datamart CSVs are used instead.\n\n**Licence and attribution.** Environment and Climate Change Canada Data Services End-use Licence (version 2.1.1, August 2026). It allows copying, adapting and publishing, provided the source is acknowledged with the attribution statement and, where possible, a link to the licence. The page says “Data Source: Environment and Climate Change Canada” and links the licence in its one paragraph. It must not suggest endorsement, and it does not use ECCC’s name as branding.\n\n**Cities.** Seven AQHI locations: Vancouver (Metro Vancouver – NW, `JBRIK`), Victoria (Victoria / Saanich, `JBOBQ`), Kelowna (Central Okanagan, `JAFUV`), Kamloops (`JAFNW`), Prince George (`JBLVS`), Calgary (`IAKID`) and Edmonton (`IACMP`). An AQHI location is a community value; Vancouver is represented by the north-west zone of Metro Vancouver only.\n\n**The question, exactly.** For each city, the number of UTC hours since the record began (4 August 2026) whose AQHI reading, rounded half up to a whole number as ECCC reports it, is 7 or more. ECCC’s categories: 1–3 low risk, 4–6 moderate, 7–10 high, 10+ very high. The CSV writes 10+ as 11, so “high-risk” here includes 10+. A reading counts when it is 6.5 or above.\n\n## The pipeline\n\n`pipeline/run.py`, Python 3.11 standard library only, so it runs the same locally and in GitHub Actions:\n\n```\npython -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date 2026-11-01\npython -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill 2026-08-04 2026-11-01\npython -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --aggregate-only\n```\n\nOptions: `--kind` (scheduled, manual, backfill, revision; defaults are inferred), `--source auto|hourly|monthly`, `--now` (inject the clock), `--data-dir`, `--source-dir` (read files from disk instead of the network, for tests and replays), `--pause` (seconds between requests, default 1)."},{"id":"0:27","path":"projects/almanac/README.md","start":27,"end":62,"text":"\n`pipeline/run.py`, Python 3.11 standard library only, so it runs the same locally and in GitHub Actions:\n\n```\npython -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date 2026-11-01\npython -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill 2026-08-04 2026-11-01\npython -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --aggregate-only\n```\n\nOptions: `--kind` (scheduled, manual, backfill, revision; defaults are inferred), `--source auto|hourly|monthly`, `--now` (inject the clock), `--data-dir`, `--source-dir` (read files from disk instead of the network, for tests and replays), `--pause` (seconds between requests, default 1).\n\n1. **Extract.** For each region, the live hourly file if the day is within the last 6 days, otherwise the corrected monthly archive if it exists, otherwise the first monthly archive. One request at a time, one-second pauses, three tries with back-off, a descriptive User-Agent, and each file fetched once per run.\n2. **Validate.** `pipeline/contract.py` applies `pipeline/contract.json`, the data contract written as data. Seven checks: schema (expected columns present), types (dates, hours 0–23, numeric or blank readings), range (1 to 11; odd values quarantined, more than 1% fails the day), uniqueness (one reading per city-hour; exact repeats warn, conflicting ones fail), completeness (all 24 hours in the file), volume (each city at least 18 of 24 hours, else a warning; under half of the 168 expected readings fails) and freshness (the live file’s newest hour at most 6 hours old, else a warning; not applicable to an archive). The day’s status is the worst check: green, amber or red.\n\n   When there is no source file at all, no check pretends to have looked at it. If the run wanted the live feed (the day is within 6 days) and found no hourly file in the last 8 hours (`hourly_lookback_hours`) and no monthly archive for the day, the freshness check fails with “the feed seems to have stalled” and the other six are marked “not run”. If it wanted an archive and none exists, the completeness check fails instead. Before a verification pass this case showed up as a schema failure with freshness skipped, which blamed the wrong thing; the stalled-feed and missing-archive tests now pin it down.\n3. **Load.** Only when the day is not red: `data/raw/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD.{pyr,pnr}.csv` (that day’s rows exactly as received), `data/validated/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD.csv` (one row per city-hour: date, hour, location, city, value, reported value, high-risk flag) and `data/quarantine/…` for readings set aside. A red day writes nothing to raw or validated, so earlier good data for that day is kept, still counted in the answer, and marked as kept on the calendar, in its tooltip and in the readings chart (a ring under the bar).\n4. **Aggregate.** `data/aggregates/summary.json` (the answer, per city and per day), `health.json` (calendar of runs, lineage counts, the SLO, known issues; the last 90 days keep a full entry with run id, times and each check’s result in words, and older days are packed into short tuples, `calendar_old`, that `model.js` unpacks) and `preview.js` (a tiny snapshot for the projects card). The page loads only these.\n5. **Log.** Every run, including a failed or crashed one, appends a record to `data/runs.ndjson`: run id, batch id, kind, day, start and finish, source URLs and bytes, rows in and out, quarantined count, every check’s result and detail, bytes written, notes and the commit.\n\n**Idempotent.** Partitions are written whole, sorted and with fixed line endings, and the summary has no timestamps. Rerunning a day on the same source gives byte-identical raw, validated and summary files; only the run log grows (by design: a rerun is a run) and `health.json`, which reports the log.\n\n**Schedule.** `pipeline/almanac.yml` is a GitHub Actions workflow: daily at 07:17 UTC (the previous UTC day is complete by then), manual dispatch with an optional day or backfill range, a concurrency group, a 15-minute timeout and only `contents: write`. It runs the Python contract tests first, processes yesterday, and on the 4th of each month reloads the previous month from ECCC’s corrected file as a “revision”. It commits only when something under `projects/almanac/data` changed; the run log changes on every run, so in practice every run is committed, which is what lets the page show it. If the contract failed, the data is still committed and then the job is marked failed. The owner’s token lacks the workflow scope, so the file is not in `.github/workflows`; the install line is at its top.\n\n**Budgets.** 90 days take about 2.2 MB on disk (raw 0.76 MB, validated 0.55 MB, run log 0.14 MB, aggregates 73 KB), so about 9 MB a year, under the 20 MB budget. The aggregates are 73 KB against a 200 KB budget. They used to grow by about 300–650 bytes a day and would have passed the budget after about 14 months; now days older than 90 are packed (about 45 bytes each), the daily maximum is stored as the reported whole number, and `tests/test_budget.py` builds two years of runs and asserts the total stays under 200 KB (it is about 150 KB). At roughly 45 KB a year, the summary should be split by year before the record reaches three years. The launch backfill downloaded 0.79 MB.\n\n## The page\n\nBack link, title, one paragraph; everything else is in the stage. The answer: a city chooser that doubles as a ranking, one big number, a sentence giving its denominator (hours that had a reading), a warning when a city’s coverage is under 90%, and a bar chart of high-risk hours per day that adds up to the big number, with a mark under days where the city had fewer than 18 readings. The health panel: a freshness clock and its rule; a tally of runs; a calendar with one square per day (status is carried by shape, like the moon-phase marks in a printed almanac: a full disc passed, a half disc warned, a struck ring was refused, a point means no run; a boxed mark ran on schedule, an unboxed one was backfilled; 22 px squares on desktop and 24 px on a phone, where the calendar scrolls sideways); the selected day’s contract results in words, each with a “what this promise means” line; a chart of readings loaded per day against the 168 expected and the 84 refusal line; a lineage strip from source to raw to contract to validated to aggregates, with live counts; and the known-issues log from `pipeline/known_issues.json`.\n\n**Look.** The stage is set as a two-colour almanac sheet: cream stock with a light paper grain, black ink, and one spot colour, wildfire-smoke orange (#d9662a), used only for high-risk hours (the bars, the rule under the headline number, the screen behind “high-risk”). Everything else, including pass, warning and refusal, is told by shape and words in black, so the only colour on the page means smoke. Type is Libre Caslon Text and Libre Caslon Display (SIL Open Font License, self-hosted in `fonts/` with `OFL.txt`, about 100 KB). The card preview prints the same marks into the calendar day by day while the orange bars rise.\n\n**Freshness, honestly.** Fresh means the newest hour is at most 36 hours old and the last run finished at most 26 hours ago (`contract.json`, `slo`). The page computes this from the visitor’s clock, not the pipeline’s. It also adds “no run” squares for every day after the last logged one up to yesterday, so a stopped pipeline shows its gap instead of hiding it. `?now=2026-11-05T12:00:00Z` sets the page’s clock for testing.\n\n**Preview.** On the projects card the run calendar fills in day by day while the high-risk bars draw and the total counts up, from `preview.js` (the last 91 days only, so the squares stay legible); no requests, and a full still frame when paused. Its caption counts the scheduled runs among those shown, so it will stop saying “all backfilled” once the schedule runs.\n\n**What the page claims about itself.** The calendar, contract results and counts come from the pipeline’s log; the freshness verdict and the “no run” squares are worked out by the page from the visitor’s clock; the known issues are written by hand. The page says so in those words. The tally’s sentence about which check causes most warnings is counted from the calendar, and only shown when one check causes most of them."},{"id":"0:53","path":"projects/almanac/README.md","start":53,"end":88,"text":"\nBack link, title, one paragraph; everything else is in the stage. The answer: a city chooser that doubles as a ranking, one big number, a sentence giving its denominator (hours that had a reading), a warning when a city’s coverage is under 90%, and a bar chart of high-risk hours per day that adds up to the big number, with a mark under days where the city had fewer than 18 readings. The health panel: a freshness clock and its rule; a tally of runs; a calendar with one square per day (status is carried by shape, like the moon-phase marks in a printed almanac: a full disc passed, a half disc warned, a struck ring was refused, a point means no run; a boxed mark ran on schedule, an unboxed one was backfilled; 22 px squares on desktop and 24 px on a phone, where the calendar scrolls sideways); the selected day’s contract results in words, each with a “what this promise means” line; a chart of readings loaded per day against the 168 expected and the 84 refusal line; a lineage strip from source to raw to contract to validated to aggregates, with live counts; and the known-issues log from `pipeline/known_issues.json`.\n\n**Look.** The stage is set as a two-colour almanac sheet: cream stock with a light paper grain, black ink, and one spot colour, wildfire-smoke orange (#d9662a), used only for high-risk hours (the bars, the rule under the headline number, the screen behind “high-risk”). Everything else, including pass, warning and refusal, is told by shape and words in black, so the only colour on the page means smoke. Type is Libre Caslon Text and Libre Caslon Display (SIL Open Font License, self-hosted in `fonts/` with `OFL.txt`, about 100 KB). The card preview prints the same marks into the calendar day by day while the orange bars rise.\n\n**Freshness, honestly.** Fresh means the newest hour is at most 36 hours old and the last run finished at most 26 hours ago (`contract.json`, `slo`). The page computes this from the visitor’s clock, not the pipeline’s. It also adds “no run” squares for every day after the last logged one up to yesterday, so a stopped pipeline shows its gap instead of hiding it. `?now=2026-11-05T12:00:00Z` sets the page’s clock for testing.\n\n**Preview.** On the projects card the run calendar fills in day by day while the high-risk bars draw and the total counts up, from `preview.js` (the last 91 days only, so the squares stay legible); no requests, and a full still frame when paused. Its caption counts the scheduled runs among those shown, so it will stop saying “all backfilled” once the schedule runs.\n\n**What the page claims about itself.** The calendar, contract results and counts come from the pipeline’s log; the freshness verdict and the “no run” squares are worked out by the page from the visitor’s clock; the known issues are written by hand. The page says so in those words. The tally’s sentence about which check causes most warnings is counted from the calendar, and only shown when one check causes most of them.\n\n**Not yet running on a schedule.** At launch all 90 days came from one backfill (batch `backfill-20261102T033929Z`); the workflow has not run in GitHub Actions yet, so the page will turn stale about a day after launch. That is the honest state, and it is the first known issue. The owner should move `almanac.yml` into `.github/workflows`, start it once by hand from the Actions tab, and only then describe the project as running every day.\n\n## How I know\n\n**What was checked, and how.**\n\n- `tests/test_contract.py`: each of the seven checks passes a clean crafted day and catches a crafted violation (renamed column, text in a reading, an hour of 25, out-of-range values below and above the 1% line, 10+ as 11, conflicting and exact duplicates, missing hours, a missing day, a quiet city, a mostly empty day, a stale feed, an unknown feed age, an archive source).\n- `tests/test_pipeline.py`: end to end on crafted files with `--source-dir`: rerunning a day and a backfill gives byte-identical partitions and summary; backfill runs are labelled and share a batch id; a red day is logged, exits 2 and leaves the earlier validated data untouched; a missing archive is a red completeness failure, not a crash; a stalled live feed (no hourly file) fails freshness, not schema, with the other checks not run; a live file 7 hours old warns; a refused rerun records that the earlier load is kept; a day that is not over is refused.\n- `tests/test_budget.py`: two years of runs, cycled from the real log and partitions, keep the aggregates under 200 KB, and packed old days unpack to the same entries as full ones.\n- `tests/recompute-headline.js`: an independent Node script recounts each city’s high-risk hours from the stored validated CSVs (and, separately, from the raw slices as ECCC wrote them), and checks both against `summary.json` and against the sum of the chart’s bars. All seven cities match (Kamloops 137, Kelowna 61, Calgary 17, Edmonton 11, Vancouver 9, Prince George 1, Victoria 0, from 14,240 stored readings).\n- `tests/freshness.test.js`: with an injected clock, fresh just inside the 36-hour limit, stale one minute past it, stale when only the run is too old, both reasons when both are, stale with no data; and the page adds “no run” days after the last logged one.\n- `tests/model.test.js`: calendar layout, unpacking of old days, each day’s colour is the worst of its checks, the kept-earlier wording, the counted cause of warnings, the headline equals its bars, the aggregates are under budget.\n- Run all with `node projects/almanac/tests/run-all.js`.\n- Real-data idempotency: I copied the data folder, reran 10 September 2026 against the live server, and diffed: only `runs.ndjson` and `health.json` changed.\n- I compared ECCC’s first and corrected September files for the BC and Yukon region: the corrected one filled 636 blank city-hours and changed 257 values. That is why the workflow reloads each month on the 4th, and why October is listed as a known issue.\n- In a browser: desktop and 375 px widths, the `?preview` card on projects.html, keyboard use of the calendar and charts, the stale state with an injected clock, and no console errors.\n\n**What is simplified.**\n\n- The record starts on 4 August 2026, because the launch backfill was capped at about 90 days. The counts are hours since then, not hours this year; July 2026 alone had 119 high-risk hours in Kamloops by ECCC’s corrected file.\n- One AQHI location stands for each city. Metro Vancouver’s other zones, for instance, can differ.\n- Readings are ECCC’s real-time values, which it says are not quality-controlled. Missing hours are not filled in, so a city with gaps (Kelowna most of all) has a count that is a floor.\n- Days are UTC days, not local days.\n- The volume threshold (18 of 24 hours per city) is a judgement: fewer readings can hide high-risk hours. With it, 36 of the 90 backfilled days are amber, 31 of them because Central Okanagan (Kelowna) or Kamloops went quiet. I did not loosen it to make the calendar greener.\n- The AQHI is a relative-risk index built from ozone, PM2.5 and NO2; this project counts its hours and makes no health claim beyond ECCC’s category names."},{"id":"0:79","path":"projects/almanac/README.md","start":79,"end":99,"text":"- In a browser: desktop and 375 px widths, the `?preview` card on projects.html, keyboard use of the calendar and charts, the stale state with an injected clock, and no console errors.\n\n**What is simplified.**\n\n- The record starts on 4 August 2026, because the launch backfill was capped at about 90 days. The counts are hours since then, not hours this year; July 2026 alone had 119 high-risk hours in Kamloops by ECCC’s corrected file.\n- One AQHI location stands for each city. Metro Vancouver’s other zones, for instance, can differ.\n- Readings are ECCC’s real-time values, which it says are not quality-controlled. Missing hours are not filled in, so a city with gaps (Kelowna most of all) has a count that is a floor.\n- Days are UTC days, not local days.\n- The volume threshold (18 of 24 hours per city) is a judgement: fewer readings can hide high-risk hours. With it, 36 of the 90 backfilled days are amber, 31 of them because Central Okanagan (Kelowna) or Kamloops went quiet. I did not loosen it to make the calendar greener.\n- The AQHI is a relative-risk index built from ozone, PM2.5 and NO2; this project counts its hours and makes no health claim beyond ECCC’s category names.\n\n**What would change the conclusion.** ECCC’s corrected monthly files can fill gaps and revise values, so October’s counts may move after the revision run. Extending the backfill to 1 January (one command; the archives are there) would turn “since 4 August” into “this year” and add July’s smoke. A change to the AQHI formula or to how the CSV encodes 10+ would be caught by the range check before it changed a count.\n\n**Local note.** On the machine that ran the backfill, the installed Python had no certificate store, so `run.py` was run with `SSL_CERT_FILE` pointing at Git for Windows’ CA bundle. GitHub’s Ubuntu runners do not need this.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Environment and Climate Change Canada, Meteorological Service of Canada. “Data and Products of the Air Quality Health Index (AQHI) observation and forecast.” MSC Open Data documentation. https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/msc-data/aqhi/readme_aqhi_en/\n- Environment and Climate Change Canada. “Environment and Climate Change Canada Data Services End-use Licence,” version 2.1.1, August 2026. https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/licence/readme_en/\n- MSC Datamart, AQHI observations, `https://dd.weather.gc.ca/today/air_quality/aqhi/` (hourly and monthly CSV), accessed 2 November 2026.\n- MSC GeoMet OGC API, collection `aqhi-observations-realtime`, `https://api.weather.gc.ca/collections/aqhi-observations-realtime`, examined 2 November 2026 and not used (about three days of history)."},{"id":"1:1","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":1,"end":36,"text":"\"\"\"Almanac pipeline: AQHI observations for seven western Canadian cities.\n\n    python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date 2026-11-01\n    python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill 2026-08-04 2026-11-01\n\nextract -> validate (contract.json) -> load (data/raw, data/validated) -> aggregate\n(data/aggregates) -> append a run record (data/runs.ndjson). Standard library only.\n\nRerunning a day on the same source gives byte-identical partitions and summary.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport csv\nimport io\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\nfrom datetime import date as Date, datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nsys.path.insert(0, HERE)  # python -I does not add the script's folder to the path\nimport contract as C  # noqa: E402\n\nVERSION = \"almanac-pipeline 1.0\"\nUSER_AGENT = \"almanac-pipeline/1.0 (+https://milbirguram.github.io/projects/almanac/)\"\nDEFAULT_DATA = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"data\"))\nVALIDATED_COLS = [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\", \"city\", \"aqhi\", \"aqhi_reported\", \"high_risk\"]\nQUARANTINE_COLS = [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\", \"city\", \"value\", \"reason\"]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- time\n\ndef utcnow():\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)"},{"id":"1:27","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":27,"end":62,"text":"USER_AGENT = \"almanac-pipeline/1.0 (+https://milbirguram.github.io/projects/almanac/)\"\nDEFAULT_DATA = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"data\"))\nVALIDATED_COLS = [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\", \"city\", \"aqhi\", \"aqhi_reported\", \"high_risk\"]\nQUARANTINE_COLS = [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\", \"city\", \"value\", \"reason\"]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- time\n\ndef utcnow():\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)\n\n\ndef iso(dt):\n    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef parse_iso(s):\n    s = s.strip().replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\")\n    dt = datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n    if dt.tzinfo is None:\n        dt = dt.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef days(start, end):\n    d = start\n    while d <= end:\n        yield d\n        d += timedelta(days=1)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- extract\n\nclass Fetcher:\n    \"\"\"One request at a time, a pause between requests, a few polite retries.\n    With source_dir set, files are read from disk by their URL's file name (tests, replays).\"\"\""},{"id":"1:53","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":53,"end":88,"text":"    while d <= end:\n        yield d\n        d += timedelta(days=1)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- extract\n\nclass Fetcher:\n    \"\"\"One request at a time, a pause between requests, a few polite retries.\n    With source_dir set, files are read from disk by their URL's file name (tests, replays).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, source_dir=None, pause=1.0):\n        self.source_dir = source_dir\n        self.pause = pause\n        self.cache = {}\n        self.last = 0.0\n        self.downloaded = 0\n        self.errors = {}\n\n    def get(self, url):\n        \"\"\"Return (bytes, fresh) or (None, False) when the file does not exist.\"\"\"\n        if url in self.cache:\n            return self.cache[url], False\n        if url in self.errors:  # do not hammer a server that just failed us\n            raise self.errors[url]\n        if self.source_dir:\n            path = os.path.join(self.source_dir, url.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1])\n            data = None\n            if os.path.exists(path):\n                with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n                    data = f.read()\n            self.cache[url] = data\n            return data, data is not None\n        data = None\n        for attempt in range(3):\n            wait = self.pause - (time.time() - self.last)"},{"id":"1:79","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":79,"end":114,"text":"            path = os.path.join(self.source_dir, url.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1])\n            data = None\n            if os.path.exists(path):\n                with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n                    data = f.read()\n            self.cache[url] = data\n            return data, data is not None\n        data = None\n        for attempt in range(3):\n            wait = self.pause - (time.time() - self.last)\n            if wait > 0:\n                time.sleep(wait)\n            self.last = time.time()\n            try:\n                req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT})\n                with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as resp:\n                    data = resp.read()\n                break\n            except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n                if e.code == 404:\n                    break\n                if attempt == 2:\n                    self.errors[url] = e\n                    raise\n            except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError) as e:\n                if attempt == 2:\n                    self.errors[url] = e\n                    raise\n            time.sleep(2 ** attempt * 2)\n        self.cache[url] = data\n        if data is not None:\n            self.downloaded += len(data)\n        return data, data is not None\n\n\ndef fill(template, **kw):"},{"id":"1:105","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":105,"end":140,"text":"                    self.errors[url] = e\n                    raise\n            time.sleep(2 ** attempt * 2)\n        self.cache[url] = data\n        if data is not None:\n            self.downloaded += len(data)\n        return data, data is not None\n\n\ndef fill(template, **kw):\n    out = template\n    for k, v in kw.items():\n        out = out.replace(\"{\" + k + \"}\", v)\n    return out\n\n\ndef hourly_snapshot(fetcher, contract, region, now, resolved):\n    \"\"\"The newest hourly file (it holds the last 168 hours). Tries back hourly_lookback_hours.\"\"\"\n    if region in resolved:  # already fetched in this run: reuse it, and do not count it twice\n        got = resolved[region]\n        return None if got is None else (got[0], got[1], got[2], False)\n    top = now.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)\n    for back in range(0, lookback_hours(contract) + 1):\n        t = top - timedelta(hours=back)\n        url = fill(contract[\"source\"][\"hourly_url\"], yyyymmdd=t.strftime(\"%Y%m%d\"),\n                   yyyymmddhh=t.strftime(\"%Y%m%d%H\"), region=region, REGION=region.upper())\n        data, fresh = fetcher.get(url)\n        if data is not None:\n            resolved[region] = (data, url, \"hourly snapshot\", fresh)\n            return resolved[region]\n    resolved[region] = None\n    return None\n\n\ndef lookback_hours(contract):\n    return int(contract[\"source\"].get(\"hourly_lookback_hours\", 8))"},{"id":"1:131","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":131,"end":166,"text":"        data, fresh = fetcher.get(url)\n        if data is not None:\n            resolved[region] = (data, url, \"hourly snapshot\", fresh)\n            return resolved[region]\n    resolved[region] = None\n    return None\n\n\ndef lookback_hours(contract):\n    return int(contract[\"source\"].get(\"hourly_lookback_hours\", 8))\n\n\ndef expects_live(contract, day, now, mode):\n    \"\"\"Whether this run should read the live hourly feed for `day`.\"\"\"\n    recent = (now.date() - day).days <= contract[\"source\"][\"hourly_window_days\"]\n    return mode == \"hourly\" or (mode == \"auto\" and recent)\n\n\ndef monthly_archive(fetcher, contract, region, day, want_revised=True):\n    for suffix, label in ((\"_BACKFILLED\", \"revised monthly archive\"), (\"\", \"monthly archive\")):\n        if suffix and not want_revised:\n            continue\n        url = fill(contract[\"source\"][\"monthly_url\"], yyyymm=day.strftime(\"%Y%m\"),\n                   region=region, REGION=region.upper(), suffix=suffix)\n        data, fresh = fetcher.get(url)\n        if data is not None:\n            return data, url, label, fresh\n    return None\n\n\ndef choose_source(fetcher, contract, region, day, now, mode, resolved):\n    \"\"\"auto: the live hourly file if it still covers the day, otherwise the monthly archive.\"\"\"\n    if expects_live(contract, day, now, mode):\n        got = hourly_snapshot(fetcher, contract, region, now, resolved)\n        if got is not None or mode == \"hourly\":\n            return got"},{"id":"1:157","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":157,"end":192,"text":"            return data, url, label, fresh\n    return None\n\n\ndef choose_source(fetcher, contract, region, day, now, mode, resolved):\n    \"\"\"auto: the live hourly file if it still covers the day, otherwise the monthly archive.\"\"\"\n    if expects_live(contract, day, now, mode):\n        got = hourly_snapshot(fetcher, contract, region, now, resolved)\n        if got is not None or mode == \"hourly\":\n            return got\n    return monthly_archive(fetcher, contract, region, day)\n\n\ndef parse_source(data, date_str, date_col):\n    text = data.decode(\"utf-8-sig\").replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").replace(\"\\r\", \"\\n\")\n    lines = [l for l in text.split(\"\\n\") if l.strip() != \"\"]\n    if not lines:\n        return {\"header\": [], \"rows\": [], \"newest\": None, \"raw_lines\": []}\n    header = next(csv.reader([lines[0]]))\n    header = [h.strip() for h in header]\n    di = header.index(date_col) if date_col in header else 0\n    hi = header.index(\"Hour (UTC)\") if \"Hour (UTC)\" in header else 1\n    rows, raw_lines, newest = [], [lines[0]], None\n    for line in lines[1:]:\n        row = next(csv.reader([line]))\n        d = row[di].strip() if di < len(row) else \"\"\n        try:\n            stamp = \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (d, int(row[hi]))\n            datetime.strptime(stamp, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n            if newest is None or stamp > newest:\n                newest = stamp\n        except (ValueError, IndexError):\n            pass\n        if d == date_str:\n            rows.append(row)\n            raw_lines.append(line)"},{"id":"1:183","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":183,"end":218,"text":"        try:\n            stamp = \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (d, int(row[hi]))\n            datetime.strptime(stamp, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n            if newest is None or stamp > newest:\n                newest = stamp\n        except (ValueError, IndexError):\n            pass\n        if d == date_str:\n            rows.append(row)\n            raw_lines.append(line)\n    return {\"header\": header, \"rows\": rows, \"newest\": newest, \"raw_lines\": raw_lines}\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- load\n\ndef write_text(path, text):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = path + \".tmp\"\n    with open(tmp, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        f.write(text)\n    os.replace(tmp, path)\n    return len(text.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef csv_text(cols, rows):\n    buf = io.StringIO()\n    w = csv.writer(buf, lineterminator=\"\\n\")\n    w.writerow(cols)\n    for r in rows:\n        w.writerow([r[c] for c in cols])\n    return buf.getvalue()\n\n\ndef partition(data_dir, layer, day, suffix):\n    return os.path.join(data_dir, layer, day.strftime(\"%Y-%m\"), day.isoformat() + suffix)\n"},{"id":"1:209","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":209,"end":244,"text":"    w = csv.writer(buf, lineterminator=\"\\n\")\n    w.writerow(cols)\n    for r in rows:\n        w.writerow([r[c] for c in cols])\n    return buf.getvalue()\n\n\ndef partition(data_dir, layer, day, suffix):\n    return os.path.join(data_dir, layer, day.strftime(\"%Y-%m\"), day.isoformat() + suffix)\n\n\ndef process_day(day, ctx):\n    contract, fetcher, data_dir = ctx[\"contract\"], ctx[\"fetcher\"], ctx[\"data_dir\"]\n    now = ctx[\"now\"]()\n    started = now\n    ds = day.isoformat()\n    record = {\n        \"run_id\": \"%s-%s\" % (started.strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\"), ds),\n        \"batch_id\": ctx[\"batch_id\"], \"kind\": ctx[\"kind\"], \"date\": ds,\n        \"started_at\": iso(started), \"finished_at\": None, \"status\": \"fail\", \"loaded\": False,\n        \"source\": [], \"rows_in\": 0, \"rows_out\": 0, \"quarantined\": 0, \"bytes_written\": 0,\n        \"checks\": [], \"notes\": [], \"pipeline\": VERSION, \"commit\": (os.environ.get(\"GITHUB_SHA\") or \"\")[:7] or None,\n    }\n    try:\n        regions = sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in contract[\"locations\"]})\n        sources, raws = {}, {}\n        for region in regions:\n            got = choose_source(fetcher, contract, region, day, now, ctx[\"source_mode\"], ctx[\"resolved\"])\n            live_wanted = expects_live(contract, day, now, ctx[\"source_mode\"])\n            if got is None:\n                if live_wanted:\n                    record[\"notes\"].append(\"No live %s file in the last %d hours, and no monthly archive covers this day yet: \"\n                                           \"the feed seems to have stalled.\" % (region.upper(), lookback_hours(contract)))\n                else:\n                    record[\"notes\"].append(\"No %s file covers this day; the source may not offer it any more.\" % region.upper())\n                sources[region] = {\"absent\": \"live\" if live_wanted else \"archive\", \"lookback_hours\": lookback_hours(contract)}"},{"id":"1:235","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":235,"end":270,"text":"        for region in regions:\n            got = choose_source(fetcher, contract, region, day, now, ctx[\"source_mode\"], ctx[\"resolved\"])\n            live_wanted = expects_live(contract, day, now, ctx[\"source_mode\"])\n            if got is None:\n                if live_wanted:\n                    record[\"notes\"].append(\"No live %s file in the last %d hours, and no monthly archive covers this day yet: \"\n                                           \"the feed seems to have stalled.\" % (region.upper(), lookback_hours(contract)))\n                else:\n                    record[\"notes\"].append(\"No %s file covers this day; the source may not offer it any more.\" % region.upper())\n                sources[region] = {\"absent\": \"live\" if live_wanted else \"archive\", \"lookback_hours\": lookback_hours(contract)}\n                continue\n            if live_wanted and got[2] != \"hourly snapshot\":\n                record[\"notes\"].append(\"No live %s file in the last %d hours, so the day was read from the %s.\"\n                                       % (region.upper(), lookback_hours(contract), got[2]))\n            data, url, label, fresh = got\n            parsed = parse_source(data, ds, contract[\"columns\"][\"date\"])\n            sources[region] = parsed\n            raws[region] = parsed[\"raw_lines\"]\n            record[\"source\"].append({\"region\": region, \"url\": url, \"type\": label, \"bytes\": len(data), \"downloaded\": fresh})\n        live = bool(record[\"source\"]) and all(s[\"type\"] == \"hourly snapshot\" for s in record[\"source\"])\n        locs = contract[\"locations\"]\n        for region, s in sources.items():\n            idx = {n: i for i, n in enumerate(s.get(\"header\", []))}\n            for row in s.get(\"rows\", []):\n                for l in locs:\n                    if l[\"region\"] == region and l[\"id\"] in idx and idx[l[\"id\"]] < len(row) and row[idx[l[\"id\"]]].strip():\n                        record[\"rows_in\"] += 1\n        checks, rows, quarantined = C.validate(contract, ds, sources, now=now, live=live)\n        record[\"checks\"] = checks\n        record[\"status\"] = C.worst(c[\"status\"] for c in checks)\n        record[\"quarantined\"] = len(quarantined)\n        qpath = partition(data_dir, \"quarantine\", day, \".csv\")\n        if record[\"status\"] != \"fail\":\n            written = 0\n            for region in regions:\n                if region in raws:"},{"id":"1:261","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":261,"end":296,"text":"                        record[\"rows_in\"] += 1\n        checks, rows, quarantined = C.validate(contract, ds, sources, now=now, live=live)\n        record[\"checks\"] = checks\n        record[\"status\"] = C.worst(c[\"status\"] for c in checks)\n        record[\"quarantined\"] = len(quarantined)\n        qpath = partition(data_dir, \"quarantine\", day, \".csv\")\n        if record[\"status\"] != \"fail\":\n            written = 0\n            for region in regions:\n                if region in raws:\n                    written += write_text(partition(data_dir, \"raw\", day, \".\" + region + \".csv\"), \"\\n\".join(raws[region]) + \"\\n\")\n            written += write_text(partition(data_dir, \"validated\", day, \".csv\"), csv_text(VALIDATED_COLS, rows))\n            if quarantined:\n                written += write_text(qpath, csv_text(QUARANTINE_COLS, quarantined))\n            elif os.path.exists(qpath):\n                os.remove(qpath)\n            record[\"rows_out\"] = len(rows)\n            record[\"bytes_written\"] = written\n            record[\"loaded\"] = True\n        else:\n            kept = os.path.exists(partition(data_dir, \"validated\", day, \".csv\"))\n            record[\"kept_earlier\"] = kept\n            record[\"notes\"].append(\"The contract failed, so nothing was loaded for this day.\"\n                                   + (\" The day's earlier load is kept and still counted.\" if kept else \"\"))\n            if quarantined:\n                record[\"bytes_written\"] = write_text(qpath, csv_text(QUARANTINE_COLS, quarantined))\n    except Exception as e:  # a crash is still a run, and the log should say so\n        record[\"status\"] = \"fail\"\n        record[\"notes\"].append(\"The run stopped with an error: %s: %s\" % (type(e).__name__, e))\n        names = {c[\"name\"] for c in record[\"checks\"]}\n        for c in contract[\"checks\"]:\n            if c[\"name\"] not in names:\n                record[\"checks\"].append({\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"status\": \"skip\", \"detail\": \"Not run, because the run stopped early.\"})\n    record[\"finished_at\"] = iso(ctx[\"now\"]())\n    append_run(data_dir, record)\n    return record"},{"id":"1:287","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":287,"end":322,"text":"    except Exception as e:  # a crash is still a run, and the log should say so\n        record[\"status\"] = \"fail\"\n        record[\"notes\"].append(\"The run stopped with an error: %s: %s\" % (type(e).__name__, e))\n        names = {c[\"name\"] for c in record[\"checks\"]}\n        for c in contract[\"checks\"]:\n            if c[\"name\"] not in names:\n                record[\"checks\"].append({\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"status\": \"skip\", \"detail\": \"Not run, because the run stopped early.\"})\n    record[\"finished_at\"] = iso(ctx[\"now\"]())\n    append_run(data_dir, record)\n    return record\n\n\ndef append_run(data_dir, record):\n    path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"runs.ndjson\")\n    os.makedirs(data_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef read_runs(data_dir):\n    path = os.path.join(data_dir, \"runs.ndjson\")\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return []\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return [json.loads(l) for l in f if l.strip()]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- aggregate\n\ndef dumps(obj):\n    return json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n\n\ndef walk(root, suffix):\n    out = []\n    if not os.path.isdir(root):"},{"id":"1:313","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":313,"end":348,"text":"\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- aggregate\n\ndef dumps(obj):\n    return json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n\n\ndef walk(root, suffix):\n    out = []\n    if not os.path.isdir(root):\n        return out\n    for dirpath, _, files in os.walk(root):\n        for name in files:\n            if name.endswith(suffix):\n                out.append(os.path.join(dirpath, name))\n    return sorted(out)\n\n\nPREVIEW_DAYS = 91\nOLD_FIELDS = [\"status\", \"kind\", \"kinds\", \"runs\", \"rows_in\", \"rows_out\", \"q\", \"loaded\", \"checks\", \"src\", \"kept\"]\nSTATUS_CODE = {\"pass\": \"p\", \"warn\": \"w\", \"fail\": \"f\", \"none\": \"n\"}\nKIND_CODE = {\"scheduled\": \"s\", \"manual\": \"m\", \"backfill\": \"b\", \"revision\": \"r\"}\nSRC_CODE = {\"hourly snapshot\": \"H\", \"monthly archive\": \"M\", \"revised monthly archive\": \"R\"}\n\n\ndef _inverse(d):\n    return {v: k for k, v in d.items()}\n\n\ndef pack_day(item):\n    \"\"\"A calendar entry as a short tuple in OLD_FIELDS order (a day with no run is [\"n\"]).\"\"\"\n    if item[\"status\"] == \"none\":\n        return [\"n\"]\n    return [STATUS_CODE[item[\"status\"]], KIND_CODE[item[\"kind\"]], \"\".join(KIND_CODE[k] for k in item[\"kinds\"]),\n            item[\"runs\"], item[\"rows_in\"], item[\"rows_out\"], item[\"q\"], 1 if item[\"loaded\"] else 0, item[\"checks\"],\n            \"\".join(SRC_CODE.get(x, \"?\") for x in item[\"src\"].split(\",\") if x), item.get(\"kept\", 0)]"},{"id":"1:339","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":339,"end":374,"text":"    return {v: k for k, v in d.items()}\n\n\ndef pack_day(item):\n    \"\"\"A calendar entry as a short tuple in OLD_FIELDS order (a day with no run is [\"n\"]).\"\"\"\n    if item[\"status\"] == \"none\":\n        return [\"n\"]\n    return [STATUS_CODE[item[\"status\"]], KIND_CODE[item[\"kind\"]], \"\".join(KIND_CODE[k] for k in item[\"kinds\"]),\n            item[\"runs\"], item[\"rows_in\"], item[\"rows_out\"], item[\"q\"], 1 if item[\"loaded\"] else 0, item[\"checks\"],\n            \"\".join(SRC_CODE.get(x, \"?\") for x in item[\"src\"].split(\",\") if x), item.get(\"kept\", 0)]\n\n\ndef calendar_items(health):\n    \"\"\"Every calendar day as a dict, old packed days first (mirrors expandCalendar in model.js).\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    old = health.get(\"calendar_old\") or {\"days\": []}\n    if old[\"days\"]:\n        first = Date.fromisoformat(old[\"first\"])\n        st, kd, sr = _inverse(STATUS_CODE), _inverse(KIND_CODE), _inverse(SRC_CODE)\n        for i, t in enumerate(old[\"days\"]):\n            ds = (first + timedelta(days=i)).isoformat()\n            if t[0] == \"n\":\n                out.append({\"date\": ds, \"status\": \"none\"})\n                continue\n            item = dict(zip(old[\"fields\"], t))\n            item.update({\"date\": ds, \"status\": st[t[0]], \"kind\": kd[item[\"kind\"]], \"kinds\": [kd[c] for c in item[\"kinds\"]],\n                         \"loaded\": bool(item[\"loaded\"]), \"src\": \",\".join(sorted(sr.get(c, c) for c in item[\"src\"]))})\n            if not item[\"kept\"]:\n                del item[\"kept\"]\n            out.append(item)\n    return out + list(health.get(\"calendar\", []))\n\n\ndef build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known_issues):\n    locs = contract[\"locations\"]\n    thr = contract[\"high_risk_threshold\"]"},{"id":"1:365","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":365,"end":400,"text":"                         \"loaded\": bool(item[\"loaded\"]), \"src\": \",\".join(sorted(sr.get(c, c) for c in item[\"src\"]))})\n            if not item[\"kept\"]:\n                del item[\"kept\"]\n            out.append(item)\n    return out + list(health.get(\"calendar\", []))\n\n\ndef build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known_issues):\n    locs = contract[\"locations\"]\n    thr = contract[\"high_risk_threshold\"]\n    vfiles = walk(os.path.join(data_dir, \"validated\"), \".csv\")\n    per = {}  # date -> lid -> [hi, max, n, maxlabel, maxhour]\n    latest_hour = None\n    vrows = 0\n    for path in vfiles:\n        ds = os.path.basename(path)[:10]\n        day = per.setdefault(ds, {})\n        with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n            for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n                vrows += 1\n                s = day.setdefault(r[\"location_id\"], [0, 0.0, 0, \"\", -1])\n                x = float(r[\"aqhi\"])\n                s[0] += 1 if C.reported(x) >= thr else 0\n                if x > s[1]:\n                    s[1], s[3], s[4] = x, r[\"aqhi_reported\"], int(r[\"hour_utc\"])\n                s[2] += 1\n                stamp = \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (ds, int(r[\"hour_utc\"]))\n                if latest_hour is None or stamp > latest_hour:\n                    latest_hour = stamp\n    runs = read_runs(data_dir)\n    run_dates = sorted({r[\"date\"] for r in runs})\n    all_dates = sorted(set(per) | set(run_dates))\n    if not all_dates:\n        return None\n    start = Date.fromisoformat(min(per) if per else all_dates[0])\n    end = Date.fromisoformat(all_dates[-1])"},{"id":"1:391","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":391,"end":426,"text":"                stamp = \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (ds, int(r[\"hour_utc\"]))\n                if latest_hour is None or stamp > latest_hour:\n                    latest_hour = stamp\n    runs = read_runs(data_dir)\n    run_dates = sorted({r[\"date\"] for r in runs})\n    all_dates = sorted(set(per) | set(run_dates))\n    if not all_dates:\n        return None\n    start = Date.fromisoformat(min(per) if per else all_dates[0])\n    end = Date.fromisoformat(all_dates[-1])\n    dates = [d.isoformat() for d in days(start, end)]\n\n    # ---- summary: the answer to the question\n    cities, series = [], {}\n    for l in locs:\n        hi, mx, n = [], [], []\n        tot_hi = tot_n = loaded_days = 0\n        peak, peak_label, peak_at, worst_day, worst_hi = 0.0, \"\", None, None, 0\n        for ds in dates:\n            s = per.get(ds, {}).get(l[\"id\"]) if ds in per else None\n            if ds not in per:\n                hi.append(None); mx.append(None); n.append(None)\n                continue\n            loaded_days += 1\n            if s is None:\n                hi.append(0); mx.append(None); n.append(0)\n                continue\n            hi.append(s[0]); mx.append(C.reported(s[1])); n.append(s[2])  # max as reported: 11 = 10+\n            tot_hi += s[0]; tot_n += s[2]\n            if s[1] > peak:\n                peak, peak_label, peak_at = s[1], s[3], \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (ds, s[4])\n            if s[0] > worst_hi:\n                worst_hi, worst_day = s[0], ds\n        series[l[\"id\"]] = {\"hi\": hi, \"max\": mx, \"n\": n}\n        cities.append({\"id\": l[\"id\"], \"city\": l[\"city\"], \"zone\": l[\"zone\"], \"high_hours\": tot_hi,\n                       \"hours_with_reading\": tot_n, \"hours_possible\": loaded_days * 24,"},{"id":"1:417","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":417,"end":452,"text":"                continue\n            hi.append(s[0]); mx.append(C.reported(s[1])); n.append(s[2])  # max as reported: 11 = 10+\n            tot_hi += s[0]; tot_n += s[2]\n            if s[1] > peak:\n                peak, peak_label, peak_at = s[1], s[3], \"%sT%02d:00:00Z\" % (ds, s[4])\n            if s[0] > worst_hi:\n                worst_hi, worst_day = s[0], ds\n        series[l[\"id\"]] = {\"hi\": hi, \"max\": mx, \"n\": n}\n        cities.append({\"id\": l[\"id\"], \"city\": l[\"city\"], \"zone\": l[\"zone\"], \"high_hours\": tot_hi,\n                       \"hours_with_reading\": tot_n, \"hours_possible\": loaded_days * 24,\n                       \"peak\": round(peak, 2), \"peak_label\": peak_label, \"peak_at\": peak_at,\n                       \"worst_day\": worst_day, \"worst_day_hours\": worst_hi})\n    loaded_dates = sorted(per)\n    summary = {\n        \"question\": \"How many hours has the air been high-risk (AQHI 7 or more) in western Canadian cities?\",\n        \"threshold\": thr, \"first_date\": dates[0], \"last_date\": dates[-1],\n        \"first_loaded\": loaded_dates[0] if loaded_dates else None,\n        \"last_loaded\": loaded_dates[-1] if loaded_dates else None,\n        \"days_loaded\": len(loaded_dates), \"latest_hour\": latest_hour,\n        \"dates\": dates, \"cities\": cities, \"series\": series,\n        \"attribution\": contract[\"source\"][\"attribution\"],\n    }\n\n    # ---- health: the pipeline's account of itself\n    # The most recent `detail_days` keep a full entry each (ids, times, every check's words).\n    # Older days are packed into short tuples (see OLD_FIELDS) so the file stays inside its\n    # budget however long the pipeline runs; model.js and calendar_items() unpack them.\n    by_date = {}\n    for r in runs:\n        e = by_date.setdefault(r[\"date\"], {\"runs\": 0, \"kinds\": []})\n        e[\"runs\"] += 1\n        if r[\"kind\"] not in e[\"kinds\"]:\n            e[\"kinds\"].append(r[\"kind\"])\n        e[\"last\"] = r\n    detail_from = (end - timedelta(days=contract[\"budgets\"][\"detail_days\"] - 1)).isoformat()\n    names = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]"},{"id":"1:443","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":443,"end":478,"text":"    # budget however long the pipeline runs; model.js and calendar_items() unpack them.\n    by_date = {}\n    for r in runs:\n        e = by_date.setdefault(r[\"date\"], {\"runs\": 0, \"kinds\": []})\n        e[\"runs\"] += 1\n        if r[\"kind\"] not in e[\"kinds\"]:\n            e[\"kinds\"].append(r[\"kind\"])\n        e[\"last\"] = r\n    detail_from = (end - timedelta(days=contract[\"budgets\"][\"detail_days\"] - 1)).isoformat()\n    names = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]\n    status_char = {\"pass\": \"p\", \"warn\": \"w\", \"fail\": \"f\", \"skip\": \"s\"}\n    cal, old = [], []\n    for ds in dates:\n        e = by_date.get(ds)\n        if not e:\n            item = {\"date\": ds, \"status\": \"none\"}\n        else:\n            r = e[\"last\"]\n            res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in r[\"checks\"]}\n            item = {\n                \"date\": ds, \"status\": r[\"status\"], \"kind\": r[\"kind\"], \"runs\": e[\"runs\"], \"kinds\": e[\"kinds\"],\n                \"rows_in\": r[\"rows_in\"], \"rows_out\": r[\"rows_out\"], \"q\": r[\"quarantined\"],\n                \"loaded\": r[\"loaded\"], \"src\": \",\".join(sorted({s[\"type\"] for s in r[\"source\"]})),\n                \"checks\": \"\".join(status_char[res[n][\"status\"]] if n in res else \"s\" for n in names),\n            }\n            if not r[\"loaded\"] and ds in per:\n                # refused, but an earlier load of this day is still in data/validated and counted\n                item[\"kept\"] = sum(v[2] for v in per[ds].values())\n        if ds < detail_from:\n            old.append(pack_day(item))\n            continue\n        if e:\n            r = e[\"last\"]\n            res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in r[\"checks\"]}\n            item.update({\"run_id\": r[\"run_id\"], \"started\": r[\"started_at\"], \"finished\": r[\"finished_at\"],\n                         \"bytes\": r[\"bytes_written\"],"},{"id":"1:469","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":469,"end":504,"text":"                # refused, but an earlier load of this day is still in data/validated and counted\n                item[\"kept\"] = sum(v[2] for v in per[ds].values())\n        if ds < detail_from:\n            old.append(pack_day(item))\n            continue\n        if e:\n            r = e[\"last\"]\n            res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in r[\"checks\"]}\n            item.update({\"run_id\": r[\"run_id\"], \"started\": r[\"started_at\"], \"finished\": r[\"finished_at\"],\n                         \"bytes\": r[\"bytes_written\"],\n                         \"details\": [res[n][\"detail\"] if n in res else \"\" for n in names]})\n            if r[\"notes\"]:\n                item[\"notes\"] = r[\"notes\"]\n        cal.append(item)\n    latest = runs[-1] if runs else None\n    totals = {\"runs\": len(runs), \"kinds\": {}, \"statuses\": {}}\n    for r in runs:\n        totals[\"kinds\"][r[\"kind\"]] = totals[\"kinds\"].get(r[\"kind\"], 0) + 1\n        totals[\"statuses\"][r[\"status\"]] = totals[\"statuses\"].get(r[\"status\"], 0) + 1\n    raw_files = walk(os.path.join(data_dir, \"raw\"), \".csv\")\n    q_files = walk(os.path.join(data_dir, \"quarantine\"), \".csv\")\n    q_rows = 0\n    for p in q_files:\n        with open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            q_rows += max(0, sum(1 for _ in f) - 1)\n    src_bytes = sum(s[\"bytes\"] for r in runs for s in r[\"source\"] if s.get(\"downloaded\"))\n    health = {\n        \"contract\": {\"name\": contract[\"name\"], \"version\": contract[\"version\"],\n                     \"checks\": [{\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"title\": c[\"title\"], \"plain\": c[\"plain\"]} for c in contract[\"checks\"]],\n                     \"slo\": contract[\"slo\"]},\n        \"source\": {k: contract[\"source\"][k] for k in (\"publisher\", \"attribution\", \"licence\", \"licence_url\", \"docs_url\")},\n        \"latest_hour\": latest_hour,\n        \"latest_run\": None if latest is None else {k: latest[k] for k in (\n            \"run_id\", \"kind\", \"date\", \"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"status\", \"rows_in\", \"rows_out\", \"quarantined\", \"notes\")},\n        \"calendar_old\": {\"first\": dates[0], \"fields\": OLD_FIELDS, \"days\": old},\n        \"calendar\": cal, \"check_names\": names, \"totals\": totals,"},{"id":"1:495","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":495,"end":530,"text":"    health = {\n        \"contract\": {\"name\": contract[\"name\"], \"version\": contract[\"version\"],\n                     \"checks\": [{\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"title\": c[\"title\"], \"plain\": c[\"plain\"]} for c in contract[\"checks\"]],\n                     \"slo\": contract[\"slo\"]},\n        \"source\": {k: contract[\"source\"][k] for k in (\"publisher\", \"attribution\", \"licence\", \"licence_url\", \"docs_url\")},\n        \"latest_hour\": latest_hour,\n        \"latest_run\": None if latest is None else {k: latest[k] for k in (\n            \"run_id\", \"kind\", \"date\", \"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"status\", \"rows_in\", \"rows_out\", \"quarantined\", \"notes\")},\n        \"calendar_old\": {\"first\": dates[0], \"fields\": OLD_FIELDS, \"days\": old},\n        \"calendar\": cal, \"check_names\": names, \"totals\": totals,\n        \"lineage\": {\n            \"source\": {\"downloaded_bytes\": src_bytes, \"files\": len({s[\"url\"] for r in runs for s in r[\"source\"]})},\n            \"raw\": {\"files\": len(raw_files), \"bytes\": sum(os.path.getsize(p) for p in raw_files)},\n            \"validated\": {\"files\": len(vfiles), \"rows\": vrows, \"bytes\": sum(os.path.getsize(p) for p in vfiles)},\n            \"quarantine\": {\"files\": len(q_files), \"rows\": q_rows},\n            \"runs_log\": {\"records\": len(runs), \"bytes\": os.path.getsize(os.path.join(data_dir, \"runs.ndjson\")) if runs else 0},\n            \"aggregates\": {\"bytes\": 0, \"budget\": contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]},\n        },\n        \"known_issues\": known_issues,\n    }\n\n    # ---- preview: a tiny precomputed snapshot for the projects card (no fetch in preview)\n    # Only the last PREVIEW_DAYS: the card has room for about thirteen weeks of squares.\n    full_cal = calendar_items({\"calendar_old\": {\"first\": dates[0], \"fields\": OLD_FIELDS, \"days\": old}, \"calendar\": cal})\n    k0 = max(0, len(dates) - PREVIEW_DAYS)\n    win = {l[\"id\"]: sum(h or 0 for h in series[l[\"id\"]][\"hi\"][k0:]) for l in locs}\n    top = max(locs, key=lambda l: (win[l[\"id\"]], -locs.index(l)))\n    letter = {\"pass\": \"g\", \"warn\": \"a\", \"fail\": \"r\", \"none\": \"n\"}\n    preview = {\n        \"city\": top[\"city\"], \"total\": win[top[\"id\"]], \"first\": dates[k0], \"last\": dates[-1],\n        \"cal\": \"\".join(letter.get(c[\"status\"], \"n\") for c in full_cal[k0:]),\n        \"backfill\": \"\".join(\"s\" if \"scheduled\" in c.get(\"kinds\", []) else \"b\" for c in full_cal[k0:]),\n        \"hi\": [h if h is not None else 0 for h in series[top[\"id\"]][\"hi\"][k0:]],\n    }\n    preview_text = \"window.ALMANAC_PREVIEW=\" + dumps(preview) + \";\\n\"\n    summary_text = dumps(summary) + \"\\n\""},{"id":"1:521","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":521,"end":556,"text":"    top = max(locs, key=lambda l: (win[l[\"id\"]], -locs.index(l)))\n    letter = {\"pass\": \"g\", \"warn\": \"a\", \"fail\": \"r\", \"none\": \"n\"}\n    preview = {\n        \"city\": top[\"city\"], \"total\": win[top[\"id\"]], \"first\": dates[k0], \"last\": dates[-1],\n        \"cal\": \"\".join(letter.get(c[\"status\"], \"n\") for c in full_cal[k0:]),\n        \"backfill\": \"\".join(\"s\" if \"scheduled\" in c.get(\"kinds\", []) else \"b\" for c in full_cal[k0:]),\n        \"hi\": [h if h is not None else 0 for h in series[top[\"id\"]][\"hi\"][k0:]],\n    }\n    preview_text = \"window.ALMANAC_PREVIEW=\" + dumps(preview) + \";\\n\"\n    summary_text = dumps(summary) + \"\\n\"\n    agg = os.path.join(data_dir, \"aggregates\")\n    for _ in range(3):  # health includes its own size; settle it\n        health_text = dumps(health) + \"\\n\"\n        size = len(summary_text.encode()) + len(health_text.encode()) + len(preview_text.encode())\n        health[\"lineage\"][\"aggregates\"][\"bytes\"] = size\n    health_text = dumps(health) + \"\\n\"\n    write_text(os.path.join(agg, \"summary.json\"), summary_text)\n    write_text(os.path.join(agg, \"health.json\"), health_text)\n    write_text(os.path.join(agg, \"preview.js\"), preview_text)\n    return {\"summary\": summary, \"health\": health, \"bytes\": size}\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- cli\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Almanac: daily AQHI pipeline with a data contract.\")\n    g = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n    g.add_argument(\"--date\", help=\"process one UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--backfill\", nargs=2, metavar=(\"START\", \"END\"), help=\"process every day from START to END\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--aggregate-only\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"rebuild data/aggregates from stored data\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--kind\", choices=[\"scheduled\", \"manual\", \"backfill\", \"revision\"],\n                   help=\"label for the run log (default: scheduled under a GitHub cron, backfill for --backfill, else manual)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--source\", choices=[\"auto\", \"hourly\", \"monthly\"], default=\"auto\",\n                   help=\"auto reads the live hourly file while it still covers the day, else the monthly archive\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--now\", help=\"pretend the clock reads this ISO time (tests)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--data-dir\", default=DEFAULT_DATA)"},{"id":"1:547","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":547,"end":582,"text":"    g = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n    g.add_argument(\"--date\", help=\"process one UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--backfill\", nargs=2, metavar=(\"START\", \"END\"), help=\"process every day from START to END\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--aggregate-only\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"rebuild data/aggregates from stored data\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--kind\", choices=[\"scheduled\", \"manual\", \"backfill\", \"revision\"],\n                   help=\"label for the run log (default: scheduled under a GitHub cron, backfill for --backfill, else manual)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--source\", choices=[\"auto\", \"hourly\", \"monthly\"], default=\"auto\",\n                   help=\"auto reads the live hourly file while it still covers the day, else the monthly archive\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--now\", help=\"pretend the clock reads this ISO time (tests)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--data-dir\", default=DEFAULT_DATA)\n    p.add_argument(\"--source-dir\", help=\"read source files from this folder instead of the network\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--contract\", help=\"path to contract.json\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--pause\", type=float, default=1.0, help=\"seconds between requests\")\n    a = p.parse_args(argv)\n\n    contract = C.load_contract(a.contract)\n    with open(os.path.join(HERE, \"known_issues.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        known = json.load(f)\n    fixed = parse_iso(a.now) if a.now else None\n    now = (lambda: fixed) if fixed else utcnow\n    data_dir = os.path.abspath(a.data_dir)\n\n    if a.aggregate_only:\n        out = build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known)\n        print(\"aggregates: %s bytes\" % (out[\"bytes\"] if out else 0))\n        return 0\n\n    if a.backfill:\n        start, end = Date.fromisoformat(a.backfill[0]), Date.fromisoformat(a.backfill[1])\n        if end < start:\n            p.error(\"END is before START\")\n        kind = a.kind or \"backfill\"\n    else:\n        start = end = Date.fromisoformat(a.date)\n        kind = a.kind or (\"scheduled\" if os.environ.get(\"GITHUB_EVENT_NAME\") == \"schedule\" else \"manual\")\n    if end >= now().date():"},{"id":"1:573","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":573,"end":604,"text":"\n    if a.backfill:\n        start, end = Date.fromisoformat(a.backfill[0]), Date.fromisoformat(a.backfill[1])\n        if end < start:\n            p.error(\"END is before START\")\n        kind = a.kind or \"backfill\"\n    else:\n        start = end = Date.fromisoformat(a.date)\n        kind = a.kind or (\"scheduled\" if os.environ.get(\"GITHUB_EVENT_NAME\") == \"schedule\" else \"manual\")\n    if end >= now().date():\n        p.error(\"a day can only be processed once it is over (UTC)\")\n\n    source_mode = \"monthly\" if kind == \"revision\" and a.source == \"auto\" else a.source\n    ctx = {\"contract\": contract, \"fetcher\": Fetcher(a.source_dir, a.pause), \"data_dir\": data_dir,\n           \"now\": now, \"kind\": kind, \"batch_id\": \"%s-%s\" % (kind, now().strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\")),\n           \"source_mode\": source_mode, \"resolved\": {}}\n    worst = \"pass\"\n    for day in days(start, end):\n        r = process_day(day, ctx)\n        worst = C.worst([worst, r[\"status\"]])\n        print(\"%s  %-9s %-5s in %4d out %4d  %s\" % (r[\"date\"], r[\"kind\"], r[\"status\"], r[\"rows_in\"], r[\"rows_out\"],\n                                                    \" \".join(\"%s:%s\" % (c[\"name\"], c[\"status\"]) for c in r[\"checks\"] if c[\"status\"] != \"pass\")))\n    out = build_aggregates(data_dir, contract, known)\n    print(\"downloaded %d bytes; aggregates %d bytes\" % (ctx[\"fetcher\"].downloaded, out[\"bytes\"] if out else 0))\n    if out and out[\"bytes\"] > contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]:\n        print(\"WARNING: aggregates are %d bytes, over their %d-byte budget\"\n              % (out[\"bytes\"], contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]), file=sys.stderr)\n    return 2 if worst == \"fail\" else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())"},{"id":"1:599","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py","start":599,"end":604,"text":"              % (out[\"bytes\"], contract[\"budgets\"][\"aggregates_bytes\"]), file=sys.stderr)\n    return 2 if worst == \"fail\" else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())"},{"id":"2:1","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":1,"end":36,"text":"\"\"\"Almanac's data contract: the checks a day of AQHI observations must pass before it is loaded.\n\nThe rules and thresholds live in contract.json. This module only knows how to apply them.\nEach check returns {\"name\", \"status\", \"detail\"}, where status is one of\npass, warn, fail or skip (skip = does not apply to this kind of run).\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nDATE_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$\")\nINT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\d{1,2}$\")\nNUM_RE = re.compile(r\"^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$\")\nRANK = {\"skip\": 0, \"pass\": 0, \"warn\": 1, \"fail\": 2}\n\n\ndef load_contract(path=None):\n    with open(path or os.path.join(HERE, \"contract.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\n\ndef check_cfg(contract, name):\n    for c in contract[\"checks\"]:\n        if c[\"name\"] == name:\n            return c\n    raise KeyError(name)\n\n\ndef reported(value):\n    \"\"\"The AQHI as the public sees it: rounded half up to a whole number; 11 means 10+.\"\"\"\n    return int(math.floor(value + 0.5))\n\n"},{"id":"2:27","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":27,"end":62,"text":"        if c[\"name\"] == name:\n            return c\n    raise KeyError(name)\n\n\ndef reported(value):\n    \"\"\"The AQHI as the public sees it: rounded half up to a whole number; 11 means 10+.\"\"\"\n    return int(math.floor(value + 0.5))\n\n\ndef worst(statuses):\n    top = \"pass\"\n    for s in statuses:\n        if RANK[s] > RANK[top]:\n            top = s\n    return top\n\n\ndef plural(n, word, many=None):\n    return \"%d %s\" % (n, word if n == 1 else (many or word + \"s\"))\n\n\ndef validate(contract, date, sources, now=None, live=True):\n    \"\"\"Apply the contract to one UTC day.\n\n    sources: {region: {\"header\": [str], \"rows\": [[str]] (rows whose date cell is `date`),\n                       \"newest\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z\" or None}}\n             A region with no file at all is None or {\"absent\": \"live\" | \"archive\",\n             \"lookback_hours\": n}: \"live\" when the run looked for the live feed and found none.\n    now:     datetime (UTC) of the run, for the freshness check.\n    live:    True when the source is the live hourly feed, False for a monthly archive.\n\n    Returns (checks, good_rows, quarantined) where good_rows are dicts ready to load\n    and quarantined are dicts with a reason.\n    \"\"\"\n    cols = contract[\"columns\"]"},{"id":"2:53","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":53,"end":88,"text":"                       \"newest\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z\" or None}}\n             A region with no file at all is None or {\"absent\": \"live\" | \"archive\",\n             \"lookback_hours\": n}: \"live\" when the run looked for the live feed and found none.\n    now:     datetime (UTC) of the run, for the freshness check.\n    live:    True when the source is the live hourly feed, False for a monthly archive.\n\n    Returns (checks, good_rows, quarantined) where good_rows are dicts ready to load\n    and quarantined are dicts with a reason.\n    \"\"\"\n    cols = contract[\"columns\"]\n    locs = contract[\"locations\"]\n    checks = []\n    quarantined = []\n\n    # 0. no file at all -----------------------------------------------------\n    # A region with no source file is not a broken schema: there is nothing to check.\n    # From the live feed it means the feed has stalled (freshness); from an archive it\n    # means the source does not cover the day (completeness). Every other check is not run.\n    absent = [r for r in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs})\n              if not sources.get(r) or sources[r].get(\"absent\")]\n    if absent:\n        names = \", \".join(r.upper() for r in absent)\n        live_absent = [r for r in absent if (sources.get(r) or {}).get(\"absent\") == \"live\"]\n        if live_absent:\n            fc = check_cfg(contract, \"freshness\")\n            look = (sources[live_absent[0]] or {}).get(\"lookback_hours\")\n            checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                           \"detail\": \"No live file for %s in the last %s: the feed seems to have stalled (limit %d hours).\" % (\n                               \", \".join(r.upper() for r in live_absent),\n                               plural(look, \"hour\") if look else \"few hours\", fc[\"max_age_hours\"])})\n        else:\n            checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                           \"detail\": \"The source has no file that covers this day (%s).\" % names})\n        done = {c[\"name\"] for c in checks}\n        for c in contract[\"checks\"]:\n            if c[\"name\"] not in done:"},{"id":"2:79","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":79,"end":114,"text":"            checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                           \"detail\": \"No live file for %s in the last %s: the feed seems to have stalled (limit %d hours).\" % (\n                               \", \".join(r.upper() for r in live_absent),\n                               plural(look, \"hour\") if look else \"few hours\", fc[\"max_age_hours\"])})\n        else:\n            checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                           \"detail\": \"The source has no file that covers this day (%s).\" % names})\n        done = {c[\"name\"] for c in checks}\n        for c in contract[\"checks\"]:\n            if c[\"name\"] not in done:\n                checks.append({\"name\": c[\"name\"], \"status\": \"skip\",\n                               \"detail\": \"Not run, because there was no file to check.\"})\n        order_ = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]\n        checks.sort(key=lambda c: order_.index(c[\"name\"]))\n        return checks, [], quarantined\n\n    # 1. schema -------------------------------------------------------------\n    missing = []\n    for region in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs}):\n        src = sources.get(region)\n        header = src[\"header\"] if src else []\n        need = [cols[\"date\"], cols[\"hour\"]] + [l[\"id\"] for l in locs if l[\"region\"] == region]\n        missing += [\"%s (%s)\" % (n, region.upper()) for n in need if n not in header]\n    if missing:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"schema\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                       \"detail\": \"Missing column%s: %s.\" % (\"\" if len(missing) == 1 else \"s\", \", \".join(missing))})\n        return finish(contract, checks), [], quarantined\n    checks.append({\"name\": \"schema\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                   \"detail\": \"All %d expected columns are present.\" % (2 + len(locs))})\n\n    # Gather cells: (hour, location) -> list of raw strings\n    bad_types = []\n    hours_seen = set()\n    cells = {}\n    for region in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs}):\n        src = sources[region]"},{"id":"2:105","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":105,"end":140,"text":"        return finish(contract, checks), [], quarantined\n    checks.append({\"name\": \"schema\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                   \"detail\": \"All %d expected columns are present.\" % (2 + len(locs))})\n\n    # Gather cells: (hour, location) -> list of raw strings\n    bad_types = []\n    hours_seen = set()\n    cells = {}\n    for region in sorted({l[\"region\"] for l in locs}):\n        src = sources[region]\n        idx = {name: i for i, name in enumerate(src[\"header\"])}\n        mine = [l for l in locs if l[\"region\"] == region]\n        region_hours = []\n        for row in src[\"rows\"]:\n            def cell(name):\n                i = idx[name]\n                return row[i].strip() if i < len(row) else \"\"\n            d, h = cell(cols[\"date\"]), cell(cols[\"hour\"])\n            if not DATE_RE.match(d) or not INT_RE.match(h) or not 0 <= int(h) <= 23:\n                bad_types.append(\"%s row with date %r and hour %r\" % (region.upper(), d, h))\n                continue\n            hour = int(h)\n            region_hours.append(hour)\n            for l in mine:\n                v = cell(l[\"id\"])\n                if v == \"\":\n                    continue\n                if not NUM_RE.match(v):\n                    bad_types.append(\"%s at %02d:00 is %r\" % (l[\"city\"], hour, v))\n                    quarantined.append(qrow(date, hour, l, v, \"not a number\"))\n                    continue\n                cells.setdefault((hour, l[\"id\"]), []).append(v)\n        hours_seen.update(region_hours)\n        sources[region][\"_hours\"] = region_hours\n\n    # 2. types --------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"2:131","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":131,"end":166,"text":"                    continue\n                if not NUM_RE.match(v):\n                    bad_types.append(\"%s at %02d:00 is %r\" % (l[\"city\"], hour, v))\n                    quarantined.append(qrow(date, hour, l, v, \"not a number\"))\n                    continue\n                cells.setdefault((hour, l[\"id\"]), []).append(v)\n        hours_seen.update(region_hours)\n        sources[region][\"_hours\"] = region_hours\n\n    # 2. types --------------------------------------------------------------\n    if bad_types:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"types\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%s of the wrong kind, e.g. %s.\" % (plural(len(bad_types), \"value\"), bad_types[0])})\n    else:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"types\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                       \"detail\": \"Every date, hour and reading parsed.\"})\n\n    # 3. range --------------------------------------------------------------\n    rc = check_cfg(contract, \"range\")\n    in_range = {}\n    odd = []\n    total_readings = 0\n    by_id = {l[\"id\"]: l for l in locs}\n    for key in sorted(cells):\n        hour, lid = key\n        kept = []\n        for v in cells[key]:\n            total_readings += 1\n            x = float(v)\n            if rc[\"min\"] <= x <= rc[\"max\"]:\n                kept.append(v)\n            else:\n                odd.append(\"%s at %02d:00 = %s\" % (by_id[lid][\"city\"], hour, v))\n                quarantined.append(qrow(date, hour, by_id[lid], v, \"outside %g to %g\" % (rc[\"min\"], rc[\"max\"])))\n        if kept:\n            in_range[key] = kept"},{"id":"2:157","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":157,"end":192,"text":"        for v in cells[key]:\n            total_readings += 1\n            x = float(v)\n            if rc[\"min\"] <= x <= rc[\"max\"]:\n                kept.append(v)\n            else:\n                odd.append(\"%s at %02d:00 = %s\" % (by_id[lid][\"city\"], hour, v))\n                quarantined.append(qrow(date, hour, by_id[lid], v, \"outside %g to %g\" % (rc[\"min\"], rc[\"max\"])))\n        if kept:\n            in_range[key] = kept\n    if not odd:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"range\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                       \"detail\": \"All %s lie between %g and %g.\" % (plural(total_readings, \"reading\"), rc[\"min\"], rc[\"max\"])})\n    else:\n        frac = len(odd) / float(max(total_readings, 1))\n        status = \"fail\" if frac > rc[\"fail_fraction\"] else \"warn\"\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"range\", \"status\": status,\n                       \"detail\": \"%s of %d set aside (%s), e.g. %s.\" % (\n                           plural(len(odd), \"reading\"), total_readings,\n                           \"too many to trust the day\" if status == \"fail\" else \"few enough to load the rest\", odd[0])})\n\n    # 4. uniqueness ---------------------------------------------------------\n    dup_same, dup_conflict = [], []\n    good = {}\n    for key in sorted(in_range):\n        vals = in_range[key]\n        if len(vals) == 1:\n            good[key] = vals[0]\n            continue\n        if len({float(v) for v in vals}) == 1:\n            dup_same.append(key)\n            good[key] = vals[0]\n        else:\n            dup_conflict.append(key)\n            for v in vals:\n                quarantined.append(qrow(date, key[0], by_id[key[1]], v, \"conflicting duplicate\"))"},{"id":"2:183","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":183,"end":218,"text":"        if len(vals) == 1:\n            good[key] = vals[0]\n            continue\n        if len({float(v) for v in vals}) == 1:\n            dup_same.append(key)\n            good[key] = vals[0]\n        else:\n            dup_conflict.append(key)\n            for v in vals:\n                quarantined.append(qrow(date, key[0], by_id[key[1]], v, \"conflicting duplicate\"))\n    def name_key(k):\n        return \"%s at %02d:00\" % (by_id[k[1]][\"city\"], k[0])\n    if dup_conflict:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"uniqueness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%s with two different readings, e.g. %s.\" % (plural(len(dup_conflict), \"city-hour\"), name_key(dup_conflict[0]))})\n    elif dup_same:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"uniqueness\", \"status\": \"warn\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%s repeated with the same reading; one copy kept.\" % plural(len(dup_same), \"city-hour\")})\n    else:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"uniqueness\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                       \"detail\": \"No city has two readings for the same hour.\"})\n\n    # 5. completeness -------------------------------------------------------\n    cc = check_cfg(contract, \"completeness\")\n    short = []\n    for region in sorted(sources):\n        if region not in {l[\"region\"] for l in locs}:\n            continue\n        n = len(set(sources[region].get(\"_hours\", [])))\n        if n < cc[\"hours\"]:\n            short.append((region, n))\n    if any(n == 0 for _, n in short):\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                       \"detail\": \"The source has no rows for this day (%s).\" % \", \".join(r.upper() for r, n in short if n == 0)})\n    elif short:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"warn\","},{"id":"2:209","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":209,"end":244,"text":"        if region not in {l[\"region\"] for l in locs}:\n            continue\n        n = len(set(sources[region].get(\"_hours\", [])))\n        if n < cc[\"hours\"]:\n            short.append((region, n))\n    if any(n == 0 for _, n in short):\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                       \"detail\": \"The source has no rows for this day (%s).\" % \", \".join(r.upper() for r, n in short if n == 0)})\n    elif short:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"warn\",\n                       \"detail\": \"Only %s.\" % \"; \".join(\"%d of %d hours in the %s file\" % (n, cc[\"hours\"], r.upper()) for r, n in short)})\n    else:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"completeness\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                       \"detail\": \"All %d hours are in the file.\" % cc[\"hours\"]})\n\n    # 6. volume -------------------------------------------------------------\n    vc = check_cfg(contract, \"volume\")\n    per_city = {l[\"id\"]: 0 for l in locs}\n    for (hour, lid) in good:\n        per_city[lid] += 1\n    expected = cc[\"hours\"] * len(locs)\n    total = sum(per_city.values())\n    thin = [(by_id[lid][\"city\"], n) for lid, n in per_city.items() if n < vc[\"min_hours_per_city\"]]\n    if total < vc[\"fail_below_fraction\"] * expected:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"fail\",\n                       \"detail\": \"Only %d of %d expected readings; too few to load.\" % (total, expected)})\n    elif thin:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"warn\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%s; high-risk hours there may be missed (%d of %d readings in all).\" % (\n                           \"; \".join(\"%s had readings for %d of 24 hours\" % t for t in thin), total, expected)})\n    else:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%d of %d readings; every city had at least %d hours.\" % (total, expected, vc[\"min_hours_per_city\"])})\n\n    # 7. freshness ----------------------------------------------------------\n    fc = check_cfg(contract, \"freshness\")"},{"id":"2:235","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":235,"end":270,"text":"    elif thin:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"warn\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%s; high-risk hours there may be missed (%d of %d readings in all).\" % (\n                           \"; \".join(\"%s had readings for %d of 24 hours\" % t for t in thin), total, expected)})\n    else:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"volume\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                       \"detail\": \"%d of %d readings; every city had at least %d hours.\" % (total, expected, vc[\"min_hours_per_city\"])})\n\n    # 7. freshness ----------------------------------------------------------\n    fc = check_cfg(contract, \"freshness\")\n    if not live:\n        checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"skip\",\n                       \"detail\": \"Read from a monthly archive, so the live feed's age does not apply.\"})\n    else:\n        newest = [s.get(\"newest\") for s in sources.values() if s.get(\"newest\")]\n        if not newest or now is None:\n            checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"fail\", \"detail\": \"Could not tell how new the source is.\"})\n        else:\n            oldest_newest = min(parse_hour(n) for n in newest)\n            age = (now - oldest_newest).total_seconds() / 3600.0\n            if age <= fc[\"max_age_hours\"]:\n                checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"pass\",\n                               \"detail\": \"The feed's newest hour was %.1f hours old.\" % max(age, 0)})\n            else:\n                checks.append({\"name\": \"freshness\", \"status\": \"warn\",\n                               \"detail\": \"The feed's newest hour was %.1f hours old (limit %d).\" % (age, fc[\"max_age_hours\"])})\n\n    status = worst(c[\"status\"] for c in checks)\n    rows = []\n    if status != \"fail\":\n        thr = contract[\"high_risk_threshold\"]\n        for (hour, lid) in sorted(good, key=lambda k: (k[0], order(locs, k[1]))):\n            x = float(good[(hour, lid)])\n            r = reported(x)\n            rows.append({\n                \"date\": date, \"hour_utc\": hour, \"location_id\": lid, \"city\": by_id[lid][\"city\"],"},{"id":"2:261","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":261,"end":296,"text":"\n    status = worst(c[\"status\"] for c in checks)\n    rows = []\n    if status != \"fail\":\n        thr = contract[\"high_risk_threshold\"]\n        for (hour, lid) in sorted(good, key=lambda k: (k[0], order(locs, k[1]))):\n            x = float(good[(hour, lid)])\n            r = reported(x)\n            rows.append({\n                \"date\": date, \"hour_utc\": hour, \"location_id\": lid, \"city\": by_id[lid][\"city\"],\n                \"aqhi\": \"%.2f\" % x, \"aqhi_reported\": \"10+\" if r > 10 else str(r),\n                \"high_risk\": 1 if r >= thr else 0,\n            })\n    return checks, rows, quarantined\n\n\ndef finish(contract, checks):\n    names = [c[\"name\"] for c in contract[\"checks\"]]\n    done = {c[\"name\"] for c in checks}\n    for n in names:\n        if n not in done:\n            checks.append({\"name\": n, \"status\": \"skip\", \"detail\": \"Not run, because an earlier check failed.\"})\n    return checks\n\n\ndef order(locs, lid):\n    for i, l in enumerate(locs):\n        if l[\"id\"] == lid:\n            return i\n    return 99\n\n\ndef qrow(date, hour, loc, value, reason):\n    return {\"date\": date, \"hour_utc\": hour, \"location_id\": loc[\"id\"], \"city\": loc[\"city\"],\n            \"value\": value, \"reason\": reason}\n"},{"id":"2:287","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.py","start":287,"end":299,"text":"    for i, l in enumerate(locs):\n        if l[\"id\"] == lid:\n            return i\n    return 99\n\n\ndef qrow(date, hour, loc, value, reason):\n    return {\"date\": date, \"hour_utc\": hour, \"location_id\": loc[\"id\"], \"city\": loc[\"city\"],\n            \"value\": value, \"reason\": reason}\n\n\ndef parse_hour(s):\n    return datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)"},{"id":"3:1","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json","start":1,"end":36,"text":"{\n  \"name\": \"aqhi-hourly-observations\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"about\": \"The promise each day's AQHI observations must keep before Almanac loads them. Read by pipeline/contract.py; the 'plain' lines are shown on the page.\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"publisher\": \"Environment and Climate Change Canada, Meteorological Service of Canada\",\n    \"attribution\": \"Data Source: Environment and Climate Change Canada\",\n    \"licence\": \"Environment and Climate Change Canada Data Services End-use Licence\",\n    \"licence_url\": \"https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/licence/readme_en/\",\n    \"docs_url\": \"https://eccc-msc.github.io/open-data/msc-data/aqhi/readme_aqhi_en/\",\n    \"hourly_url\": \"https://dd.weather.gc.ca/{yyyymmdd}/WXO-DD/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/realtime/csv/{yyyymmddhh}_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs.csv\",\n    \"monthly_url\": \"https://dd.weather.gc.ca/today/air_quality/aqhi/{region}/observation/monthly/csv/{yyyymm}_MONTHLY_AQHI_{REGION}_SiteObs{suffix}.csv\",\n    \"hourly_window_days\": 6,\n    \"hourly_lookback_hours\": 8\n  },\n  \"key\": [\"date\", \"hour_utc\", \"location_id\"],\n  \"columns\": {\n    \"date\": \"Date\",\n    \"hour\": \"Hour (UTC)\"\n  },\n  \"locations\": [\n    { \"id\": \"JBRIK\", \"city\": \"Vancouver\", \"zone\": \"Metro Vancouver – NW\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"JBOBQ\", \"city\": \"Victoria\", \"zone\": \"Victoria / Saanich\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"JAFUV\", \"city\": \"Kelowna\", \"zone\": \"Central Okanagan\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"JAFNW\", \"city\": \"Kamloops\", \"zone\": \"Kamloops\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"JBLVS\", \"city\": \"Prince George\", \"zone\": \"Prince George\", \"region\": \"pyr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"IAKID\", \"city\": \"Calgary\", \"zone\": \"Calgary\", \"region\": \"pnr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"IACMP\", \"city\": \"Edmonton\", \"zone\": \"Edmonton\", \"region\": \"pnr\" }\n  ],\n  \"high_risk_threshold\": 7,\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"schema\",\n      \"title\": \"The columns are where we expect them\",\n      \"plain\": \"The file must have a date column, an hour column and one column for each of the seven cities. If ECCC renames or drops a column, nothing is loaded.\",\n      \"severity\": \"fail\""},{"id":"3:27","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json","start":27,"end":62,"text":"    { \"id\": \"IAKID\", \"city\": \"Calgary\", \"zone\": \"Calgary\", \"region\": \"pnr\" },\n    { \"id\": \"IACMP\", \"city\": \"Edmonton\", \"zone\": \"Edmonton\", \"region\": \"pnr\" }\n  ],\n  \"high_risk_threshold\": 7,\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"schema\",\n      \"title\": \"The columns are where we expect them\",\n      \"plain\": \"The file must have a date column, an hour column and one column for each of the seven cities. If ECCC renames or drops a column, nothing is loaded.\",\n      \"severity\": \"fail\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"types\",\n      \"title\": \"Every value is the right kind of thing\",\n      \"plain\": \"Dates must be dates, hours must be whole numbers from 0 to 23, and readings must be numbers or blank. Anything else means the format changed, so nothing is loaded.\",\n      \"severity\": \"fail\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"range\",\n      \"title\": \"Readings are on the AQHI scale\",\n      \"plain\": \"A reading must lie between 1 and 11 (the file writes the top category, 10+, as 11). Odd values are set aside; if more than 1 in 100 are odd, the day is refused.\",\n      \"min\": 1.0,\n      \"max\": 11.0,\n      \"fail_fraction\": 0.01\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"uniqueness\",\n      \"title\": \"One reading per city per hour\",\n      \"plain\": \"Each city may have only one reading for each hour. Exact repeats are dropped with a warning; two different readings for the same hour stop the load.\",\n      \"severity\": \"fail\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"completeness\",\n      \"title\": \"All 24 hours of the day are in the file\",\n      \"plain\": \"The source file must contain a row for every hour of the day, even if some cities are blank in it. A short day is a warning; a missing day is a failure.\",\n      \"hours\": 24"},{"id":"3:53","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json","start":53,"end":87,"text":"      \"name\": \"uniqueness\",\n      \"title\": \"One reading per city per hour\",\n      \"plain\": \"Each city may have only one reading for each hour. Exact repeats are dropped with a warning; two different readings for the same hour stop the load.\",\n      \"severity\": \"fail\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"completeness\",\n      \"title\": \"All 24 hours of the day are in the file\",\n      \"plain\": \"The source file must contain a row for every hour of the day, even if some cities are blank in it. A short day is a warning; a missing day is a failure.\",\n      \"hours\": 24\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"volume\",\n      \"title\": \"Enough cities reported\",\n      \"plain\": \"Each city should have a reading for at least 18 of the 24 hours. Fewer is a warning, because high-risk hours could be missed. Under half of all expected readings is a failure.\",\n      \"min_hours_per_city\": 18,\n      \"fail_below_fraction\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"freshness\",\n      \"title\": \"The source is up to date\",\n      \"plain\": \"When the daily run reads the live feed, its newest hour should be at most 6 hours old. Older is a warning that the feed may be stalling; no live file at all in the last 8 hours means it has stalled, and the day is refused. A backfill reads a monthly archive, so this does not apply.\",\n      \"max_age_hours\": 6\n    }\n  ],\n  \"slo\": {\n    \"plain\": \"Fresh means the newest hour on this page is at most 36 hours old and the pipeline has run in the last 26 hours.\",\n    \"max_data_age_hours\": 36,\n    \"max_run_age_hours\": 26\n  },\n  \"budgets\": {\n    \"aggregates_bytes\": 200000,\n    \"detail_days\": 90\n  }\n}"},{"id":"3:79","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json","start":79,"end":87,"text":"    \"plain\": \"Fresh means the newest hour on this page is at most 36 hours old and the pipeline has run in the last 26 hours.\",\n    \"max_data_age_hours\": 36,\n    \"max_run_age_hours\": 26\n  },\n  \"budgets\": {\n    \"aggregates_bytes\": 200000,\n    \"detail_days\": 90\n  }\n}"},{"id":"4:1","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml","start":1,"end":36,"text":"# Install (once, from the repo root, with a token that has the workflow scope): mkdir -p .github/workflows && git mv projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml .github/workflows/almanac.yml && git commit -m \"Schedule the Almanac pipeline\" && git push\n#\n# Almanac: fetch yesterday's AQHI observations from ECCC, check them against\n# projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json, store them, rebuild the page's aggregates and\n# append a run record. Commits only when something under projects/almanac/data changed.\n# A run whose contract fails is still committed (the page must show the red day), and\n# then the job is marked failed so the owner is told.\n\nname: Almanac pipeline\n\non:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"17 7 * * *\" # 07:17 UTC every day; the previous UTC day is complete by then\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      date:\n        description: \"UTC day to process, YYYY-MM-DD (blank means yesterday)\"\n        required: false\n        default: \"\"\n      backfill_start:\n        description: \"Backfill from this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD (with backfill_end)\"\n        required: false\n        default: \"\"\n      backfill_end:\n        description: \"Backfill to this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\"\n        required: false\n        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: almanac-pipeline\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:"},{"id":"4:27","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml","start":27,"end":62,"text":"        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: almanac-pipeline\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  run:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    steps:\n      - name: Check out\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Python\n        uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: \"3.11\"\n\n      - name: Contract tests\n        run: python -I -m unittest discover -s projects/almanac/tests -p \"test_*.py\"\n\n      - name: Run the pipeline\n        id: run\n        env:\n          IN_DATE: ${{ github.event.inputs.date }}\n          IN_START: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_start }}\n          IN_END: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_end }}\n          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n        run: |\n          set +e\n          code=0\n          if [ -n \"$IN_START\" ] && [ -n \"$IN_END\" ]; then"},{"id":"4:53","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml","start":53,"end":88,"text":"        id: run\n        env:\n          IN_DATE: ${{ github.event.inputs.date }}\n          IN_START: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_start }}\n          IN_END: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_end }}\n          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n        run: |\n          set +e\n          code=0\n          if [ -n \"$IN_START\" ] && [ -n \"$IN_END\" ]; then\n            label=\"backfill $IN_START to $IN_END\"\n            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$IN_START\" \"$IN_END\" || code=$?\n          else\n            day=\"${IN_DATE:-$(date -u -d yesterday +%F)}\"\n            label=\"$day\"\n            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date \"$day\" || code=$?\n            # On the 4th, reload last month from ECCC's corrected (\"backfilled\") monthly file.\n            if [ \"$EVENT\" = \"schedule\" ] && [ \"$(date -u +%d)\" = \"04\" ]; then\n              first=$(date -u +%Y-%m-01)\n              start=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 month\" +%F)\n              end=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 day\" +%F)\n              label=\"$label, revision $start to $end\"\n              python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$start\" \"$end\" --kind revision || code=$?\n            fi\n          fi\n          echo \"code=$code\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          echo \"label=$label\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Commit the data if it changed\n        env:\n          LABEL: ${{ steps.run.outputs.label }}\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n          git add projects/almanac/data\n          if git diff --cached --quiet; then"},{"id":"4:79","path":"projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml","start":79,"end":100,"text":"          echo \"label=$label\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Commit the data if it changed\n        env:\n          LABEL: ${{ steps.run.outputs.label }}\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n          git add projects/almanac/data\n          if git diff --cached --quiet; then\n            echo \"Nothing changed.\"\n            exit 0\n          fi\n          git commit -m \"Almanac: $LABEL\"\n          git pull --rebase\n          git push\n\n      - name: Report a failed contract\n        if: steps.run.outputs.code != '0'\n        run: |\n          echo \"The pipeline recorded a failed run (exit ${{ steps.run.outputs.code }}). See projects/almanac/data/runs.ndjson.\"\n          exit 1"},{"id":"5:1","path":".github/workflows/almanac.yml","start":1,"end":36,"text":"# Install (once, from the repo root, with a token that has the workflow scope): mkdir -p .github/workflows && git mv projects/almanac/pipeline/almanac.yml .github/workflows/almanac.yml && git commit -m \"Schedule the Almanac pipeline\" && git push\n#\n# Almanac: fetch yesterday's AQHI observations from ECCC, check them against\n# projects/almanac/pipeline/contract.json, store them, rebuild the page's aggregates and\n# append a run record. Commits only when something under projects/almanac/data changed.\n# A run whose contract fails is still committed (the page must show the red day), and\n# then the job is marked failed so the owner is told.\n\nname: Almanac pipeline\n\non:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: \"17 7 * * *\" # 07:17 UTC every day; the previous UTC day is complete by then\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      date:\n        description: \"UTC day to process, YYYY-MM-DD (blank means yesterday)\"\n        required: false\n        default: \"\"\n      backfill_start:\n        description: \"Backfill from this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD (with backfill_end)\"\n        required: false\n        default: \"\"\n      backfill_end:\n        description: \"Backfill to this UTC day, YYYY-MM-DD\"\n        required: false\n        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: almanac-pipeline\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:"},{"id":"5:27","path":".github/workflows/almanac.yml","start":27,"end":62,"text":"        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: almanac-pipeline\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  run:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    steps:\n      - name: Check out\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Python\n        uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: \"3.11\"\n\n      - name: Contract tests\n        run: python -I -m unittest discover -s projects/almanac/tests -p \"test_*.py\"\n\n      - name: Run the pipeline\n        id: run\n        env:\n          IN_DATE: ${{ github.event.inputs.date }}\n          IN_START: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_start }}\n          IN_END: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_end }}\n          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n        run: |\n          set +e\n          code=0\n          if [ -n \"$IN_START\" ] && [ -n \"$IN_END\" ]; then"},{"id":"5:53","path":".github/workflows/almanac.yml","start":53,"end":88,"text":"        id: run\n        env:\n          IN_DATE: ${{ github.event.inputs.date }}\n          IN_START: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_start }}\n          IN_END: ${{ github.event.inputs.backfill_end }}\n          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n        run: |\n          set +e\n          code=0\n          if [ -n \"$IN_START\" ] && [ -n \"$IN_END\" ]; then\n            label=\"backfill $IN_START to $IN_END\"\n            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$IN_START\" \"$IN_END\" || code=$?\n          else\n            day=\"${IN_DATE:-$(date -u -d yesterday +%F)}\"\n            label=\"$day\"\n            python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --date \"$day\" || code=$?\n            # On the 4th, reload last month from ECCC's corrected (\"backfilled\") monthly file.\n            if [ \"$EVENT\" = \"schedule\" ] && [ \"$(date -u +%d)\" = \"04\" ]; then\n              first=$(date -u +%Y-%m-01)\n              start=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 month\" +%F)\n              end=$(date -u -d \"$first -1 day\" +%F)\n              label=\"$label, revision $start to $end\"\n              python -I projects/almanac/pipeline/run.py --backfill \"$start\" \"$end\" --kind revision || code=$?\n            fi\n          fi\n          echo \"code=$code\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          echo \"label=$label\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Commit the data if it changed\n        env:\n          LABEL: ${{ steps.run.outputs.label }}\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n          git add projects/almanac/data\n          if git diff --cached --quiet; then"},{"id":"5:79","path":".github/workflows/almanac.yml","start":79,"end":100,"text":"          echo \"label=$label\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Commit the data if it changed\n        env:\n          LABEL: ${{ steps.run.outputs.label }}\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n          git add projects/almanac/data\n          if git diff --cached --quiet; then\n            echo \"Nothing changed.\"\n            exit 0\n          fi\n          git commit -m \"Almanac: $LABEL\"\n          git pull --rebase\n          git push\n\n      - name: Report a failed contract\n        if: steps.run.outputs.code != '0'\n        run: |\n          echo \"The pipeline recorded a failed run (exit ${{ steps.run.outputs.code }}). See projects/almanac/data/runs.ndjson.\"\n          exit 1"},{"id":"6:1","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":1,"end":36,"text":"// Almanac: the page's logic, kept apart from drawing so Node can test it.\n// Works in the browser (window.AlmanacModel) and in Node (module.exports).\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n\n  var HOUR = 3600 * 1000;\n  var MONTHS = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];\n  var LONG_MONTHS = ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', 'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'];\n  var DAYS = ['Sun', 'Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri', 'Sat'];\n\n  function parse(iso) {\n    if (!iso) return NaN;\n    if (/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/.test(iso)) iso += 'T00:00:00Z';\n    return Date.parse(iso);\n  }\n\n  // ---- words and numbers -------------------------------------------------\n\n  function plural(n, word, many) {\n    return fmtInt(n) + ' ' + (n === 1 ? word : (many || word + 's'));\n  }\n\n  function fmtInt(n) {\n    return String(Math.round(n)).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ',');\n  }\n\n  function ageText(hours) {\n    if (!isFinite(hours)) return 'unknown';\n    if (hours < 0) hours = 0;\n    if (hours < 1) {\n      var m = Math.round(hours * 60);\n      return m <= 1 ? 'a minute' : m + ' minutes';\n    }\n    if (hours < 48) {\n      var h = Math.round(hours);\n      return h === 1 ? '1 hour' : h + ' hours';"},{"id":"6:27","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":27,"end":62,"text":"  function ageText(hours) {\n    if (!isFinite(hours)) return 'unknown';\n    if (hours < 0) hours = 0;\n    if (hours < 1) {\n      var m = Math.round(hours * 60);\n      return m <= 1 ? 'a minute' : m + ' minutes';\n    }\n    if (hours < 48) {\n      var h = Math.round(hours);\n      return h === 1 ? '1 hour' : h + ' hours';\n    }\n    var d = Math.floor(hours / 24);\n    return d + ' days';\n  }\n\n  function dayLabel(iso, withYear) {\n    var t = new Date(parse(iso));\n    return t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + (withYear ? ' ' + t.getUTCFullYear() : '');\n  }\n\n  function longDay(iso) {\n    var t = new Date(parse(iso));\n    return DAYS[t.getUTCDay()] + ' ' + t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + LONG_MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + ' ' + t.getUTCFullYear();\n  }\n\n  function stamp(iso) {\n    var t = new Date(parse(iso));\n    var hh = ('0' + t.getUTCHours()).slice(-2), mm = ('0' + t.getUTCMinutes()).slice(-2);\n    return t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + ', ' + hh + ':' + mm + ' UTC';\n  }\n\n  function bytesText(b) {\n    if (b >= 1e6) return (b / 1e6).toFixed(1) + ' MB';\n    if (b >= 1e3) return Math.round(b / 1e3) + ' KB';\n    return b + ' bytes';\n  }"},{"id":"6:53","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":53,"end":88,"text":"    var t = new Date(parse(iso));\n    var hh = ('0' + t.getUTCHours()).slice(-2), mm = ('0' + t.getUTCMinutes()).slice(-2);\n    return t.getUTCDate() + ' ' + MONTHS[t.getUTCMonth()] + ', ' + hh + ':' + mm + ' UTC';\n  }\n\n  function bytesText(b) {\n    if (b >= 1e6) return (b / 1e6).toFixed(1) + ' MB';\n    if (b >= 1e3) return Math.round(b / 1e3) + ' KB';\n    return b + ' bytes';\n  }\n\n  // ---- freshness ---------------------------------------------------------\n  // Fresh only when the newest hour of data is within the data SLO AND the pipeline\n  // ran recently enough. `now` is injected so the rule can be tested without a clock.\n\n  function freshness(now, latestHour, latestRunFinished, slo) {\n    var dataAge = (now - parse(latestHour)) / HOUR;\n    var runAge = (now - parse(latestRunFinished)) / HOUR;\n    var reasons = [];\n    if (!isFinite(dataAge)) reasons.push('There is no data yet.');\n    else if (dataAge > slo.max_data_age_hours) {\n      reasons.push('The newest hour is ' + ageText(dataAge) + ' old; the limit is ' + slo.max_data_age_hours + ' hours.');\n    }\n    if (!isFinite(runAge)) reasons.push('The pipeline has never run.');\n    else if (runAge > slo.max_run_age_hours) {\n      reasons.push('The last run was ' + ageText(runAge) + ' ago; it should run at least every ' + slo.max_run_age_hours + ' hours.');\n    }\n    var stale = reasons.length > 0;\n    return {\n      state: stale ? 'stale' : 'fresh',\n      word: stale ? 'Stale' : 'Fresh',\n      dataAgeHours: dataAge,\n      runAgeHours: runAge,\n      reasons: reasons,\n      // fraction of the data SLO used, for the dial (can exceed 1)\n      used: isFinite(dataAge) ? Math.max(0, dataAge) / slo.max_data_age_hours : Infinity"},{"id":"6:79","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":79,"end":114,"text":"    }\n    var stale = reasons.length > 0;\n    return {\n      state: stale ? 'stale' : 'fresh',\n      word: stale ? 'Stale' : 'Fresh',\n      dataAgeHours: dataAge,\n      runAgeHours: runAge,\n      reasons: reasons,\n      // fraction of the data SLO used, for the dial (can exceed 1)\n      used: isFinite(dataAge) ? Math.max(0, dataAge) / slo.max_data_age_hours : Infinity\n    };\n  }\n\n  // ---- runs and contract -------------------------------------------------\n\n  var STATUS = {\n    pass: { word: 'Passed', glyph: '✓', day: 'all checks passed' },\n    warn: { word: 'Warning', glyph: '!', day: 'loaded with a warning' },\n    fail: { word: 'Failed', glyph: '×', day: 'refused: a check failed' },\n    skip: { word: 'Not run', glyph: '–', day: '' },\n    none: { word: 'No run', glyph: '', day: 'no run for this day' }\n  };\n  var CODE = { p: 'pass', w: 'warn', f: 'fail', s: 'skip' };\n\n  var KIND = {\n    scheduled: 'scheduled run',\n    manual: 'run by hand',\n    backfill: 'backfill',\n    revision: 'revision from ECCC’s corrected file'\n  };\n\n  function dayChecks(day, health) {\n    // [{name, title, plain, status, detail}] for one calendar entry\n    var defs = health.contract.checks;\n    return defs.map(function (def, i) {\n      var code = day.checks ? day.checks.charAt(i) : 's';"},{"id":"6:105","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":105,"end":140,"text":"    manual: 'run by hand',\n    backfill: 'backfill',\n    revision: 'revision from ECCC’s corrected file'\n  };\n\n  function dayChecks(day, health) {\n    // [{name, title, plain, status, detail}] for one calendar entry\n    var defs = health.contract.checks;\n    return defs.map(function (def, i) {\n      var code = day.checks ? day.checks.charAt(i) : 's';\n      return {\n        name: def.name, title: def.title, plain: def.plain,\n        status: CODE[code] || 'skip',\n        detail: day.details ? day.details[i] : null\n      };\n    });\n  }\n\n  function describeDay(day) {\n    var s = STATUS[day.status] || STATUS.none;\n    if (day.status === 'none') return longDay(day.date) + '. No run.';\n    var kind = KIND[day.kind] || day.kind;\n    var parts = [longDay(day.date) + '.', s.word + ': ' + s.day + '.'];\n    parts.push(kind.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + kind.slice(1) + (day.runs > 1 ? ' (' + day.runs + ' runs; latest shown)' : '') + '.');\n    parts.push(loadedText(day));\n    if (day.details && day.checks) {\n      for (var i = 0; i < day.checks.length; i++) {\n        var c = day.checks.charAt(i);\n        if ((c === 'w' || c === 'f') && day.details[i]) { parts.push(day.details[i]); break; }\n      }\n    }\n    return parts.join(' ');\n  }\n\n  function loadedText(day) {\n    if (day.loaded) return fmtInt(day.rows_out) + ' of 168 readings loaded.';"},{"id":"6:131","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":131,"end":166,"text":"      for (var i = 0; i < day.checks.length; i++) {\n        var c = day.checks.charAt(i);\n        if ((c === 'w' || c === 'f') && day.details[i]) { parts.push(day.details[i]); break; }\n      }\n    }\n    return parts.join(' ');\n  }\n\n  function loadedText(day) {\n    if (day.loaded) return fmtInt(day.rows_out) + ' of 168 readings loaded.';\n    if (day.kept) return 'Nothing new loaded; the day’s earlier load (' + plural(day.kept, 'reading') + ') is kept and still counted.';\n    return 'Nothing loaded.';\n  }\n\n  // Which check causes the amber days: {total, counts: {name: days}, top: name, topCount}\n  function warnCauses(calendar, names) {\n    var out = { total: 0, counts: {}, top: null, topCount: 0 };\n    calendar.forEach(function (d) {\n      if (d.status !== 'warn' || !d.checks) return;\n      out.total++;\n      for (var i = 0; i < d.checks.length && i < names.length; i++) {\n        if (d.checks.charAt(i) === 'w') out.counts[names[i]] = (out.counts[names[i]] || 0) + 1;\n      }\n    });\n    names.forEach(function (n) {\n      if ((out.counts[n] || 0) > out.topCount) { out.top = n; out.topCount = out.counts[n]; }\n    });\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  // health.json keeps full entries for recent days and packs older ones into short tuples\n  // (health.calendar_old); this returns one plain entry per day, oldest first.\n  var UNPACK = {\n    status: { p: 'pass', w: 'warn', f: 'fail', n: 'none' },\n    kind: { s: 'scheduled', m: 'manual', b: 'backfill', r: 'revision' },\n    src: { H: 'hourly snapshot', M: 'monthly archive', R: 'revised monthly archive' }"},{"id":"6:157","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":157,"end":192,"text":"    });\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  // health.json keeps full entries for recent days and packs older ones into short tuples\n  // (health.calendar_old); this returns one plain entry per day, oldest first.\n  var UNPACK = {\n    status: { p: 'pass', w: 'warn', f: 'fail', n: 'none' },\n    kind: { s: 'scheduled', m: 'manual', b: 'backfill', r: 'revision' },\n    src: { H: 'hourly snapshot', M: 'monthly archive', R: 'revised monthly archive' }\n  };\n  function expandCalendar(health) {\n    var out = [], old = health.calendar_old;\n    if (old && old.days && old.days.length) {\n      var t0 = parse(old.first);\n      old.days.forEach(function (t, i) {\n        var ds = new Date(t0 + i * 24 * HOUR).toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n        if (t[0] === 'n') { out.push({ date: ds, status: 'none' }); return; }\n        var d = { date: ds };\n        old.fields.forEach(function (f, k) { d[f] = t[k]; });\n        d.status = UNPACK.status[d.status];\n        d.kind = UNPACK.kind[d.kind];\n        d.kinds = d.kinds.split('').map(function (c) { return UNPACK.kind[c]; });\n        d.loaded = !!d.loaded;\n        d.src = d.src.split('').map(function (c) { return UNPACK.src[c] || c; }).sort().join(',');\n        if (!d.kept) delete d.kept;\n        out.push(d);\n      });\n    }\n    return out.concat(health.calendar || []);\n  }\n\n  function tally(calendar) {\n    var t = { pass: 0, warn: 0, fail: 0, none: 0, backfill: 0, scheduled: 0, total: 0 };\n    calendar.forEach(function (d) {\n      t[d.status] = (t[d.status] || 0) + 1;"},{"id":"6:183","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":183,"end":218,"text":"        out.push(d);\n      });\n    }\n    return out.concat(health.calendar || []);\n  }\n\n  function tally(calendar) {\n    var t = { pass: 0, warn: 0, fail: 0, none: 0, backfill: 0, scheduled: 0, total: 0 };\n    calendar.forEach(function (d) {\n      t[d.status] = (t[d.status] || 0) + 1;\n      if (d.status !== 'none') {\n        t.total++;\n        if (d.kind === 'backfill' || d.kind === 'revision') t.backfill++;\n        if (d.kind === 'scheduled') t.scheduled++;\n      }\n    });\n    return t;\n  }\n\n  // Lay days out as week columns (Monday first), like a wall calendar turned sideways.\n  function calendarGrid(calendar) {\n    if (!calendar.length) return { weeks: 0, cells: [], months: [] };\n    var first = new Date(parse(calendar[0].date));\n    var offset = (first.getUTCDay() + 6) % 7; // Monday = 0\n    var cells = [], months = [], lastMonth = -1;\n    calendar.forEach(function (d, i) {\n      var k = i + offset;\n      var col = Math.floor(k / 7), row = k % 7;\n      var m = new Date(parse(d.date)).getUTCMonth();\n      if (m !== lastMonth) { months.push({ col: col, label: MONTHS[m] }); lastMonth = m; }\n      cells.push({ day: d, col: col, row: row });\n    });\n    return { weeks: Math.floor((calendar.length - 1 + offset) / 7) + 1, cells: cells, months: months };\n  }\n\n  // The pipeline can only log days it ran. If it stops, the page itself adds the missing"},{"id":"6:209","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":209,"end":244,"text":"      var k = i + offset;\n      var col = Math.floor(k / 7), row = k % 7;\n      var m = new Date(parse(d.date)).getUTCMonth();\n      if (m !== lastMonth) { months.push({ col: col, label: MONTHS[m] }); lastMonth = m; }\n      cells.push({ day: d, col: col, row: row });\n    });\n    return { weeks: Math.floor((calendar.length - 1 + offset) / 7) + 1, cells: cells, months: months };\n  }\n\n  // The pipeline can only log days it ran. If it stops, the page itself adds the missing\n  // days, up to yesterday by the visitor's clock, as \"no run\", so a silent gap still shows.\n  function extendCalendar(calendar, now) {\n    var out = calendar.slice();\n    if (!out.length) return out;\n    var day = 24 * HOUR;\n    var last = parse(out[out.length - 1].date);\n    var yesterday = Math.floor(now / day) * day - day;\n    for (var t = last + day, k = 0; t <= yesterday && k < 400; t += day, k++) {\n      out.push({ date: new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 10), status: 'none', added: true });\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  // ---- the answer --------------------------------------------------------\n\n  function cityView(summary, id) {\n    var c = null;\n    summary.cities.forEach(function (x) { if (x.id === id) c = x; });\n    if (!c) return null;\n    var s = summary.series[id];\n    var sum = 0;\n    s.hi.forEach(function (h) { if (h) sum += h; });\n    var coverage = c.hours_possible ? c.hours_with_reading / c.hours_possible : 0;\n    return {\n      city: c, total: c.high_hours, seriesTotal: sum, coverage: coverage,\n      share: c.hours_with_reading ? c.high_hours / c.hours_with_reading : 0,"},{"id":"6:235","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":235,"end":264,"text":"    var c = null;\n    summary.cities.forEach(function (x) { if (x.id === id) c = x; });\n    if (!c) return null;\n    var s = summary.series[id];\n    var sum = 0;\n    s.hi.forEach(function (h) { if (h) sum += h; });\n    var coverage = c.hours_possible ? c.hours_with_reading / c.hours_possible : 0;\n    return {\n      city: c, total: c.high_hours, seriesTotal: sum, coverage: coverage,\n      share: c.hours_with_reading ? c.high_hours / c.hours_with_reading : 0,\n      gappy: coverage < 0.9\n    };\n  }\n\n  function ranked(summary) {\n    return summary.cities.slice().sort(function (a, b) {\n      return b.high_hours - a.high_hours || summary.cities.indexOf(a) - summary.cities.indexOf(b);\n    });\n  }\n\n  var api = {\n    parse: parse, plural: plural, fmtInt: fmtInt, ageText: ageText, dayLabel: dayLabel, longDay: longDay,\n    stamp: stamp, bytesText: bytesText, freshness: freshness, STATUS: STATUS, KIND: KIND,\n    dayChecks: dayChecks, describeDay: describeDay, loadedText: loadedText, warnCauses: warnCauses, expandCalendar: expandCalendar,\n    extendCalendar: extendCalendar, tally: tally, calendarGrid: calendarGrid,\n    cityView: cityView, ranked: ranked, MONTHS: MONTHS\n  };\n  if (typeof module !== 'undefined' && module.exports) module.exports = api;\n  else root.AlmanacModel = api;\n})(this);"},{"id":"6:261","path":"projects/almanac/model.js","start":261,"end":264,"text":"  };\n  if (typeof module !== 'undefined' && module.exports) module.exports = api;\n  else root.AlmanacModel = api;\n})(this);"},{"id":"7:1","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":1,"end":36,"text":"\"\"\"Each contract check passes clean data and catches a crafted violation.\n\n    python -I -m unittest discover -s projects/almanac/tests -p \"test_*.py\"\n\"\"\"\nimport copy\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport unittest\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\nimport fixtures as F  # noqa: E402\nfrom fixtures import C, CONTRACT, DAY  # noqa: E402\n\nNOW = datetime(2026, 8, 16, 7, 17, tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef run(src, live=True, now=NOW):\n    checks, rows, q = C.validate(CONTRACT, DAY, src, now=now, live=live)\n    return {c[\"name\"]: c for c in checks}, rows, q\n\n\nclass CleanData(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_clean_day_passes_every_check(self):\n        res, rows, q = run(F.sources())\n        for name in (\"schema\", \"types\", \"range\", \"uniqueness\", \"completeness\", \"volume\", \"freshness\"):\n            self.assertEqual(res[name][\"status\"], \"pass\", (name, res[name][\"detail\"]))\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)\n        self.assertEqual(q, [])\n\n    def test_high_risk_rounding(self):\n        _, rows, _ = run(F.sources())\n        hi = [r for r in rows if r[\"high_risk\"]]\n        self.assertEqual(len(hi), 4)\n        self.assertTrue(all(r[\"city\"] == \"Kamloops\" for r in hi))\n        self.assertEqual(C.reported(6.49), 6)"},{"id":"7:27","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":27,"end":62,"text":"            self.assertEqual(res[name][\"status\"], \"pass\", (name, res[name][\"detail\"]))\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)\n        self.assertEqual(q, [])\n\n    def test_high_risk_rounding(self):\n        _, rows, _ = run(F.sources())\n        hi = [r for r in rows if r[\"high_risk\"]]\n        self.assertEqual(len(hi), 4)\n        self.assertTrue(all(r[\"city\"] == \"Kamloops\" for r in hi))\n        self.assertEqual(C.reported(6.49), 6)\n        self.assertEqual(C.reported(6.5), 7)\n        self.assertEqual(C.reported(11.0), 11)\n\n    def test_every_check_is_reported_once(self):\n        res, _, _ = run(F.sources())\n        self.assertEqual(sorted(res), sorted(c[\"name\"] for c in CONTRACT[\"checks\"]))\n\n\nclass Schema(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_missing_city_column_fails_and_loads_nothing(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        i = src[\"pnr\"][\"header\"].index(\"IAKID\")\n        src[\"pnr\"][\"header\"][i] = \"IAKIX\"\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertIn(\"IAKID\", res[\"schema\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n\n    def test_extra_columns_are_fine(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pyr\"][\"header\"].append(\"ZZNEW\")\n        for r in src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"]:\n            r.append(\"2.00\")\n        res, _, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")"},{"id":"7:53","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":53,"end":88,"text":"        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n\n    def test_extra_columns_are_fine(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pyr\"][\"header\"].append(\"ZZNEW\")\n        for r in src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"]:\n            r.append(\"2.00\")\n        res, _, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")\n\n\nclass Types(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_text_in_a_reading_fails(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBRIK\", 5, \"n/a\")\n        res, rows, q = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n        self.assertEqual(q[0][\"reason\"], \"not a number\")\n\n    def test_bad_hour_fails(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"][0][1] = \"25\"\n        res, _, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n\n    def test_blank_reading_is_allowed(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBRIK\", 5, \"\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 1)\n\n\nclass Range(unittest.TestCase):"},{"id":"7:79","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":79,"end":114,"text":"\n    def test_blank_reading_is_allowed(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBRIK\", 5, \"\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"types\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 1)\n\n\nclass Range(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_one_odd_value_is_set_aside_with_a_warning(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JBOBQ\", 3, \"-9.00\")\n        res, rows, q = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 1)\n        self.assertEqual(len(q), 1)\n        self.assertEqual(q[0][\"city\"], \"Victoria\")\n\n    def test_many_odd_values_fail(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        for h in range(4):\n            F.set_cell(src, \"pnr\", \"IACMP\", h, \"120.00\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n\n    def test_ten_plus_written_as_eleven_is_in_range(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        F.set_cell(src, \"pnr\", \"IAKID\", 2, \"11.00\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")\n        r = [r for r in rows if r[\"location_id\"] == \"IAKID\" and r[\"hour_utc\"] == 2][0]\n        self.assertEqual(r[\"aqhi_reported\"], \"10+\")\n        self.assertEqual(r[\"high_risk\"], 1)\n"},{"id":"7:105","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":105,"end":140,"text":"\n    def test_ten_plus_written_as_eleven_is_in_range(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        F.set_cell(src, \"pnr\", \"IAKID\", 2, \"11.00\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"range\"][\"status\"], \"pass\")\n        r = [r for r in rows if r[\"location_id\"] == \"IAKID\" and r[\"hour_utc\"] == 2][0]\n        self.assertEqual(r[\"aqhi_reported\"], \"10+\")\n        self.assertEqual(r[\"high_risk\"], 1)\n\n\nclass Uniqueness(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_conflicting_duplicate_fails(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        dup = copy.deepcopy(src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"][0])\n        dup[src[\"pyr\"][\"header\"].index(\"JBRIK\")] = \"4.00\"\n        src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"].append(dup)\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"uniqueness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n\n    def test_exact_duplicate_warns_and_keeps_one(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"].append(list(src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"][3]))\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"uniqueness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n        keys = [(r[\"hour_utc\"], r[\"location_id\"]) for r in rows]\n        self.assertEqual(len(keys), len(set(keys)))\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)\n\n\nclass Completeness(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_missing_hours_warn(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"] = [r for r in src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"] if int(r[1]) not in (0, 1)]\n        res, _, _ = run(src)"},{"id":"7:131","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":131,"end":166,"text":"        keys = [(r[\"hour_utc\"], r[\"location_id\"]) for r in rows]\n        self.assertEqual(len(keys), len(set(keys)))\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)\n\n\nclass Completeness(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_missing_hours_warn(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"] = [r for r in src[\"pyr\"][\"rows\"] if int(r[1]) not in (0, 1)]\n        res, _, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n        self.assertIn(\"22 of 24\", res[\"completeness\"][\"detail\"])\n\n    def test_missing_day_fails(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pnr\"][\"rows\"] = []\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n\n\nclass Volume(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_quiet_city_warns(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        for h in range(10):\n            F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", \"JAFUV\", h, \"\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n        self.assertIn(\"Kelowna had readings for 14 of 24 hours\", res[\"volume\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 10)\n\n    def test_mostly_empty_day_fails(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        for station in (\"JAFUV\", \"JAFNW\", \"JBLVS\", \"JBOBQ\"):\n            for h in range(24):\n                F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", station, h, \"\")"},{"id":"7:157","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":157,"end":192,"text":"        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n        self.assertIn(\"Kelowna had readings for 14 of 24 hours\", res[\"volume\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7 - 10)\n\n    def test_mostly_empty_day_fails(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        for station in (\"JAFUV\", \"JAFNW\", \"JBLVS\", \"JBOBQ\"):\n            for h in range(24):\n                F.set_cell(src, \"pyr\", station, h, \"\")\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"volume\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n\n\nclass Freshness(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_stale_feed_warns(self):\n        res, _, _ = run(F.sources(newest=\"2026-08-15T20:00:00Z\"))\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n\n    def test_archive_skips(self):\n        res, rows, _ = run(F.sources(), live=False)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n        self.assertEqual(len(rows), 24 * 7)\n\n    def test_unknown_age_fails(self):\n        res, _, _ = run(F.sources(newest=None))\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n\n    def test_no_live_file_is_a_stalled_feed_not_a_schema_break(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pyr\"] = {\"absent\": \"live\", \"lookback_hours\": 8}\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertIn(\"PYR\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertIn(\"8 hours\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])"},{"id":"7:183","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":183,"end":210,"text":"        res, _, _ = run(F.sources(newest=None))\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n\n    def test_no_live_file_is_a_stalled_feed_not_a_schema_break(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pyr\"] = {\"absent\": \"live\", \"lookback_hours\": 8}\n        res, rows, _ = run(src)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertIn(\"PYR\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertIn(\"8 hours\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n\n\nclass NoFile(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_no_archive_file_fails_completeness(self):\n        src = F.sources()\n        src[\"pnr\"] = None\n        res, rows, _ = run(src, live=False)\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertIn(\"PNR\", res[\"completeness\"][\"detail\"])\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows, [])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()"},{"id":"7:209","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_contract.py","start":209,"end":210,"text":"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()"},{"id":"8:1","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":1,"end":36,"text":"\"\"\"End-to-end pipeline tests on crafted files read from disk (no network):\nidempotency, backfill, failed days keep earlier data, and the run log.\"\"\"\nimport filecmp\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\nimport fixtures as F  # noqa: E402\nimport run as R  # noqa: E402  (pipeline/run.py, on the path via fixtures)\n\nDAYS = [\"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-15\", \"2026-08-16\"]\n\n\ndef write_sources(folder, days=DAYS, broken=None):\n    os.makedirs(folder, exist_ok=True)\n    for region in (\"pyr\", \"pnr\"):\n        text = F.csv_file(region, days)\n        if broken and broken[0] == region:\n            text = broken[1](text)\n        name = \"202608_MONTHLY_AQHI_%s_SiteObs.csv\" % region.upper()\n        with open(os.path.join(folder, name), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n            f.write(text)\n\n\ndef tree(folder, skip=(\"runs.ndjson\", \"health.json\")):\n    out = {}\n    for dirpath, _, files in os.walk(folder):\n        for n in files:\n            if n in skip:\n                continue\n            p = os.path.join(dirpath, n)\n            with open(p, \"rb\") as f:"},{"id":"8:27","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":27,"end":62,"text":"\n\ndef tree(folder, skip=(\"runs.ndjson\", \"health.json\")):\n    out = {}\n    for dirpath, _, files in os.walk(folder):\n        for n in files:\n            if n in skip:\n                continue\n            p = os.path.join(dirpath, n)\n            with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n                out[os.path.relpath(p, folder)] = f.read()\n    return out\n\n\nclass Pipeline(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"almanac-test-\")\n        self.src = os.path.join(self.tmp, \"src\")\n        self.data = os.path.join(self.tmp, \"data\")\n        write_sources(self.src)\n\n    def tearDown(self):\n        shutil.rmtree(self.tmp, ignore_errors=True)\n\n    def cli(self, *args):\n        return R.main(list(args) + [\"--source-dir\", self.src, \"--data-dir\", self.data,\n                                    \"--now\", \"2026-11-02T07:17:00Z\", \"--pause\", \"0\"])\n\n    def runs(self):\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"runs.ndjson\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            return [json.loads(l) for l in f]\n\n    def test_rerunning_a_day_gives_identical_output(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\"), 0)\n        first = tree(self.data)\n        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\"), 0)"},{"id":"8:53","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":53,"end":88,"text":"                                    \"--now\", \"2026-11-02T07:17:00Z\", \"--pause\", \"0\"])\n\n    def runs(self):\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"runs.ndjson\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            return [json.loads(l) for l in f]\n\n    def test_rerunning_a_day_gives_identical_output(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\"), 0)\n        first = tree(self.data)\n        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\"), 0)\n        second = tree(self.data)\n        self.assertEqual(sorted(first), sorted(second))\n        for k in first:\n            self.assertEqual(first[k], second[k], k)\n        self.assertIn(os.path.join(\"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), first)\n        # the log grows: every run is recorded, including reruns\n        self.assertEqual(len(self.runs()), 7)\n\n    def test_backfill_labels_and_partitions(self):\n        self.cli(\"--backfill\", \"2026-08-14\", \"2026-08-16\")\n        runs = self.runs()\n        self.assertEqual([r[\"kind\"] for r in runs], [\"backfill\"] * 3)\n        self.assertEqual(len({r[\"batch_id\"] for r in runs}), 1)\n        for d in DAYS:\n            self.assertTrue(os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.data, \"validated\", \"2026-08\", d + \".csv\")))\n            self.assertTrue(os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.data, \"raw\", \"2026-08\", d + \".pyr.csv\")))\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            s = json.load(f)\n        kam = [c for c in s[\"cities\"] if c[\"city\"] == \"Kamloops\"][0]\n        self.assertEqual(kam[\"high_hours\"], 12)  # 4 smoky hours a day x 3 days\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"health.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            h = json.load(f)\n        self.assertEqual([c[\"kind\"] for c in h[\"calendar\"]], [\"backfill\"] * 3)\n        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][0][\"checks\"], \"pppppps\")\n"},{"id":"8:79","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":79,"end":114,"text":"            self.assertTrue(os.path.exists(os.path.join(self.data, \"raw\", \"2026-08\", d + \".pyr.csv\")))\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            s = json.load(f)\n        kam = [c for c in s[\"cities\"] if c[\"city\"] == \"Kamloops\"][0]\n        self.assertEqual(kam[\"high_hours\"], 12)  # 4 smoky hours a day x 3 days\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"health.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            h = json.load(f)\n        self.assertEqual([c[\"kind\"] for c in h[\"calendar\"]], [\"backfill\"] * 3)\n        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][0][\"checks\"], \"pppppps\")\n\n    def test_failed_day_is_logged_and_keeps_earlier_data(self):\n        self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")\n        before = tree(os.path.join(self.data, \"validated\"))\n        # the source renames a city column: the contract must refuse the day\n        write_sources(self.src, broken=(\"pnr\", lambda t: t.replace(\"IAKID\", \"IAKIX\")))\n        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 2)\n        last = self.runs()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(last[\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertFalse(last[\"loaded\"])\n        self.assertEqual(tree(os.path.join(self.data, \"validated\")), before)\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"health.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            h = json.load(f)\n        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"runs\"], 2)\n        # the refused rerun says the earlier load is still counted, and how much of it\n        self.assertTrue(last[\"kept_earlier\"])\n        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"kept\"], 24 * 7)\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            s = json.load(f)\n        self.assertEqual(sum(c[\"high_hours\"] for c in s[\"cities\"]), 4)\n\n    def test_missing_archive_is_a_red_run_not_a_crash(self):\n        shutil.rmtree(self.src)\n        os.makedirs(self.src)\n        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")"},{"id":"8:105","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":105,"end":140,"text":"        self.assertTrue(last[\"kept_earlier\"])\n        self.assertEqual(h[\"calendar\"][-1][\"kept\"], 24 * 7)\n        with open(os.path.join(self.data, \"aggregates\", \"summary.json\"), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            s = json.load(f)\n        self.assertEqual(sum(c[\"high_hours\"] for c in s[\"cities\"]), 4)\n\n    def test_missing_archive_is_a_red_run_not_a_crash(self):\n        shutil.rmtree(self.src)\n        os.makedirs(self.src)\n        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-08-15\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 2)\n        last = self.runs()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(last[\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertTrue(any(\"No PYR file\" in n for n in last[\"notes\"]))\n        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}\n        # no file is a missing day, not a renamed column\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"completeness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"schema\"][\"status\"], \"skip\")\n        self.assertEqual([c[\"name\"] for c in last[\"checks\"]], [c[\"name\"] for c in F.CONTRACT[\"checks\"]])\n\n    def test_stalled_live_feed_fails_freshness_not_schema(self):\n        # What the daily run sees when ECCC's hourly feed has stopped: no live file at all.\n        shutil.rmtree(self.src)\n        os.makedirs(self.src)\n        code = self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-11-01\")\n        self.assertEqual(code, 2)\n        last = self.runs()[-1]\n        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertIn(\"stalled\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])\n        for name in (\"schema\", \"types\", \"range\", \"uniqueness\", \"completeness\", \"volume\"):\n            self.assertEqual(res[name][\"status\"], \"skip\", name)\n        self.assertTrue(any(\"stalled\" in n for n in last[\"notes\"]))\n\n    def test_live_feed_six_to_eight_hours_old_warns(self):\n        # an hourly file from 7 hours ago is found (within the lookback), but its newest hour is old"},{"id":"8:131","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":131,"end":158,"text":"        last = self.runs()[-1]\n        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"fail\")\n        self.assertIn(\"stalled\", res[\"freshness\"][\"detail\"])\n        for name in (\"schema\", \"types\", \"range\", \"uniqueness\", \"completeness\", \"volume\"):\n            self.assertEqual(res[name][\"status\"], \"skip\", name)\n        self.assertTrue(any(\"stalled\" in n for n in last[\"notes\"]))\n\n    def test_live_feed_six_to_eight_hours_old_warns(self):\n        # an hourly file from 7 hours ago is found (within the lookback), but its newest hour is old\n        for region in (\"pyr\", \"pnr\"):\n            text = F.csv_file(region, [\"2026-11-01\"])\n            name = \"2026110200_AQHI_%s_SiteObs.csv\" % region.upper()\n            with open(os.path.join(self.src, name), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n                f.write(text)\n        self.assertEqual(self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-11-01\"), 0)\n        last = self.runs()[-1]\n        res = {c[\"name\"]: c for c in last[\"checks\"]}\n        self.assertEqual(res[\"freshness\"][\"status\"], \"warn\")\n        self.assertEqual(last[\"source\"][0][\"type\"], \"hourly snapshot\")\n\n    def test_refuses_a_day_that_is_not_over(self):\n        with self.assertRaises(SystemExit):\n            self.cli(\"--date\", \"2026-11-02\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()"},{"id":"8:157","path":"projects/almanac/tests/test_pipeline.py","start":157,"end":158,"text":"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()"},{"id":"9:1","path":"projects/almanac/tests/freshness.test.js","start":1,"end":36,"text":"// The page must say \"stale\" honestly. The clock is injected, so no waiting is needed.\nvar assert = require('assert');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar M = require('../model.js');\n\nvar slo = { max_data_age_hours: 36, max_run_age_hours: 26 };\nvar H = 3600 * 1000;\nvar latestHour = '2026-11-01T23:00:00Z';\nvar lastRun = '2026-11-02T07:20:00Z';\nvar t0 = Date.parse(latestHour);\n\n// A normal morning after the daily run: fresh.\nvar f = M.freshness(t0 + 9 * H, latestHour, lastRun, slo);\nassert.strictEqual(f.state, 'fresh');\nassert.strictEqual(f.word, 'Fresh');\nassert.deepStrictEqual(f.reasons, []);\n\n// Exactly at the limit is still fresh; one minute past is stale.\nassert.strictEqual(M.freshness(t0 + 36 * H, latestHour, '2026-11-02T20:00:00Z', slo).state, 'fresh');\nvar late = M.freshness(t0 + 36 * H + 60000, latestHour, '2026-11-02T20:00:00Z', slo);\nassert.strictEqual(late.state, 'stale');\nassert.ok(/newest hour/.test(late.reasons[0]));\n\n// The latest run is older than its SLO, even though the data is recent enough: stale.\nvar noRun = M.freshness(Date.parse('2026-11-03T10:00:00Z'), '2026-11-02T23:00:00Z', '2026-11-02T07:20:00Z', slo);\nassert.strictEqual(noRun.state, 'stale');\nassert.strictEqual(noRun.reasons.length, 1);\nassert.ok(/last run was/.test(noRun.reasons[0]), noRun.reasons[0]);\n\n// Both broken: both reasons are given.\nvar both = M.freshness(t0 + 5 * 24 * H, latestHour, lastRun, slo);\nassert.strictEqual(both.state, 'stale');\nassert.strictEqual(both.reasons.length, 2);\n\n// No data at all is stale, never fresh by default."},{"id":"9:27","path":"projects/almanac/tests/freshness.test.js","start":27,"end":56,"text":"assert.strictEqual(noRun.state, 'stale');\nassert.strictEqual(noRun.reasons.length, 1);\nassert.ok(/last run was/.test(noRun.reasons[0]), noRun.reasons[0]);\n\n// Both broken: both reasons are given.\nvar both = M.freshness(t0 + 5 * 24 * H, latestHour, lastRun, slo);\nassert.strictEqual(both.state, 'stale');\nassert.strictEqual(both.reasons.length, 2);\n\n// No data at all is stale, never fresh by default.\nassert.strictEqual(M.freshness(t0, null, null, slo).state, 'stale');\n\n// Against the real aggregates: what a visitor sees soon after the last run, and a month later.\nvar health = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, '..', 'data', 'aggregates', 'health.json'), 'utf8'));\nhealth.calendar = M.expandCalendar(health);\nvar finished = health.latest_run.finished_at;\nvar soon = M.freshness(Date.parse(finished) + H, health.latest_hour, finished, health.contract.slo);\nvar month = M.freshness(Date.parse(finished) + 30 * 24 * H, health.latest_hour, finished, health.contract.slo);\nassert.strictEqual(month.state, 'stale');\nassert.strictEqual(health.contract.slo.max_data_age_hours, 36);\n// Days with no run are not invisible: the page adds them up to yesterday by its own clock.\nvar lastDay = Date.parse(health.calendar[health.calendar.length - 1].date + 'T00:00:00Z');\nvar D = 24 * H;\nvar ext = M.extendCalendar(health.calendar, lastDay + 4 * D + 12 * H); // three whole days later, no runs\nvar added = ext.slice(health.calendar.length);\nassert.deepStrictEqual(added.map(function (d) { return d.date; }),\n  [1, 2, 3].map(function (k) { return new Date(lastDay + k * D).toISOString().slice(0, 10); }));\nassert.ok(added.every(function (d) { return d.status === 'none'; }));\nassert.strictEqual(M.extendCalendar(health.calendar, lastDay + D + 8 * H).length, health.calendar.length);\nconsole.log('freshness: ok (an hour after the last run the page says ' + soon.word + '; a month later it says ' + month.word + ')');"},{"id":"9:53","path":"projects/almanac/tests/freshness.test.js","start":53,"end":56,"text":"  [1, 2, 3].map(function (k) { return new Date(lastDay + k * D).toISOString().slice(0, 10); }));\nassert.ok(added.every(function (d) { return d.status === 'none'; }));\nassert.strictEqual(M.extendCalendar(health.calendar, lastDay + D + 8 * H).length, health.calendar.length);\nconsole.log('freshness: ok (an hour after the last run the page says ' + soon.word + '; a month later it says ' + month.word + ')');"}]};
